window.SECTOR_NARR={"ech":{"legs":{"2011-08-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:trough:2011-08"},"2011-08-31":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2011-08"},"2011-10-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:trough:2011-10"},"2012-04-02":{"body":"From April 2012 through early 2014 ECH fell roughly 41% in USD terms as copper rolled over from its post-2008 supercycle peak. China's fixed-asset investment growth decelerated, pulling copper demand and Chilean miners' earnings lower. The peso weakened alongside the metal, compounding the dollar-return loss for foreign holders. The domestic economy held up reasonably well, but the commodity-driven equity market could not escape the global metals downturn.","body_zh":"从2012年4月至2014年初，随着铜价从2008年后超级周期高点回落，ECH美元跌幅约41%。中国固定资产投资增速放缓，拖累铜需求并打压智利矿企盈利。比索随铜价同步走弱，进一步放大了美元计价的损失。国内经济相对稳定，但以大宗商品为主导的股市无法摆脱全球金属下行周期的冲击。","drivers":["China capex slowdown","Copper price peak-to-trough","CLP weakness vs USD","EM risk-off flows"],"prev_key":"2012-04","prev_key_chain":["2012-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Copper supercycle ends, peso fades (-41%)","title_zh":"铜超级周期终结，比索走软（-41%）","turn_id":"ech:peak:2012-04"},"2014-02-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:trough:2014-02"},"2014-05-13":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2014-05"},"2015-01-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:trough:2015-01"},"2015-05-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2015-05"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"ECH surged roughly 97% between early 2016 and February 2018, one of its strongest upcycles. Copper bottomed in early 2016 alongside broader EM commodities, then rallied as China re-accelerated infrastructure spending and synchronized global growth lifted metals demand. The peso recovered against the dollar, adding an FX tailwind on top of local equity gains. Sebastian Pinera won the late-2017 presidential election on a business-friendly platform, adding a domestic sentiment kicker as the leg matured.","body_zh":"ECH从2016年初至2018年2月累计上涨约97%，是其最强的上行周期之一。铜价在2016年初随大宗商品触底后反弹，中国重启基建投资、全球经济同步扩张共同推升金属需求。比索对美元回升，在本地股市涨幅之上叠加汇率顺风。2017年底，皮涅拉凭借亲商纲领赢得总统大选，为这轮牛市尾声增添了国内情绪助推。","drivers":["Copper recovery from multi-year lows","China infrastructure re-acceleration","CLP appreciation vs USD","Pinera election boosts business confidence"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Copper rebound powers +97% bull run","title_zh":"铜价反弹推动+97%牛市","turn_id":"ech:trough:2016-01"},"2018-02-01":{"body":"ECH fell roughly 67% between February 2018 and March 2020, one of its deepest drawdowns, driven by a convergence of shocks. Copper slid amid the US-China trade war and slowing Chinese growth. In October 2019 mass protests erupted across Chile over inequality and living costs, and the peso hit record lows as capital fled. The 2020 COVID-19 shock delivered the final blow, collapsing copper demand and global risk appetite at once while the dollar surged against EM currencies.","body_zh":"ECH从2018年2月至2020年3月累计下跌约67%，是其历史上最深的回撤之一，由多重冲击共振造成。铜价在美中贸易战与中国经济放缓中下滑。2019年10月，智利爆发针对不平等与生活成本的大规模抗议，比索跌至历史低点，资本外流。2020年新冠冲击作为最后一击，同时压垮铜需求与全球风险偏好，美元兑新兴市场货币全面走强。","drivers":["US-China trade war hits copper","October 2019 social uprising & CLP record low","COVID-19 demand collapse","Global EM risk-off & USD surge"],"prev_key":"2018-02","prev_key_chain":["2018-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade war, unrest & COVID erase gains (-67%)","title_zh":"贸易战、动荡与新冠抹去涨幅（-67%）","turn_id":"ech:peak:2018-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"ECH rebounded roughly 61% from the March 2020 COVID lows through July 2020 as the global stimulus wave lifted copper and risk appetite recovered. China's early reopening and infrastructure push drove copper back toward pre-COVID levels faster than most commodities, and the peso stabilized as commodity revenues recovered. The first leg of the recovery paused mid-2020 as Chile entered its constitutional rewrite process.","body_zh":"从2020年3月新冠低点至2020年7月，ECH反弹约61%，全球刺激浪潮推升铜价，风险偏好修复。中国率先重启并加大基建投入，铜价回升速度快于多数大宗商品，比索随大宗商品收入回升而企稳。2020年中期，智利进入制宪进程，此轮反弹的第一段随之暂歇。","drivers":["Global fiscal/monetary stimulus","China reopening & infrastructure spending","Copper recovery toward pre-COVID levels","CLP stabilization on commodity inflows"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Copper stimulus bounce, +61% snap-back","title_zh":"铜价刺激反弹，+61%急速修复","turn_id":"ech:trough:2020-03"},"2020-06-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2020-06"},"2020-09-23":{"body":"A second up-leg ran from September 2020 through April 2021, adding about 56%. Copper surged to multi-year highs by early 2021 on green-energy demand expectations and tightening supply, while the global reflation trade boosted EM commodity exporters. Chile's October 2020 plebiscite approved drafting a new constitution with overwhelming support, temporarily lifting the political overhang and improving sentiment toward Chilean assets.","body_zh":"第二段上行从2020年9月延续至2021年4月，累计上涨约56%。受绿色能源需求预期与供应收紧推动，铜价在2021年初升至多年高位，全球再通胀交易提振新兴市场大宗商品出口国。2020年10月，智利制宪公投以压倒性支持率通过，短暂缓解政治压力，提振市场对智利资产的情绪。","drivers":["Copper surge on green-energy demand","Global reflation trade","October 2020 constitution plebiscite eases uncertainty","EM commodity exporter outperformance"],"prev_key":"2020-09","prev_key_chain":["2020-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Constitution plebiscite + copper boom, +56%","title_zh":"制宪公投+铜价繁荣，+56%","turn_id":"ech:trough:2020-09"},"2021-04-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2021-04"},"2021-10-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:trough:2021-10"},"2021-11-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2021-11"},"2021-12-20":{"body":"A partial recovery of roughly 44% ran from December 2021 through June 2022. Copper held elevated levels as supply disruptions and energy-transition demand kept the metal well bid even while broader EM sentiment stayed cautious. This leg unfolded ahead of Chile's September 2022 constitutional referendum, where voters rejected the left-leaning draft by a wide margin — an outcome markets read as reducing the risk of radical mining and property reform.","body_zh":"从2021年12月至2022年6月，ECH出现约44%的阶段性反弹。铜价因供应中断与能源转型需求保持高位，即便更广泛的新兴市场情绪偏谨慎。这一段发生在2022年9月制宪公投之前——选民以悬殊比例否决偏左草案，市场将其解读为激进矿业与产权改革风险下降。","drivers":["Copper supply disruptions keep prices elevated","Energy-transition demand underpins metals","Sept 2022 left-leaning draft rejected, reducing policy risk","Partial CLP stabilization"],"prev_key":"2021-12","prev_key_chain":["2021-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Copper-led counter-rally, +44%","title_zh":"铜价主导的阶段性反弹，+44%","turn_id":"ech:trough:2021-12"},"2022-06-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2022-06"},"2022-07-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:trough:2022-07"},"2022-09-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2022-09"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"ECH rallied about 47% from October 2022 through July 2023 as political risk receded further. The constitutional rewrite continued, but the May 2023 Constitutional Council elections shifted the drafting balance away from left-wing mining and property reforms. Copper recovered from its 2022 lows as China's post-COVID reopening lifted demand expectations, and a somewhat firmer peso added to dollar returns.","body_zh":"2022年10月至2023年7月，ECH累计上涨约47%，政治风险进一步消退。制宪进程继续，但2023年5月制宪委员会选举使草案走向偏离左翼矿业与产权改革方向。随着中国解封重启，市场对铜需求预期改善，铜价从2022年低点回升，比索略有走强，进一步提升美元回报。","drivers":["May 2023 Constitutional Council shifts away from left reforms","China reopening lifts copper demand","Left-wing mining reform risk fades","CLP partial recovery"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Relief rally as left-policy risk fades, +47%","title_zh":"左翼政策风险消退带来宽慰行情，+47%","turn_id":"ech:trough:2022-10"},"2023-07-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2023-07"},"2023-10-23":{"body":"ECH's strongest sustained leg in the window ran from October 2023 to January 2026, gaining roughly 111%. The December 2023 referendum rejected the conservative draft by 56-44, ending the multi-year constitutional saga and letting investors refocus on fundamentals. Copper traded up toward record highs through 2024-2025 on energy-transition and AI-driven power-infrastructure demand, pulling Chilean miners higher. Jose Antonio Kast's December 2025 presidential win on a pro-market, fiscal-discipline platform supported a further re-rating of Chilean assets, with the peso firming on improved macro confidence.","body_zh":"2023年10月至2026年1月是ECH在该窗口中最强劲的持续上行，累计涨幅约111%。2023年12月公投以56比44否决保守派草案，多年制宪进程就此落幕，投资者得以重新聚焦基本面。受能源转型与AI电力基础设施需求推动，铜价在2024-2025年间走高并逼近历史高位，带动智利矿企走强。2025年12月，卡斯特以亲市场、财政纪律纲领赢得总统大选，支撑智利资产进一步重估，比索随宏观信心改善而走强。","drivers":["Dec 2023 referendum ends constitutional uncertainty","Copper near record highs on energy transition & AI power demand","Kast Dec-2025 win supports market-friendly re-rating","CLP firms on improved macro confidence"],"prev_key":"2023-10","prev_key_chain":["2023-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Copper & political-clarity bull run: +111% to Jan 2026","title_zh":"铜价+政治清晰化牛市：+111%至2026年1月","turn_id":"ech:trough:2023-10"},"2024-05-20":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:peak:2024-05"},"2024-08-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ech:trough:2024-08"},"2026-01-27":{"body":"After the January 2026 peak, ECH fell roughly 20% into a March 2026 trough. The size and pace of the prior 111% run left the ETF technically stretched, and the pullback was consistent with a cooling in copper and a broader EM risk-off rotation that also pressured the Chilean peso, amplifying the drawdown in USD terms. Specific late-cycle catalysts are uncertain, but the move reads as a commodity-and-FX-driven mean reversion after an exceptional advance.","body_zh":"2026年1月见顶后，ECH回落约20%至2026年3月低点。前期111%的涨幅过大且过快，令ETF在技术上明显偏高；此次回调与铜价降温及更广泛的新兴市场风险规避相一致，后者同时压制比索，放大了美元计价的跌幅。后周期的具体催化因素尚不确定，但此次走势更像是大幅上行后由大宗商品与汇率驱动的均值回归。","drivers":["Technical exhaustion after the +111% run","Copper cooling from highs","EM risk-off rotation","CLP softening amplifies USD drawdown"],"prev_key":"2026-01","prev_key_chain":["2026-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Sharp reversal off the peak, -20%","title_zh":"见顶后急速反转，-20%","turn_id":"ech:peak:2026-01"},"2026-03-20":{"body":"From the March 2026 trough ECH bounced about 18% into April, but the rebound stalled at a lower high than the January peak and the ETF has since slid back toward the cycle floor (position 6.9). With this leg falling beyond the range of reliable knowledge, it is best read quantitatively: a partial, low-conviction recovery within an ongoing corrective phase rather than a confirmed new uptrend. Direction will likely hinge on copper and the peso stabilizing.","body_zh":"自2026年3月低点，ECH反弹约18%至4月，但此次反弹止步于低于1月高点的位置，此后ETF再度滑向周期底部（位置6.9）。鉴于该段超出可靠认知范围，宜从量化角度解读：这是持续调整阶段内一次部分、低信心的修复，而非已确认的新上升趋势。后续方向很可能取决于铜价与比索能否企稳。","drivers":["Partial rebound off the March trough","Stalled at a lower high vs January peak","Still in a corrective phase (cycle position 6.9)","Outcome hinges on copper & CLP stabilizing"],"prev_key":"2026-03","prev_key_chain":["2026-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Modest bounce to a lower high, +18%","title_zh":"温和反弹至更低高点，+18%","turn_id":"ech:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"ECH sits in a Trough phase with a cycle position of just 6.9 out of 100, near the washout floor. Over the prior quarter it lagged SPY by about 11 percentage points (RS rank 19th of 24 markets, sixth from the bottom) and its trailing-window return is roughly -22%. The big 2.3-year bull run (+111% from Oct 2023 to its Jan 2026 peak) has rolled over: ECH dropped about 20% into a March 2026 trough, staged a modest bounce to a lower high in April, and has since slid back toward the floor. The structural backdrop stays constructive longer term — Jose Antonio Kast won the December 2025 presidential election on a pro-market, fiscal-discipline platform (inaugurated March 2026), and Chile's central role in copper and lithium supply chains anchors the fundamental case — but the cycle read is firmly washed-out for now.","now_zh":"ECH 目前处于周期低谷阶段，周期位置仅为6.9/100，接近洗盘底部。过去一个季度相对标普500跑输约11个百分点（相对强弱排名第19/24，倒数第六），滚动窗口回报约为-22%。此前约2.3年的牛市（2023年10月至2026年1月高点累计上涨约111%）已经反转：ECH一度回落约20%至2026年3月低点，随后小幅反弹至4月的更低高点，此后再度滑向底部。中长期结构性背景仍偏积极——卡斯特以亲市场、财政纪律纲领赢得2025年12月总统大选（2026年3月就职），智利在铜与锂供应链中的核心地位为基本面提供支撑——但当前的周期读数明显处于超卖洗盘状态。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"eido":{"legs":{"2011-08-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:peak:2011-08"},"2011-09-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:trough:2011-09"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:peak:2011-10"},"2012-06-04":{"body":"From mid-2012 Indonesia rode the global EM recovery: the Fed's QE3 (launched September 2012) kept the dollar soft, foreign capital flowed into high-yielding EM assets, and Indonesia's commodity exports were still holding up. The rupiah traded near 9,500-10,000/USD, relatively stable, letting the USD ETF capture a local equity rally of roughly +41% into May 2013.","body_zh":"2012年中期起，印尼乘上全球新兴市场复苏东风：美联储于同年9月启动QE3，美元保持疲软，外资涌入高收益新兴市场资产，印尼大宗商品出口依然坚挺。印尼盾维持在约9,500-10,000/美元的相对稳定水平，使美元ETF得以捕捉约+41%的本地股票涨幅，至2013年5月。","drivers":["Fed QE3 dollar softness","EM capital inflow wave","Stable rupiah near 10,000","Commodity export revenues intact"],"drivers_zh":["美联储QE3压低美元","新兴市场资本流入潮","印尼盾稳定于约10,000","大宗商品出口收入稳健"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis EM rally, rupiah stable","title_zh":"危机后新兴市场反弹，印尼盾稳定","turn_id":"eido:trough:2012-06"},"2013-05-20":{"body":"Bernanke's May 2013 taper hint triggered a brutal reversal. Indonesia was tagged one of the 'Fragile Five', with a current-account deficit that had widened to around 4% of GDP, leaving it acutely exposed to capital outflows. The rupiah fell sharply as the Jakarta market also declined, producing a -40.8% USD loss in three months as both channels hit at once. Bank Indonesia raised its policy rate by roughly 175-200 bps and the government cut fuel subsidies, pushing fuel prices up about 40%, to restore stability.","body_zh":"伯南克2013年5月暗示缩减购债，触发剧烈逆转。印尼被列为'脆弱五国'之一，经常账户赤字已扩大至GDP约4%，对资本外流极度脆弱。印尼盾急贬，雅加达股市同步下跌，仅三个月便造成美元计价-40.8%的亏损，股票与汇率两个渠道同时受损。印尼央行将政策利率上调约175-200个基点，政府削减燃油补贴、推升油价约40%，以恢复稳定。","drivers":["Taper tantrum EM capital flight","Current-account deficit near 4% GDP","Rupiah slide amplifies USD losses","Forced fiscal-monetary tightening"],"drivers_zh":["缩减恐慌引发新兴市场资本出逃","经常账户赤字约GDP 4%","印尼盾贬值放大美元损失","被迫采取财政货币紧缩"],"prev_key":"2013-05","prev_key_chain":["2013-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Taper tantrum — rupiah double blow","title_zh":"缩减恐慌——印尼盾双重打击","turn_id":"eido:peak:2013-05"},"2013-08-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:trough:2013-08"},"2013-09-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:peak:2013-09"},"2014-01-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:trough:2014-01"},"2014-05-16":{"body":"From mid-2014 Indonesia entered a prolonged down-leg driven by the global commodity collapse — coal and palm oil, two of its largest exports, fell sharply as China demand slowed and supply ran ahead. Simultaneously the Fed's taper completion and approaching hike cycle strengthened the dollar, pushing the rupiah from around 11,500 toward 14,000+/USD by late 2015. The -42.8% USD decline into September 2015 reflected both a weak Jakarta market and a heavy currency-debasement component.","body_zh":"2014年中期起，印尼进入漫长下行段，由全球大宗商品崩跌驱动——煤炭和棕榈油（两大主要出口）因中国需求放缓和供应过剩而大幅下跌。同时，美联储完成缩减并临近加息，美元走强，印尼盾从约11,500贬向2015年底的14,000+/美元。至2015年9月-42.8%的美元跌幅，既反映雅加达股市疲软，也包含沉重的汇率贬值成分。","drivers":["Coal and palm oil price collapse","China demand slowdown","Fed taper + approaching hikes lift USD","Rupiah slides toward 14,000+/USD"],"drivers_zh":["煤炭和棕榈油价格崩跌","中国需求放缓","美联储缩减+临近加息推升美元","印尼盾贬向14,000+/美元"],"prev_key":"2014-07","prev_key_chain":["2014-07"],"rekey_shift_days":60,"status":"shifted","title":"Commodity bear + strong-dollar beatdown","title_zh":"大宗商品熊市+强美元打压","turn_id":"eido:peak:2014-05"},"2015-09-28":{"body":"From the September 2015 trough, Indonesia staged its longest up-leg in this window — about +89% over roughly 28 months to January 2018. The recovery was propelled by President Jokowi's infrastructure push and deregulation packages, a stabilization of coal and palm oil prices, the Fed's 2016 hike pause that eased EM pressure, and a gradually steadier rupiah. Commodity prices recovered into 2017 as Chinese stimulus reflated demand, amplifying USD returns.","body_zh":"自2015年9月谷底，印尼开启本窗口内最长的上升段——约+89%，历时约28个月至2018年1月。复苏由总统佐科威的基建推进和放松管制、煤炭和棕榈油价格企稳、2016年美联储暂停加息缓解新兴市场压力，以及印尼盾逐步回稳共同驱动。大宗商品价格随中国刺激政策在2017年回升，放大了美元计价回报。","drivers":["Jokowi infrastructure and deregulation","Commodity price stabilization and recovery","Fed 2016 pause eased EM outflows","Rupiah gradually steadier from 2015 lows"],"drivers_zh":["佐科威基建与放松管制","大宗商品价格企稳回升","2016年美联储暂停加息缓解新兴市场外流","印尼盾自2015年低位逐步回稳"],"prev_key":"2015-09","prev_key_chain":["2015-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Jokowi reforms + commodity bounce, long recovery","title_zh":"佐科威改革+大宗商品反弹，漫长复苏","turn_id":"eido:trough:2015-09"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:peak:2018-01"},"2018-10-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:trough:2018-10"},"2019-02-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:peak:2019-02"},"2019-05-17":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:trough:2019-05"},"2019-07-18":{"body":"From mid-2019 EIDO declined steadily into the March 2020 COVID crash, a combined -55.1% loss. The early phase (mid-2019 to early 2020) reflected slowing domestic growth, a widening current account, and a firm dollar amid US-China trade-war uncertainty, with the rupiah drifting to around 14,000/USD. The final plunge in February-March 2020 was the COVID shock — the Jakarta Composite fell sharply as global risk assets collapsed and the rupiah spiked past 16,000/USD.","body_zh":"自2019年中期，EIDO持续下跌，至2020年3月新冠崩盘，累计跌幅-55.1%。早期阶段（2019年中至2020年初）反映国内增长放缓、经常账户赤字扩大、中美贸易战不确定性下美元坚挺，印尼盾缓贬至约14,000/美元。2020年2-3月的最终急跌来自新冠冲击——全球风险资产崩跌，雅加达综合指数大幅下挫，印尼盾骤贬至16,000/美元以上。","drivers":["Indonesia-specific growth slowdown pre-COVID","Trade-war USD strength weight","COVID global risk-off shock","Rupiah spike past 16,000/USD"],"drivers_zh":["新冠前印尼经济增速放缓","贸易战美元走强拖累","新冠全球避险冲击","印尼盾急贬破16,000/美元"],"prev_key":"2019-07","prev_key_chain":["2019-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Pre-COVID slide into the crash","title_zh":"疫情前滑落至崩盘","turn_id":"eido:peak:2019-07"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The March 2020 trough began a +113.6% recovery over 10 months to January 2021. The Fed's emergency cuts and unlimited QE crushed the dollar and unleashed a large EM inflow wave. Indonesia benefited as coal demand rebounded with China's stimulus and palm oil rallied. The rupiah recovered from its crisis level back toward 14,000/USD by early 2021, adding to the dollar-return upswing alongside a robust Jakarta equity recovery.","body_zh":"2020年3月谷底开启了一段历时10个月至2021年1月、+113.6%的大幅反弹。美联储紧急降息及无限量QE压低美元，推动新兴市场大规模流入。随着中国刺激推动煤炭需求反弹、棕榈油上涨，印尼受益。印尼盾从危机低位回升至2021年初约14,000/美元，叠加雅加达股市强劲复苏，共同推动美元计价回报回升。","drivers":["Fed unlimited QE dollar suppression","EM inflow wave — Fragile Five reversion","Coal and palm oil commodity rebound","Rupiah recovery toward 14,000"],"drivers_zh":["美联储无限QE压低美元","新兴市场资金流入——脆弱五国逆转","煤炭和棕榈油反弹","印尼盾回升至约14,000"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID rebound — liquidity and commodity surge","title_zh":"新冠反弹——流动性与大宗商品激增","turn_id":"eido:trough:2020-03"},"2021-01-20":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:peak:2021-01"},"2021-07-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:trough:2021-07"},"2022-05-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:peak:2022-05"},"2024-06-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:trough:2024-06"},"2024-09-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eido:peak:2024-09"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From the April 2025 low, EIDO recovered +38.8% through January 2026, alongside a broader EM relief rally as the dollar softened and risk appetite returned after the 2025 tariff shock. Domestically, early optimism about Indonesia's new Danantara sovereign wealth fund (consolidating state-owned enterprises) and still-intact nickel and coal revenues supported the Jakarta market. The rally was relatively shallow and short-lived versus prior cycles, hinting at fragile fiscal fundamentals beneath the surface.","body_zh":"自2025年4月低点，EIDO反弹+38.8%至2026年1月，与美元走软、2025年关税冲击消退后风险偏好回暖带来的新兴市场整体反弹同步。在国内，市场对印尼新设的丹安塔拉主权财富基金（整合国有企业）的初期乐观情绪，以及仍然坚挺的镍和煤炭收入，为雅加达市场提供支撑。与以往周期相比，本轮反弹相对浅薄且短暂，暗示表面之下的财政基本面已显脆弱。","drivers":["EM-wide relief rally on USD softness","Nickel and coal revenues still intact","Danantara sovereign-wealth-fund optimism","Shallow recovery vs prior cycles — fragility signal"],"drivers_zh":["美元走软推动新兴市场普遍反弹","镍和煤炭收入仍稳健","丹安塔拉主权财富基金乐观情绪","与以往周期相比反弹较浅——脆弱信号"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Brief Prabowo-era relief rally","title_zh":"普拉博沃时代短暂反弹","turn_id":"eido:trough:2025-04"},"2026-01-15":{"body":"From January 2026 EIDO fell -43.8% into a June trough, the worst-performing country ETF in the universe. The drivers were a loss of policy credibility under President Prabowo: a roughly $20bn free-meals program and other populist spending, fears over Bank Indonesia's independence, and a move to bring palm-oil and coal exports under centralized state control. MSCI and FTSE index downgrades forced heavy foreign outflows (over $3bn), the rupiah broke toward record lows near 18,000/USD, and the Jakarta Composite fell about 36% from its January peak. The simultaneous equity-and-currency collapse is the defining 'Fragile Five' signature.","body_zh":"自2026年1月，EIDO下跌-43.8%至6月谷底，成为本宇宙中表现最差的国家ETF。驱动因素是普拉博沃总统执政下政策公信力的下滑：约200亿美元免费餐计划及其他民粹支出、对印尼央行独立性的担忧、以及将棕榈油和煤炭出口收归中央管控。MSCI和FTSE指数下调迫使外资大规模流出（逾30亿美元），印尼盾跌向接近18,000/美元的历史低位，雅加达综合指数较1月高点跌约36%。股票与汇率的同步崩溃，正是'脆弱五国'的标志性特征。","drivers":["Policy-credibility loss under Prabowo","~$20bn free-meals populist spending + BI-independence fears","Palm-oil and coal export centralization","MSCI/FTSE downgrades force foreign outflows; rupiah near 18,000/USD"],"drivers_zh":["普拉博沃执政下政策公信力下滑","约200亿美元免费餐民粹支出+央行独立性担忧","棕榈油和煤炭出口收归中央管控","MSCI/FTSE下调迫使外资流出；印尼盾接近18,000/美元"],"prev_key":"2026-01","prev_key_chain":["2026-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal-credibility shock — rupiah record lows","title_zh":"财政公信力冲击——印尼盾创历史低位","turn_id":"eido:peak:2026-01"},"2026-06-08":{"body":"Off the June 2026 low, EIDO has bounced about +20% — the move that lifts cycle position off zero to 8.2. At this stage it is an early, low-conviction recovery rather than a confirmed cycle turn: it would need rupiah stabilization, a pause in foreign outflows, and easing policy-credibility concerns to mature into a durable up-leg. Treat as a washed-out, oversold bounce pending confirmation.","body_zh":"自2026年6月低点，EIDO反弹约+20%——正是这一波动将周期位置从零抬升至8.2。现阶段这是一次早期、低确信度的修复，而非已确认的周期转折：需要印尼盾企稳、外资流出停歇、政策公信力担忧缓解，才可能演变为持久的上升段。在确认之前，视为超卖后的washed-out反弹。","drivers":["Oversold bounce off deep trough","Needs rupiah stabilization to confirm","Foreign-outflow pause required","Policy-credibility overhang unresolved"],"drivers_zh":["深度谷底的超卖反弹","需印尼盾企稳确认","需外资流出停歇","政策公信力阴霾未消"],"prev_key":"2026-06","prev_key_chain":["2026-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Nascent bounce off the trough","title_zh":"谷底初步反弹","turn_id":"eido:trough:2026-06"}},"now":"EIDO sits at a deep trough — cycle position 8.2 out of 100, below its 200-day moving average, and the worst-ranked country ETF in the universe with a -50.1% trailing return and roughly -34% relative strength vs SPY over the past 63 days. The 2026 collapse is a classic Fragile-Five dual hit: Indonesian equities AND the rupiah falling together. The triggers were a loss of policy credibility under President Prabowo — costly populist spending led by a ~$20bn free-meals program, fears over Bank Indonesia's independence, and a move to centralize palm-oil and coal exports — which combined with MSCI/FTSE index downgrades to force heavy foreign outflows (over $3bn). The rupiah sank toward record lows near 18,000/USD and the Jakarta Composite fell roughly 36% from its January 2026 peak. At a position of 8.2 the ETF is washed-out on a cycle basis, but the underlying macro and political risks are not yet resolved.","now_zh":"EIDO处于深度谷底——周期位置仅8.2/100，位于200日均线下方，是本宇宙中排名垫底的国家ETF，过去回报-50.1%，过去63日相对SPY的相对强弱约-34%。2026年的崩跌是典型的\"脆弱五国\"双重打击：印尼股票与印尼盾同步下跌。导火索是普拉博沃总统执政下政策公信力的下滑——以约200亿美元免费餐计划为代表的高成本民粹支出、对印尼央行独立性的担忧、以及将棕榈油和煤炭出口收归中央管控的举措——叠加MSCI/FTSE指数下调，迫使外资大规模流出（逾30亿美元）。印尼盾跌向接近18,000/美元的历史低位，雅加达综合指数较2026年1月高点跌约36%。周期位置8.2意味着技术上已极度超卖，但宏观与政治风险尚未消除。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"epol":{"legs":{"2011-08-10":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:trough:2011-08"},"2011-08-31":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2011-08"},"2011-09-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:trough:2011-09"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2011-10"},"2012-01-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:trough:2012-01"},"2012-02-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2012-02"},"2012-06-01":{"body":"After the eurozone sovereign-debt crisis stabilized in mid-2012, helped by ECB President Draghi's July 2012 'whatever it takes' pledge, peripheral and EM European markets rallied. Poland, with relatively sound public finances and resilient domestic demand, participated in the relief rally, and a recovering zloty against the dollar amplified the USD-denominated gain of roughly 51% over about seven months into January 2013.","body_zh":"2012年7月欧央行行长德拉吉'不惜一切代价'讲话推动下，欧元区主权债务危机于2012年中期企稳，外围及新兴欧洲市场反弹。波兰凭借相对稳健的公共财政和有韧性的内需参与了这波救济性行情，兹罗提对美元回升进一步放大了至2013年1月约七个月内约51%的美元计价涨幅。","drivers":["ECB 'whatever it takes' backstop","EM risk-appetite recovery","PLN/USD tailwind","Poland's resilient domestic demand"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-eurocrisis relief rally","title_zh":"欧债危机后救济性反弹","turn_id":"epol:trough:2012-06"},"2013-01-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2013-01"},"2013-06-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:trough:2013-06"},"2013-10-29":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2013-10"},"2015-03-13":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:trough:2015-03"},"2015-05-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2015-05"},"2016-01-21":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:trough:2016-01"},"2016-03-31":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2016-03"},"2016-07-05":{"body":"From mid-2016 a synchronized global reflation trade — commodity-price recovery, a stabilizing China, and improving global growth — lifted EM Europe broadly. Poland additionally benefited from absorption of the 2014-2020 EU structural-fund cycle flowing into infrastructure and manufacturing. EPOL rose roughly 92% over about 18 months into January 2018.","body_zh":"2016年中期起，大宗商品价格回升、中国经济企稳及全球增长改善共同推动全球同步再通胀交易，广泛提振新兴欧洲。波兰还受益于2014-2020欧盟结构基金周期的吸收，资金流入基础设施和制造业。EPOL在至2018年1月约18个月内上涨约92%。","drivers":["Global reflation trade","EU structural-fund absorption","Commodity-price recovery","Improving global growth"],"prev_key":"2016-07","prev_key_chain":["2016-07"],"status":"exact","title":"EM reflation and EU fund cycle","title_zh":"新兴市场再通胀与欧盟资金周期","turn_id":"epol:trough:2016-07"},"2018-01-24":{"body":"The Fed's 2018 tightening and a broadly stronger dollar drained liquidity from EM markets, and the zloty weakened against the dollar. EPOL fell about 57% from its January 2018 peak through the March 2020 trough, with the COVID-19 crash forming the final leg down. Persistent EU rule-of-law tensions over Polish judicial reforms also weighed on sentiment and kept the risk premium elevated.","body_zh":"2018年美联储紧缩及美元整体走强从新兴市场抽走流动性，兹罗提对美元走弱。EPOL从2018年1月峰值到2020年3月谷底下跌约57%，新冠疫情冲击构成最后一段跌势。波兰司法改革引发的与欧盟持续的法治争端也压制情绪、推高风险溢价。","drivers":["Fed tightening / USD strength","EM liquidity drain","PLN/USD depreciation","EU rule-of-law dispute risk premium","COVID-19 final leg crash"],"prev_key":"2018-01","prev_key_chain":["2018-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Tightening-cycle downturn into COVID","title_zh":"紧缩周期下行直至新冠","turn_id":"epol:peak:2018-01"},"2020-03-16":{"body":"The post-COVID liquidity flood — NBP rate cuts, ECB asset purchases, and Polish fiscal support — fueled a sharp bounce off the March 2020 low. EPOL gained about 52% into August 2020 as feared bank-sector loan losses proved overstated and the zloty partially recovered.","body_zh":"波兰国家银行降息、欧央行资产购买及波兰财政支持共同引发的新冠后流动性洪潮，推动市场从2020年3月低点大幅反弹。随着所担忧的银行业贷款损失被证明过度，兹罗提部分修复，EPOL在至2020年8月期间上涨约52%。","drivers":["NBP emergency rate cuts","ECB QE spillover","Fiscal support packages","Bank-sector loss fears overstated"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID recovery — first bounce","title_zh":"新冠疫情后首波反弹","turn_id":"epol:trough:2020-03"},"2020-08-18":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2020-08"},"2020-10-30":{"body":"The second, stronger leg of the COVID recovery ran from October 2020 to October 2021, driven by vaccine-rollout optimism, surging European industrial production, and a construction boom fueled by record-low NBP rates. Poland's export-oriented manufacturing (autos, furniture, electronics) benefited from the global goods-demand surge, and EPOL gained about 73%.","body_zh":"2020年10月至2021年10月，新冠后复苏进入第二段更强劲行情，由疫苗推广乐观预期、欧洲工业生产大幅回升，以及波兰国家银行超低利率催生的建筑热潮驱动。波兰出口导向型制造业（汽车、家具、电子）受益于全球商品需求激增，EPOL上涨约73%。","drivers":["Vaccine rollout / re-opening","European industrial-demand surge","NBP near-zero rates fueling construction","Manufacturing export boom"],"prev_key":"2020-10","prev_key_chain":["2020-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Re-opening bull: ~73% in a year","title_zh":"重开放牛市：约一年涨73%","turn_id":"epol:trough:2020-10"},"2021-10-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2021-10"},"2022-03-07":{"body":"Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine in late February 2022 triggered an immediate geopolitical shock across CEE markets. EPOL had a brief technical bounce of roughly 28% in early March 2022 before reversing. As Ukraine's primary logistics corridor and refugee host, Poland faced acute risk-premium repricing: the zloty fell against the dollar, energy costs surged, and inflation spiked into double digits. From the March 2022 local peak EPOL fell about 45% to the October 2022 trough.","body_zh":"2022年2月底俄罗斯全面入侵乌克兰，立即在中东欧市场引发地缘政治冲击。EPOL在2022年3月初短暂技术性反弹约28%后逆转。作为乌克兰主要后勤走廊和难民接收国，波兰面临急剧的风险溢价重新定价：兹罗提对美元下跌，能源成本飙升，通胀升至两位数。从2022年3月局部峰值起，EPOL下跌约45%至2022年10月谷底。","drivers":["Russia-Ukraine war geopolitical shock","PLN sharp depreciation","Energy-cost surge","Double-digit inflation spike"],"prev_key":"2022-03","prev_key_chain":["2022-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Russia-invasion shock and crash","title_zh":"俄乌战争冲击与急跌","turn_id":"epol:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-30":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2022-03"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"October 2022 marked a global EM bottom as the Fed's tightening pace slowed and the dollar rolled over. For Poland the geopolitical war discount began to normalize as the front line stabilized, and the zloty recovered sharply as EM risk appetite returned. EPOL roughly doubled (about +100%) into July 2023, its fastest doubling in the 15-year window. Note: this rally preceded the EU rule-of-law resolution — the frozen EU funds were not actually unlocked until after the October 2023 election.","body_zh":"2022年10月随着美联储紧缩步伐放缓、美元见顶回落，全球新兴市场触底。对波兰而言，前线趋于稳定使地缘政治战争折价开始正常化，兹罗提随新兴市场风险偏好回归而大幅升值。EPOL在至2023年7月期间约翻倍（约+100%），创15年窗口内最快翻倍纪录。注意：此轮上涨发生在欧盟法治争端解决之前——冻结的欧盟资金直到2023年10月大选之后才实际解锁。","drivers":["Fed-pivot / EM liquidity return","War-discount normalization as the front stabilized","PLN recovery on improved risk sentiment"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"CEE rebound: ~100% in nine months","title_zh":"中东欧反弹：九个月约翻倍","turn_id":"epol:trough:2022-10"},"2023-07-31":{"body":"After roughly doubling in nine months, EPOL consolidated and fell about 22% from July to October 2023. Global rate concerns re-emerged as US 10-year yields pushed toward 5%, pressuring EM assets broadly, and pre-election uncertainty ahead of Poland's October 2023 parliamentary vote weighed on sentiment.","body_zh":"在九个月约翻倍后，EPOL于2023年7月至10月回调约22%。美国十年期国债收益率逼近5%，全球加息忧虑再起，广泛压制新兴市场资产；2023年10月波兰议会大选前的不确定性也压制了情绪。","drivers":["US yields near 5% — EM pressure","Post-doubling profit taking","Pre-election political uncertainty"],"prev_key":"2023-07","prev_key_chain":["2023-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Summer correction — profit taking","title_zh":"夏季回调：获利了结","turn_id":"epol:peak:2023-07"},"2023-10-03":{"body":"Poland's October 2023 parliamentary election produced a historic pivot: the nationalist PiS government lost its majority and a pro-EU coalition led by Donald Tusk took power in December 2023. Markets re-rated sharply — the EU rule-of-law cloud lifted and roughly EUR 137 billion in previously frozen EU recovery and cohesion funds was unlocked in early 2024, with foreign investors returning aggressively to Polish equities and the zloty strengthening, amplifying USD returns. EPOL was among the world's best-performing single-country markets over this stretch. The cycle ran a measured 184% (trough-to-peak) into the June 2026 peak. The election, the Tusk government, and the EU-fund unlock are verified through early 2024; the continuation into 2026 is reported as the dashboard's measured magnitude rather than attributed to specific later catalysts.","body_zh":"2023年10月波兰议会大选带来历史性转折：民族主义的法律与公正党失去多数席位，由图斯克领导的亲欧盟联合政府于2023年12月执政。市场大幅重估——欧盟法治阴云消散，约1370亿欧元此前冻结的欧盟复苏与凝聚基金于2024年初解锁，外国投资者积极回归波兰股市，兹罗提走强放大了美元计价回报。在此区间EPOL跻身全球表现最佳的单国市场之列。该周期从低点到2026年6月峰值录得184%涨幅。大选、图斯克政府及欧盟资金解锁经核实截至2024年初；至2026年的延续以仪表盘所测涨幅呈现，未归因于具体的后续催化剂。","drivers":["Pro-EU Tusk government — political re-rating","~EUR 137bn frozen EU funds unlocked (early 2024)","Foreign investor re-entry into Polish equities","PLN appreciation amplifying USD returns"],"prev_key":"2023-10","prev_key_chain":["2023-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Pro-EU pivot: 184% bull run","title_zh":"转向亲欧盟：184%牛市行情","turn_id":"epol:trough:2023-10"},"2024-05-20":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:peak:2024-05"},"2024-12-18":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"epol:trough:2024-12"}},"now":"EPOL (iShares MSCI Poland ETF) registered a cycle peak in June 2026, capping an extraordinary 184% advance from its October 2023 trough, and the dashboard now reads it in Trough phase at a cycle position of 31.2 out of 100, meaning the ETF has already pulled back from that high. Relative strength versus the US has turned mildly negative over the past quarter (rs_63d -4.1%), ranking 8th among the tracked markets. The ETF still sits above its 200-day moving average, so the broader uptrend is not yet decisively broken. The model projects the next significant trough around November 2026, roughly five months out.","now_zh":"EPOL（iShares MSCI波兰ETF）于2026年6月触及周期峰值，为自2023年10月低点起184%的非凡涨幅画上句号。目前仪表盘将其读为\"谷底\"阶段，周期位置31.2（满分100），意味着ETF已从该高点回撤。相对于美国市场，近三个月相对强度略为负值（rs_63d -4.1%），在跟踪市场中排名第8。ETF仍处于200日均线上方，因此中期上升趋势尚未明确破坏。模型预测下一个显著低点约在2026年11月前后，距今约五个月。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewa":{"legs":{"2011-08-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2011-08"},"2011-08-31":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2011-08"},"2011-10-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2011-10"},"2011-10-27":{"body":"After the 2011 global risk-off selloff, Australia rebounded as Chinese infrastructure and property demand kept iron ore prices elevated and the RBA's 2012-2013 easing cycle supported domestic financials. The AUD held near parity with the USD for much of this period, reducing currency drag for USD investors and lifting the ETF +48% into the April 2013 peak.","body_zh":"2011年全球风险规避抛售后，中国基础设施和房地产需求令铁矿石价格保持高位，2012-2013年澳储行降息周期支撑国内金融板块，澳大利亚市场随之反弹。这一时期澳元长期接近与美元平价，降低了美元投资者的汇率阻力，推动ETF上涨+48%至2013年4月峰值。","drivers":["China property/infrastructure demand","Elevated iron ore prices","AUD near parity vs USD","RBA easing cycle 2012-2013"],"drivers_zh":["中国房地产/基础设施需求","铁矿石价格高位","澳元接近与美元平价","澳储行2012-2013年降息周期"],"prev_key":"2011-11","prev_key_chain":["2011-11"],"rekey_shift_days":19,"status":"shifted","title":"China demand & AUD strength","title_zh":"中国需求与澳元走强","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2011-10"},"2012-06-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2012-06"},"2013-04-30":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2013-04"},"2013-07-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2013-07"},"2013-10-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2013-10"},"2014-02-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2014-02"},"2014-09-03":{"body":"China's property market decelerated through 2014-2015 and iron ore collapsed from above $130/t toward $40/t by early 2016, gutting the earnings outlook for BHP and Rio Tinto. The AUD/USD fell sharply over the same span, compounding the loss for USD investors. The combined commodity and FX shock drove a -35% drawdown into the January 2016 trough.","body_zh":"2014至2015年中国房地产市场降温，铁矿石价格从130美元/吨以上崩跌至2016年初的约40美元/吨，严重打压必和必拓和力拓的盈利预期。同期澳元/美元大幅走低，加重了美元投资者的损失。大宗商品与汇率的双重冲击导致EWA回撤-35%，至2016年1月触底。","drivers":["Iron ore collapse toward $40/t","China property slowdown 2014-2015","AUD/USD sharp decline","BHP/Rio earnings downgrades"],"drivers_zh":["铁矿石崩跌至约40美元/吨","中国房地产放缓2014-2015","澳元/美元大幅走低","必和必拓/力拓盈利下调"],"prev_key":"2014-09","prev_key_chain":["2014-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Iron ore crash & AUD devaluation","title_zh":"铁矿石崩盘与澳元贬值","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2014-09"},"2016-01-15":{"body":"China's supply-side reform and infrastructure stimulus from late 2015 reflated commodity prices; iron ore bottomed in early 2016 and roughly doubled by 2017. The AUD recovered from its lows, providing a currency tailwind for USD investors, and Australian banks benefited from a stable housing cycle. EWA advanced +62% into the January 2018 peak, tracking the synchronized global reflation trade.","body_zh":"中国自2015年底启动供给侧改革和基础设施刺激，大宗商品价格回升；铁矿石于2016年初触底，至2017年约翻倍。澳元从低点回升，为美元投资者提供汇率顺风，澳大利亚银行业也受益于稳定的房市周期。EWA上涨+62%至2018年1月峰值，紧密跟踪全球同步再通胀交易。","drivers":["China supply-side reform & infrastructure push","Iron ore doubling from 2016 lows","AUD/USD recovery","Global synchronized reflation 2016-2017"],"drivers_zh":["中国供给侧改革与基础设施推进","铁矿石从2016年低点约翻倍","澳元/美元回升","全球同步再通胀2016-2017"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Commodity trough & China reflation","title_zh":"大宗商品触底与中国再通胀","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The December 2018 global growth scare bottomed with the Fed's early-2019 pivot and a US-China trade truce that eased fears of a sharp China slowdown. Iron ore got a further boost from the January 2019 Brumadinho dam disaster in Brazil, which knocked out significant Vale production and sent prices to multi-year highs. EWA gained +33% before COVID-19 fears hit in early 2020.","body_zh":"2018年12月全球增长恐慌随着美联储2019年初转向和中美贸易休战而触底，缓解了对中国急剧放缓的担忧。铁矿石还受到2019年1月巴西布鲁马迪尼奥溃坝事故的额外提振——该事故令淡水河谷大量产能停产，铁矿石价格创多年新高。EWA在2020年初新冠疫情恐慌来袭前上涨了+33%。","drivers":["Fed pivot early 2019","US-China trade truce","Brumadinho dam disaster cut Vale supply","Iron ore to multi-year highs"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年初转向","中美贸易休战","布鲁马迪尼奥溃坝减少淡水河谷供应","铁矿石升至多年高点"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade-truce bounce & Vale supply shock","title_zh":"贸易休战反弹与淡水河谷供应冲击","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-16":{"body":"COVID-19 fears triggered a synchronized global risk-off collapse. EWA fell -45.5% into the March 2020 trough as commodity demand expectations cratered and the AUD/USD plunged to around 0.57, its lowest in over a decade, while Australian financials faced a near-zero rate environment and rising loan-loss provisions. The speed and severity of the drawdown reflected the FX amplification characteristic of commodity-currency markets.","body_zh":"新冠疫情恐慌引发全球同步风险规避崩盘。EWA下跌-45.5%至2020年3月低点：大宗商品需求预期骤降，澳元/美元跌至约0.57，为十余年来最低，同时澳大利亚金融板块面临接近零利率的环境和贷款损失准备金上升的压力。回撤之快之深，反映出商品货币市场特有的汇率放大效应。","drivers":["COVID-19 global risk-off","AUD/USD plunged to around 0.57","Commodity demand expectations cratered","Bank loan-loss provisions rising"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情全球风险规避","澳元/美元跌至约0.57","大宗商品需求预期骤降","银行贷款损失准备金上升"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 commodity & AUD collapse","title_zh":"新冠疫情引发大宗商品与澳元崩跌","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"Massive global stimulus and China's rapid infrastructure-driven recovery sent commodity demand surging. Iron ore reached above $200/t in May 2021, a record at the time. The AUD recovered strongly, adding to USD returns, and Australian banks rallied on loan-loss reserve releases. The +125% gain into the April 2022 peak was one of EWA's strongest cycles in the modern era, fueled by both the commodities supercycle and the AUD recovery.","body_zh":"全球大规模刺激政策与中国基础设施驱动的快速复苏推动大宗商品需求急剧攀升。铁矿石于2021年5月涨至200美元/吨以上，创当时纪录。澳元强劲回升，为美元投资者带来额外回报，银行业随贷款损失准备金释放而反弹。至2022年4月峰值上涨+125%，是近代以来最强劲的一轮周期之一，同时受益于大宗商品超级周期与澳元回升。","drivers":["Iron ore above $200/t in May 2021","China rapid infrastructure recovery","AUD/USD recovery","Global fiscal stimulus wave","Bank loan-loss reserve releases"],"drivers_zh":["铁矿石2021年5月涨至200美元/吨以上","中国基础设施快速复苏","澳元/美元回升","全球财政刺激浪潮","银行贷款损失准备金释放"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Commodity supercycle & fiscal boom","title_zh":"大宗商品超级周期与财政刺激繁荣","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2020-03"},"2021-06-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2021-06"},"2022-01-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2022-01"},"2022-04-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2022-04"},"2022-10-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2022-10"},"2023-02-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2023-02"},"2023-10-27":{"body":"After China's post-zero-COVID reopening disappointed on growth, renewed China stimulus expectations and a stabilization in iron ore prices in late 2023 provided a fresh entry point for EWA. The AUD steadied and Australian banks delivered resilient earnings. EWA gained +37% into the September 2024 peak.","body_zh":"中国后清零时代的经济重开在增长上令市场失望后，2023年底新一轮中国刺激预期与铁矿石价格企稳为EWA提供了新的买入窗口。澳元趋于稳定，澳大利亚银行业盈利稳健。EWA上涨+37%至2024年9月峰值。","drivers":["Renewed China stimulus expectations late 2023","Iron ore price stabilization","AUD steadied","Australian banks resilient earnings"],"drivers_zh":["2023年底中国新一轮刺激预期","铁矿石价格企稳","澳元趋稳","澳大利亚银行业盈利稳健"],"prev_key":"2023-10","prev_key_chain":["2023-10"],"status":"exact","title":"China stimulus hopes & iron ore stabilization","title_zh":"中国刺激预期与铁矿石企稳","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2023-10"},"2024-09-30":{"body":"Iron ore prices retreated from mid-2024 as China's property sector stayed deeply stressed and steel demand was revised down. The AUD weakened alongside the commodity complex. EWA fell -21.9% from its September 2024 high into the April 2025 trough, with the decline concentrated in materials while financials provided a partial cushion.","body_zh":"铁矿石价格自2024年中期回落，原因是中国房地产行业持续深度承压，钢铁需求预期被下调。澳元随大宗商品复合体走弱。EWA从2024年9月高点至2025年4月低点下跌-21.9%，跌幅集中于材料板块，金融板块提供了部分缓冲。","drivers":["Iron ore retreat from mid-2024","China property sector stress","Steel demand revised down","AUD weakened with commodities"],"drivers_zh":["铁矿石2024年中期回落","中国房地产行业承压","钢铁需求预期下调","澳元随大宗商品走弱"],"prev_key":"2024-09","prev_key_chain":["2024-09"],"status":"exact","title":"China demand doubts & AUD weakness","title_zh":"中国需求疑虑与澳元走弱","turn_id":"ewa:peak:2024-09"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From the April 2025 trough EWA advanced +50% into its April 2026 peak, consistent with recovering commodity-linked equities and a firmer AUD. For this most recent leg, the magnitude and direction are data-derived; specific catalysts are not asserted here given the limits of reliable verification beyond late 2025.","body_zh":"EWA从2025年4月低点上涨+50%至2026年4月峰值，与商品关联股回升及澳元走强相一致。对于这一最新的周期腿，其幅度与方向均基于量化数据；鉴于2025年底之后可靠核实的局限，本文不对具体催化因素作出断言。","drivers":["Commodity-linked equity recovery","Firmer AUD","Magnitude and direction data-derived"],"drivers_zh":["商品关联股回升","澳元走强","幅度与方向基于量化数据"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Recovery into the 2026 peak","title_zh":"复苏至2026年峰值","turn_id":"ewa:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"EWA is in Downturn at cycle position 34.7/100, having peaked in April 2026 and slipped since. Its 63-day relative strength of -10.4 versus SPY ranks 18th of the 24 country and regional markets tracked, placing it among the weaker performers as commodity-linked, China-demand-sensitive markets lag a US-led tape. The ETF still sits above its 200-day moving average, so the move reads as a correction within a longer uptrend rather than a structural breakdown, but near-term momentum is clearly negative.","now_zh":"EWA目前处于下行阶段，周期位置34.7/100，于2026年4月见顶后回落。过去63日相对SPY表现为-10.4，在所追踪的24个国家及区域市场中排名第18，属于表现较弱的一档，反映出在美股领涨的环境下，商品关联、对中国需求敏感的市场相对落后。ETF仍位于200日均线之上，因此该走势更像是长期上行趋势内的修正，而非结构性破位，但短期动能明显偏弱。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewc":{"legs":{"2011-10-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewc:trough:2011-10"},"2012-03-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewc:peak:2012-03"},"2012-06-04":{"body":"From mid-2012 through September 2014, EWC rose roughly 40% as global risk appetite recovered from the 2011 European debt crisis. Brent crude held above $100/bbl, Canadian oil sands production expanded, and the TSX energy and materials sectors drove the gain. The CAD traded near parity with the USD through much of this period, limiting currency drag and keeping USD-denominated returns close to local gains.","body_zh":"2012年中至2014年9月，EWC累计上涨约40%。全球风险偏好从2011年欧债危机中复苏，布伦特原油稳定在100美元/桶上方，加拿大油砂产能持续扩张，TSX能源及原材料板块引领涨势。这一时期加元与美元基本保持平价，汇率拖累有限，美元计价回报与本地涨幅接近。","drivers":["Global risk-on post-EU crisis","Oil above $100/bbl","CAD near parity","TSX materials expansion"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Commodity recovery, risk-on lift","title_zh":"大宗商品复苏，风险偏好回升","turn_id":"ewc:trough:2012-06"},"2014-09-03":{"body":"From September 2014 to January 2016, EWC fell roughly 41% after OPEC's November 2014 decision to defend market share triggered a collapse in WTI crude from above $90 to below $30. The Bank of Canada cut rates twice in 2015 to cushion the shock, sending the CAD down roughly 20% against the USD. This currency depreciation compounded the local equity losses for USD-based EWC holders, producing one of the sharpest drawdowns in the ETF's history.","body_zh":"2014年9月至2016年1月，EWC累计下跌约41%。欧佩克于2014年11月决定维持市场份额而非减产，导致WTI原油从90美元以上暴跌至30美元以下。加拿大央行2015年两度降息以缓冲冲击，加元兑美元贬值约20%。汇率贬值叠加本地股市下跌，使美元计价的EWC持有者遭受了该ETF历史上最惨烈的回撤之一。","drivers":["OPEC Nov 2014 supply war","WTI crude collapse to sub-$30","CAD -20% vs USD","Bank of Canada rate cuts"],"prev_key":"2014-09","prev_key_chain":["2014-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil crash & strong USD erase gains","title_zh":"油价崩跌与强美元抹去涨幅","turn_id":"ewc:peak:2014-09"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"From January 2016 to January 2018, EWC surged roughly 70% in USD terms. The OPEC-Russia production cut agreement in late 2016 stabilized oil prices and sparked a recovery in the Canadian energy sector. Simultaneously, the CAD rebounded alongside improving commodity terms of trade and a synchronized global growth upswing. Canadian bank earnings remained robust, reinforcing the broad market recovery.","body_zh":"2016年1月至2018年1月，EWC美元计价涨幅约70%。欧佩克与俄罗斯于2016年底达成减产协议，油价企稳并推动加拿大能源板块复苏。与此同时，大宗商品贸易条件改善及全球增长共振拉动加元反弹。加拿大银行业盈利保持稳健，进一步支撑大盘全面回升。","drivers":["OPEC-Russia late-2016 cut deal","Oil price recovery","CAD rebound","Synchronized global growth uplift"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil rebound & CAD recovery rally","title_zh":"油价反弹与加元回升驱动反攻","turn_id":"ewc:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewc:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"From December 2018 through February 2020, EWC gained roughly 36% as a US-China trade truce and the Fed's pivot to easing lifted global risk assets. Oil prices recovered from the Q4 2018 sell-off and the USMCA (successor to NAFTA) was signed in late 2018, removing a key political overhang for the Canadian economy. The CAD was relatively stable against the USD, allowing full participation in the TSX rally.","body_zh":"2018年12月至2020年2月，EWC累计上涨约36%。美中贸易休战及美联储转向宽松提振全球风险资产，油价从2018年四季度暴跌中回升，美墨加协定（USMCA，取代北美自贸协定）于2018年底签署，消除了加拿大经济的主要政治不确定性。加元兑美元相对稳定，EWC得以充分参与TSX的上涨行情。","drivers":["US-China trade truce","Fed pivot to easing","USMCA signing removes NAFTA risk","Oil price recovery"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Late-cycle extension into pandemic peak","title_zh":"周期末段延伸至疫情前高点","turn_id":"ewc:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"In just over four weeks from late February to late March 2020, EWC collapsed roughly 43% — among the steepest drops in its history. The COVID-19 pandemic triggered a simultaneous global demand shock and a Saudi-Russia oil price war that would send WTI briefly negative in April 2020. Canada's heavy exposure to energy and financial sectors magnified the drawdown versus other developed markets, while the CAD fell sharply against the USD as risk-off demand swept global markets.","body_zh":"2020年2月底至3月底短短四周内，EWC暴跌约43%，创历史最大跌幅之一。新冠疫情引发全球需求骤降，叠加沙特与俄罗斯石油价格战，并令WTI原油在2020年4月一度跌至负值。加拿大对能源及金融板块的高度集中使其回撤幅度超过多数发达市场，避险资金涌入美元令加元大幅贬值，进一步放大了美元计价的损失。","drivers":["COVID-19 global demand shock","Saudi-Russia oil price war","CAD risk-off sell-off","TSX energy & financials double hit"],"prev_key":"2020-02","prev_key_chain":["2020-02"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash: commodity and credit shock","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：大宗商品与信贷双重冲击","turn_id":"ewc:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From March 2020 through March 2022, EWC surged roughly 140% — its largest bull leg in the 15-year window. Massive fiscal and monetary stimulus in Canada and the US combined with supply disruptions to ignite a commodity supercycle: WTI crude rallied from its trough back above $100, base metals soared, and lumber prices hit all-time highs. The CAD recovered sharply, trading above 0.80 USD by late 2021 and adding a meaningful currency tailwind to the local TSX gains.","body_zh":"2020年3月至2022年3月，EWC累计大涨约140%，为15年窗口内最大一段牛市行情。加拿大与美国推出大规模财政及货币刺激措施，叠加供应端中断，引爆新一轮大宗商品超级周期：WTI原油从低谷反弹至100美元以上，基础金属大涨，木材价格创历史新高。加元大幅回升，2021年底一度突破0.80美元，为TSX本地涨幅再添汇率顺风。","drivers":["Commodity supercycle (oil, metals, lumber)","Massive fiscal stimulus","CAD recovery to 0.80+ USD","Supply-chain disruption premium"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Stimulus & commodity supercycle launch","title_zh":"财政刺激与大宗商品超级周期启动","turn_id":"ewc:trough:2020-03"},"2022-03-30":{"body":"From March 2022 to October 2022, EWC fell roughly 25%. Although commodity prices spiked further after Russia's February 2022 invasion of Ukraine, the rapid Fed rate hike cycle crushed risk appetite and triggered a global growth scare. The CAD weakened as the USD surged across major pairs, compressing USD-denominated EWC returns beyond what local TSX declines alone would imply.","body_zh":"2022年3月至10月，EWC下跌约25%。尽管俄罗斯2022年2月入侵乌克兰后大宗商品价格曾再度飙升，但美联储随后激进加息重创风险偏好，引发全球经济衰退担忧。美元强势横扫主要货币对，加元走弱，使EWC美元计价跌幅超出TSX本地跌幅。","drivers":["Fed rapid hike cycle","USD surge vs CAD","Global growth scare","Commodity demand destruction fears"],"prev_key":"2022-03","prev_key_chain":["2022-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed hike cycle knocks commodity stocks","title_zh":"美联储加息周期打压大宗商品股","turn_id":"ewc:peak:2022-03"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"From October 2022 through June 2026, EWC gained roughly 111% — a sustained multi-year recovery as the US economy proved resilient, oil prices stabilized, and appetite returned for commodity-linked developed-market assets. Canadian banks rebuilt earnings as recession fears subsided, and the Bank of Canada began a gradual easing cycle in 2024. The CAD stayed under modest pressure from persistent USD strength but avoided the punishing depreciation of prior downturns, allowing local gains to largely translate into USD returns. The leg extends into 2026, where the path is more uncertain.","body_zh":"2022年10月至2026年6月，EWC累计上涨约111%，是一段由美国经济展现韧性、油价企稳以及大宗商品挂钩发达市场资产需求复苏共同驱动的多年行情。随着衰退担忧消散，加拿大银行业盈利逐步修复，加拿大央行亦于2024年启动渐进式降息周期。加元虽因美元持续偏强而承压，但未重演此前周期中的大幅贬值，本地涨幅基本得以转化为美元计价回报。该波段延伸至2026年，后续路径不确定性较高。","drivers":["US economy resilient","Oil price stabilization","Bank of Canada easing from 2024","Canadian bank earnings recovery"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Soft-landing recovery & energy re-rating","title_zh":"软着陆复苏与能源板块重估","turn_id":"ewc:trough:2022-10"},"2024-12-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewc:peak:2024-12"},"2025-04-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewc:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"EWC is in the Trough phase as of end-June 2026, sitting at a cycle position of just 20.9 out of 100 — historically washed-out territory. The ETF has shed about 7.8% relative to SPY over the trailing 63 days, ranking 13th of 24 markets tracked, as oil, base metals, and the Canadian dollar all face headwinds from global growth concerns and trade uncertainty. EWC still trades above its 200-day moving average, but the cycle model projects the next trough around November 2026, suggesting the current weakness may persist before a durable recovery takes hold.","now_zh":"截至2026年6月底，EWC处于周期低谷阶段，周期位置仅为20.9/100，属历史上的深度超卖区间。过去63个交易日，EWC相对标普500落后约7.8%，在24个追踪市场中排名第13。油价、基础金属及加元同时承压于全球增长忧虑与贸易不确定性，令EWC持续走弱。尽管EWC仍位于200日均线上方，周期模型预测下一个低谷或在2026年11月前后出现，当前弱势可能延续一段时间后才会迎来持久复苏。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewd":{"legs":{"2011-09-23":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewd:trough:2011-09"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewd:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-25":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewd:trough:2011-11"},"2012-02-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewd:peak:2012-02"},"2012-06-01":{"body":"Mario Draghi's July 2012 'whatever it takes' pledge eased the European sovereign debt crisis and triggered a broad re-rating of European equities. Sweden, with its AAA-rated economy and recovering export demand, outperformed as Riksbank policy remained accommodative. The 69% gain to May 2014 reflected rising Swedish corporate earnings alongside broad euro-area stabilization, with FX a secondary factor.","body_zh":"2012年7月，欧央行行长德拉吉的'不惜一切'承诺缓解了欧洲主权债务危机，引发欧洲股市广泛重估。瑞典凭借AAA评级经济体和出口需求复苏，在宽松的央行环境下表现突出。至2014年5月累计涨幅达69%，主要受益于瑞典企业盈利回升以及欧元区整体企稳，汇率为次要因素。","drivers":["ECB 'whatever it takes' re-rating","Swedish export recovery","Accommodative Riksbank policy","Euro-area stabilization"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行'不惜一切'重新定价","瑞典出口需求复苏","瑞典央行宽松政策","欧元区企稳"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Euro crisis trough to 'whatever it takes' rally","title_zh":"欧债危机底部至'不惜一切'反弹","turn_id":"ewd:trough:2012-06"},"2014-05-21":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewd:peak:2014-05"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"From the February 2016 global growth stabilization, a synchronized expansion ran through January 2018. Sweden's export-heavy economy of industrials, autos and telecoms was a prime beneficiary of accelerating global trade. The Riksbank held its repo rate at a record -0.5% through the period, suppressing the SEK and supporting competitiveness and asset prices, producing a 51.9% gain.","body_zh":"自2016年2月全球增长预期企稳起，一轮持续至2018年1月的全球同步扩张展开。以工业、汽车和电信为主的瑞典出口型经济从全球贸易加速中大幅受益。瑞典央行全程将回购利率维持在-0.5%的历史低位，压制SEK、提升出口竞争力并推升资产价格，最终录得51.9%涨幅。","drivers":["Global synchronized expansion","Riksbank repo rate at record -0.5%","Swedish industrial export outperformance","Rising global trade volumes"],"drivers_zh":["全球同步扩张周期","瑞典央行回购利率处于-0.5%历史低位","瑞典工业出口板块强势","全球贸易量回升"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Synchronized global expansion rally","title_zh":"全球同步扩张驱动上涨","turn_id":"ewd:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewd:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"After the late-2018 global growth scare and Fed pivot, Sweden rebounded with the rest of developed Europe. The Riksbank raised its rate out of negative territory in December 2019 (to zero), signaling confidence in the outlook. The 33.5% gain through February 2020 was a beta-to-global-risk-on move, led by industrial exports and financials.","body_zh":"2018年底全球增长恐慌消退、美联储政策转向后，瑞典随其他发达欧洲市场反弹。瑞典央行于2019年12月将利率上调至零、退出负利率区间，释放出对前景的信心。至2020年2月累计涨33.5%，本质上是全球风险偏好修复的贝塔行情，由工业出口和金融板块领涨。","drivers":["Fed pivot removing global tightening risk","Riksbank exiting negative rates to zero","Beta to global risk-on recovery","Industrial and financial sector leadership"],"drivers_zh":["美联储转向消除全球紧缩风险","瑞典央行退出负利率升至零","全球风险偏好修复贝塔行情","工业与金融板块领涨"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Late-cycle rebound, Riksbank exits negative rates","title_zh":"周期末段反弹，央行退出负利率","turn_id":"ewd:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-12":{"body":"EWD fell 37% in roughly four weeks as COVID-19 triggered a global liquidation of risk assets. The SEK sold off as investors fled to USD, amplifying losses for dollar-based holders. Sweden's lighter restrictions offered no market protection; the collapse was synchronous with global equities.","body_zh":"新冠疫情引发全球风险资产清仓性抛售，EWD在约四周内暴跌37%。投资者涌向美元避险，SEK走弱，放大了美元计价持有者的损失。瑞典相对宽松的管控并未提供市场保护，跌势与全球股市高度同步。","drivers":["Global COVID-19 liquidity panic","USD flight-to-safety pressuring SEK","Broad risk asset deleveraging"],"drivers_zh":["全球新冠疫情流动性恐慌","美元避险需求施压SEK","广泛风险资产去杠杆"],"prev_key":"2020-02","prev_key_chain":["2020-02"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash: global risk-off liquidation","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：全球风险资产抛售","turn_id":"ewd:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The Riksbank's SEK 700 billion QE program plus government stimulus, combined with global central bank action, fueled a powerful recovery. Sweden's lighter restrictions allowed a faster reopening, with GDP contracting only around 3% in 2020 versus far steeper drops across most of the EU. The SEK recovered against the dollar as risk appetite returned, contributing to EWD's 135.7% gain from March 2020 to August 2021.","body_zh":"瑞典央行7000亿克朗量化宽松计划与政府财政刺激，叠加全球央行联合行动，共同推动了强劲复苏。瑞典相对宽松的管控使经济更早重启，2020年GDP仅萎缩约3%，远好于欧盟多数国家更深的跌幅。随着风险偏好回升，SEK对美元回升，助推EWD从2020年3月至2021年8月录得135.7%涨幅。","drivers":["Riksbank SEK 700bn QE program","Swedish economy faster reopening","SEK recovery vs USD","Global fiscal and monetary stimulus"],"drivers_zh":["瑞典央行7000亿克朗量化宽松","瑞典经济更早重启","SEK对美元回升","全球财政与货币政策刺激"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Policy bazooka fuels 136% V-recovery","title_zh":"政策火力全开，V形反弹136%","turn_id":"ewd:trough:2020-03"},"2021-06-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewd:peak:2021-06"},"2022-03-07":{"body":"From March through September 2022, EWD fell 32.1% as Russia's invasion of Ukraine escalated the European energy crisis and the Riksbank began its most aggressive tightening in decades, ultimately raising rates from zero to 4.0% by 2023. Sweden's largely floating-rate mortgage market transmitted hikes directly into household disposable income; listed real estate names fell 50% or more as funding costs soared. The SEK hit a record low near EUR/SEK 11.96 in summer 2022, amplifying the drawdown in USD terms.","body_zh":"2022年3月至9月，EWD下跌32.1%。俄乌战争升级引发欧洲能源危机，瑞典央行随即启动数十年来最激进的加息周期，至2023年将利率从零上调至4.0%。以浮动利率为主的抵押贷款市场将加息效应直接传导至居民可支配收入；上市房地产公司股价腰斩逾50%，融资成本飙升。SEK于2022年夏跌至EUR/SEK约11.96的历史低点，进一步放大了美元计价的回撤幅度。","drivers":["Russia-Ukraine war European energy shock","Riksbank hiking from zero toward 4.0%","Swedish floating-rate mortgage shock","SEK at record low vs EUR in summer 2022"],"drivers_zh":["俄乌战争引发欧洲能源危机","瑞典央行从零加息至4.0%","浮动利率抵押贷款冲击","SEK于2022年夏跌至欧元历史低点"],"prev_key":"2022-03","prev_key_chain":["2022-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Energy and rate shock bear market","title_zh":"能源与利率双冲击熊市","turn_id":"ewd:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewd:peak:2022-03"},"2022-09-26":{"body":"From September 2022, markets began pricing Riksbank peak rates and eventual cuts, lifting Sweden's rate-sensitive sectors from deeply depressed levels. The Riksbank then cut rates through 2025 to reach 1.75%, and the SEK became the best-performing G10 currency in 2025 with a 16.8% gain vs. USD (its strongest year since 2003) — a powerful dual tailwind for dollar-based holders. A stabilizing real-estate market and solid Swedish GDP growth (consensus around 2.5-2.7% for 2026) underpinned the 122.7% gain into the February 2026 peak.","body_zh":"自2022年9月起，市场开始定价瑞典央行政策利率见顶及最终降息预期，带动瑞典利率敏感型板块从极度低估水平反弹。瑞典央行随后在2025年逐步降息至1.75%，SEK由此成为2025年G10表现最强货币（对美元升值16.8%，创2003年以来最强年度涨幅），为美元计价持有者提供了强劲双重顺风。房地产市场企稳以及瑞典稳健的GDP增长（2026年市场预期约2.5%-2.7%）共同支撑EWD录得122.7%涨幅，直至2026年2月再度触顶。","drivers":["Riksbank rate cuts through 2025 to 1.75%","SEK best-performing G10 currency in 2025","Swedish real estate market stabilization","Solid Swedish GDP growth into 2026"],"drivers_zh":["瑞典央行降息至2025年的1.75%","SEK成为2025年G10最强货币","瑞典房地产市场企稳","瑞典GDP增长稳健延续至2026年"],"prev_key":"2022-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate-peak to SEK rebound, 123% bull run","title_zh":"利率见顶至SEK强势反弹，涨幅123%","turn_id":"ewd:trough:2022-09"}},"now":"EWD is currently in a Trough phase, sitting at just 20.7 out of 100 on the cycle position scale, deep in washed-out territory after peaking in February 2026 and pulling back sharply. The ETF has underperformed SPY by 7.3 percentage points over the past 63 trading days, the weakest developed-market relative strength in the cohort (RS rank 12). Sweden's small, export-tilted market is pressured by rotation away from smaller European markets and its residual sensitivity to rate-sensitive real-estate and banking sectors. The SEK, after a 16.8% rally vs. USD in 2025 (the best G10 currency and its strongest year since 2003), now offers limited incremental tailwind as the Riksbank holds at 1.75% with its easing cycle effectively complete.","now_zh":"EWD目前处于周期底部阶段，周期位置仅为20.7（满分100），在2026年2月触顶后明显回落，属于深度超卖区域。过去63个交易日，EWD相对标普500跑输7.3个百分点，是发达市场样本中相对强度最弱的（排名第12）。瑞典这一小型、出口导向的市场承压，源于资金从小型欧洲市场撤离，叠加该国房地产及银行板块对利率的高度敏感性。瑞典克朗（SEK）在2025年对美元升值16.8%（G10最强、为2003年以来最强年度涨幅），但随着瑞典央行将政策利率维持在1.75%、宽松周期基本结束，汇率的边际顺风效应已趋于减弱。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewg":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:trough:2011-10"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-25":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:trough:2011-11"},"2012-03-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:peak:2012-03"},"2012-06-25":{"body":"Mario Draghi's July 2012 'whatever it takes' pledge broke the back of the eurozone sovereign debt crisis, compressing peripheral spreads and reviving risk appetite across European equities. Germany, with its export-oriented industrials and financials, was a prime beneficiary as intra-eurozone demand stabilized and breakup risk faded. The USD-denominated gain of 80.5% through June 2014 also reflected a broadly stable EUR/USD over the period, so local DAX gains translated cleanly into dollar returns. German export orders recovered as the eurozone avoided break-up and global manufacturing picked up.","body_zh":"德拉吉2012年7月的'不惜一切代价'表态打破了欧元区主权债务危机的僵局，欧元区外围国国债利差大幅收窄，欧洲股市风险偏好全面回暖。德国凭借以出口为导向的工业和金融板块成为主要受益者，欧元区内需企稳，系统性解体风险消退。截至2014年6月，EWG美元计价涨幅达80.5%，同期欧元兑美元基本稳定，本地涨幅得以完整转化为美元回报。德国出口订单随着欧元区系统性风险消退和全球制造业复苏而回升。","drivers":["ECB 'whatever it takes' backstop","Eurozone breakup risk priced out","German export recovery","EUR/USD broadly stable"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Draghi saves eurozone, DAX rips","title_zh":"德拉吉救市，DAX大涨","turn_id":"ewg:trough:2012-06"},"2014-06-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:peak:2014-06"},"2014-10-16":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:trough:2014-10"},"2015-04-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:peak:2015-04"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"The ECB's quantitative easing program, launched in March 2015 and expanded through 2016, compressed eurozone yields and pushed capital into equities. Germany's industrial complex benefited from the synchronized global growth cycle of 2017, with manufacturing PMIs across the US, Europe, and Asia expanding simultaneously. The EUR initially weakened under QE, boosting German export competitiveness and providing an FX tailwind to USD returns early in the leg; a EUR recovery in late 2017 partially offset late-period dollar gains. EWG gained 63.2% through January 2018.","body_zh":"欧洲央行于2015年3月启动并在2016年持续扩大的量化宽松计划压低了欧元区收益率，推动资金流入股市。德国工业联合体受益于2017年全球同步增长周期，美国、欧洲和亚洲制造业PMI同步扩张。欧元在QE初期走弱，提升了德国出口竞争力，并为美元回报提供汇率顺风；但2017年下半年欧元反弹，部分抵消了后期美元收益。EWG截至2018年1月上涨63.2%。","drivers":["ECB QE yield compression","Synchronized global manufacturing expansion","German export competitiveness","EUR/USD initially a tailwind then neutral"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"ECB QE + synchronized global expansion","title_zh":"欧洲央行QE叠加全球同步扩张","turn_id":"ewg:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-23":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-02":{"body":"The COVID-19 pandemic triggered a near-40% collapse in EWG in under two months through March 2020, one of the steepest drawdowns in the ETF's history. Germany's industrial, auto, and chemicals sectors were among the hardest hit as supply chains froze and demand collapsed. The EUR also weakened in the acute phase as dollar liquidity was hoarded, compounding losses for USD investors. A swift policy response from the ECB (PEPP) and global fiscal stimulus set the stage for the reversal.","body_zh":"新冠疫情导致EWG在不到两个月内（至2020年3月）暴跌近40%，是该ETF历史上最惨烈的回撤之一。德国工业、汽车和化工板块受到最严重冲击，供应链冻结、需求崩溃。危机急性期欧元也随之走弱，美元流动性被哄抢，放大了美元投资者的损失。欧洲央行（PEPP）和全球财政刺激的快速政策响应为此后反转奠定了基础。","drivers":["Global pandemic demand collapse","Supply chain freeze in autos and industrials","EUR weakness amplified USD losses","ECB PEPP backstop set recovery stage"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID pandemic crash","title_zh":"新冠疫情恐慌性下跌","turn_id":"ewg:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"EWG more than doubled (+107.1%) from the March 2020 trough to June 2021, driven by a powerful reopening trade in Germany's cyclical-heavy index and a significant EUR/USD appreciation that boosted USD returns. The EU Recovery Fund agreed in July 2020 was a historic fiscal step that strengthened the EUR; EUR/USD moved from roughly 1.08 to above 1.22 by early 2021, adding currency tailwind on top of the local DAX rally. German industrial output recovered rapidly as global goods demand surged during lockdowns, particularly in autos, machinery, and chemicals.","body_zh":"EWG从2020年3月低谷至2021年6月累计上涨逾107%，驱动力来自两方面：德国高周期性指数的强劲开放复苏，以及欧元兑美元大幅升值带来的汇率增益。2020年7月达成的欧盟复苏基金协议是历史性财政里程碑，强化了欧元；欧元兑美元从约1.08升至2021年初的1.22上方，在本地DAX涨幅之上叠加了汇率顺风。随着全球封锁期间商品需求激增，德国工业产出迅速回升，尤以汽车、机械和化工领域为甚。","drivers":["EU Recovery Fund supported EUR","EUR/USD rally from 1.08 to 1.22+","Global goods demand surge","Cyclical sector (autos, industrials) reopening premium"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Cyclical V-recovery, EUR surge","title_zh":"周期性V型复苏，欧元强劲上涨","turn_id":"ewg:trough:2020-03"},"2021-06-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:peak:2021-06"},"2022-03-07":{"body":"Russia's February 2022 invasion of Ukraine was an acute shock to Germany specifically: as Europe's most gas-dependent major economy, Germany faced energy rationing risk and soaring industrial input costs. The DAX fell sharply from late February, extending through a broader European bear market driven by the energy-price spike, surging inflation, and ECB rate hikes beginning in July 2022. EUR/USD also fell substantially, breaking below parity in September 2022, amplifying losses in USD terms. EWG lost 31.9% from March to September 2022.","body_zh":"2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰对德国造成了特别严峻的冲击：作为欧洲对天然气依赖最深的主要经济体，德国面临能源配给风险和工业投入成本暴涨。DAX从2月下旬急剧下跌，随着能源价格飙升、通胀高企和欧洲央行自2022年7月起加息，整个欧洲股市进入熊市。欧元兑美元也大幅下跌，于2022年9月跌破平价，进一步放大了美元计价的损失。EWG从2022年3月至9月累计下跌31.9%。","drivers":["Russia-Ukraine energy supply shock","German gas dependency risk premium","ECB rate hike cycle began","EUR/USD parity breach amplified USD losses"],"prev_key":"2022-03","prev_key_chain":["2022-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Ukraine energy shock crash","title_zh":"乌克兰能源冲击引发暴跌","turn_id":"ewg:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewg:peak:2022-03"},"2022-09-27":{"body":"From the September 2022 trough, EWG surged 144.2% through February 2026, one of its strongest extended runs. Three forces propelled the move: first, energy-crisis relief as LNG supplies diversified and gas prices normalized through 2023; second, ECB rate cuts beginning in 2024 as eurozone inflation fell; and third, Germany's landmark fiscal turn — parliament's March 2025 reform of the debt brake, creating a roughly EUR500bn infrastructure fund and exempting higher defense spending, which re-rated industrials and defense names (Rheinmetall rose well over 100% in 2025). A EUR/USD recovery from sub-parity lows back toward 1.18 provided a sustained FX tailwind for USD investors.","body_zh":"从2022年9月低谷至2026年2月，EWG累计上涨144.2%，是其历史上最强劲的持续行情之一。三股力量推动了这轮上涨：第一，能源危机缓和，液化天然气供应多元化，2023年天然气价格回归正常；第二，欧元区通胀回落，欧洲央行于2024年开始降息；第三，德国标志性的财政转向——2025年3月议会改革债务刹车，设立约5000亿欧元基建基金并豁免更高的国防支出，推动工业与国防股重估（莱茵金属2025年累计上涨远超100%）。欧元兑美元从跌破平价的低位回升至约1.18，为美元投资者提供了持续的汇率顺风。","drivers":["European gas crisis relief via LNG diversification","ECB pivot to rate cuts from 2024","Germany debt-brake reform: ~EUR500bn fund + defense (Mar 2025)","EUR/USD recovery from sub-parity toward 1.18"],"prev_key":"2022-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Multi-year recovery: energy relief, ECB cuts, fiscal reboot","title_zh":"多年复苏：能源缓和、欧洲央行降息与财政重启","turn_id":"ewg:trough:2022-09"}},"now":"EWG sits in Trough territory (pos 26.4/100), below its 200-day moving average and lagging SPY by 6.2% over the past quarter, ranking 11th of 24 markets tracked. The February 2026 peak near DAX 25,000 gave way to a sharp pullback driven by US tariffs on European goods (15% baseline framework, with autos and steel exposed) and persistent German industrial weakness after back-to-back GDP contractions in 2023 and 2024. The EUR/USD component has been a modest headwind, with the euro easing to roughly 1.15 after touching early-2026 highs near 1.19. The model projects the cycle trough around September 2026, implying continued digestion before a potential turn.","now_zh":"EWG目前处于周期低谷区间（位置26.4/100），已跌破200日均线，近三个月相对标普500落后6.2%，在24个追踪市场中排名第11。2026年2月DAX触及约25,000点高峰后，受美国关税冲击（欧洲商品15%基准框架，汽车和钢铁尤其承压）以及德国工业持续疲软（2023与2024连续两年GDP收缩）的拖累，市场急剧回落。欧元兑美元也构成温和阻力，欧元从2026年初约1.19的高位回落至约1.15。模型预计本轮低谷约于2026年9月确立，此后或迎来新的周期转折。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewh":{"legs":{"2011-10-04":{"body":"From October 2011, a deeply oversold Hang Seng bounced as fears of a China hard landing faded and the PBOC shifted toward easing with reserve-requirement cuts. The rally sustained through May 2015 as mainland capital-account liberalisation advanced, China's growth held above 7%, and a credit-fuelled property boom underpinned bank earnings. With the HKD pegged to the USD, dollar investors captured the full ~97% local-equity gain with no currency drag.","body_zh":"2011 年 10 月起，受中国经济硬着陆恐慌消散、人民银行转向降准宽松的推动，严重超卖的恒生指数展开反弹。随着资本账户自由化推进、中国增速维持在 7% 以上，以及信贷驱动的房地产繁荣支撑银行盈利，牛市一直延续至 2015 年 5 月。港元与美元挂钩意味着 USD 投资者以零汇率损耗完整捕获约 97% 的本地股票涨幅。","drivers":["PBOC easing: RRR cuts boosted bank lending","China property boom: developer and bank earnings rose","Mainland capital liberalisation lifted HK demand","Low valuation base after the 2011 European crisis selloff"],"drivers_zh":["人民银行宽松：降准提振银行放贷","内地房地产繁荣：开发商及银行盈利上升","内地资本自由化提振港股需求","2011 年欧债危机抛售后的低估值基础"],"prev_key":"2011-10","prev_key_chain":["2011-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-Crisis China Recovery Bull","title_zh":"后危机中国复苏牛市","turn_id":"ewh:trough:2011-10"},"2015-05-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewh:peak:2015-05"},"2016-02-09":{"body":"EWH bottomed in February 2016 near multi-decade-low valuations after the HKD peg came under speculative pressure. A stabilising CNY, a global reflation trade, and the launch of the Shenzhen-Hong Kong Stock Connect (5 December 2016) brought sustained southbound inflows that re-rated HK equities. The ~72% rally into January 2018 coincided with synchronised global growth, a weakening USD, and strong Chinese corporate earnings, all amplifying returns for dollar-based investors.","body_zh":"2016 年 2 月，港元联系汇率遭受投机压力后，恒生指数估值跌至数十年低位，EWH 随之触底。人民币企稳、全球通胀交易盛行，以及深港股票通（2016 年 12 月 5 日开通）带来的持续南向资金流入，推动港股重估。至 2018 年 1 月约 72% 的涨幅与全球经济同步增长、美元走弱及中国企业盈利强劲同步出现，进一步放大了 USD 计价回报。","drivers":["Deep valuation reset near multi-decade lows","Shenzhen-Hong Kong Stock Connect launched December 2016","Synchronised global growth 2016-2018, USD weakening","CNY stabilisation removed the HKD-peg tail-risk premium"],"drivers_zh":["估值深度重置至数十年低位","深港股票通：2016 年 12 月开通","2016-2018 年全球经济同步增长，美元走弱","人民币企稳消除港元联系汇率的尾部风险溢价"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Stock Connect & Reform Re-Rating","title_zh":"股票通与改革驱动重估","turn_id":"ewh:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewh:peak:2018-01"},"2018-10-29":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewh:trough:2018-10"},"2019-04-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewh:peak:2019-04"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The March 2020 pandemic trough gave way to a ~59% recovery as global liquidity flooded markets and the Hang Seng Tech complex, led by Alibaba, Tencent, and Meituan, ran to record highs by early 2021. With the HKD pegged, EWH's USD return closely tracked the local-equity surge. The rally peaked in May 2021 as the first signs of Beijing's regulatory pivot against internet platforms began to register.","body_zh":"2020 年 3 月疫情低点后，全球流动性泛滥，由阿里巴巴、腾讯及美团引领的恒生科技板块于 2021 年初创历史新高，EWH 随之展开约 59% 的反弹。港元联系汇率稳定了汇率端，EWH 的 USD 回报几乎完整映射本地股票涨幅。随着北京针对互联网平台监管转向的早期信号显现，行情于 2021 年 5 月见顶。","drivers":["Global QE flood drove EM inflows","China tech leadership: Alibaba, Tencent, Meituan","Containment kept HK's 2020 economic hit relatively contained","HKD peg passed the full local-equity gain to USD investors"],"drivers_zh":["全球量化宽松泛滥推动新兴市场资金流入","中国科技主导：阿里巴巴、腾讯、美团","防疫使香港 2020 年经济冲击相对受控","港元联系汇率将本地股票涨幅完整传导至 USD 投资者"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Rebound & Tech Euphoria","title_zh":"新冠疫情反弹与科技热潮","turn_id":"ewh:trough:2020-03"},"2021-05-28":{"body":"Beijing's sweeping crackdown on technology, education, and property from mid-2021 hammered Hang Seng Tech constituents, while the Evergrande crisis triggered a wave of developer defaults that crushed the financial stocks anchoring the index. The ~40% decline from May 2021 to October 2022 ranks among EWH's sharpest sustained drawdowns, compounded by rising US rates that tightened HK conditions via the peg and by prolonged mainland COVID lockdowns.","body_zh":"2021 年中起，北京针对科技、教育及房地产的全面整治重创恒生科技成份股，同时恒大危机引发开发商违约潮，重创指数中权重最高的金融股。从 2021 年 5 月至 2022 年 10 月约 40% 的跌幅是 EWH 历史上最惨烈的持续性回撤之一，美国加息通过联系汇率收紧香港货币条件，以及内地延续的封控，进一步加剧了跌势。","drivers":["Beijing tech & education crackdown hit valuations","Evergrande and developer-default wave crushed property stocks","Fed hike cycle: HKD peg transmitted tightening directly to HK","COVID Zero lockdowns hit mainland demand and HK tourism"],"drivers_zh":["北京科技与教育整治打压估值","恒大及开发商违约潮重创地产股","美联储加息周期：联系汇率直接将收紧传导至香港","清零封控冲击内地需求与香港旅游业"],"prev_key":"2021-05","prev_key_chain":["2021-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Regulatory Assault & Property Collapse","title_zh":"监管整治与房地产崩溃","turn_id":"ewh:peak:2021-05"},"2022-10-31":{"body":"October 2022 marked a double trough: the global EM selloff bottom and early signals that China would exit zero-COVID. The Hang Seng surged ~42% in roughly three months as markets priced a reopening dividend. The rally faded by January 2023 as the consumer recovery proved sluggish, property stress persisted, and US-China geopolitical tensions stayed elevated, leaving the fundamental picture unresolved.","body_zh":"2022 年 10 月出现双重触底：全球新兴市场抛售见底，加之中国清零政策即将结束的早期信号。恒生指数在约三个月内急升约 42%，市场提前定价重开红利。然而，随着消费复苏不如预期、房地产压力延续以及美中地缘政治紧张持续，行情至 2023 年 1 月逐步退潮，基本面问题悬而未决。","drivers":["China zero-COVID exit signals from late 2022","Extreme undervaluation near decade lows","Global EM relief rally as Fed hike expectations moderated","Short-covering of heavy net-short positioning"],"drivers_zh":["2022 年底中国清零退出信号","接近十年低点的极端低估值","美联储加息预期放缓带动新兴市场救济反弹","机构净空头头寸的空头回补"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Reopening Hope Spike","title_zh":"重开经济的短暂反弹","turn_id":"ewh:trough:2022-10"},"2023-01-23":{"body":"The reopening trade unwound from January 2023 into April 2024 as China's consumer recovery proved anaemic, deflation risks mounted, and the property crisis deepened with successive developer failures. Hong Kong's own economy faced high US-linked rates, depressed property transactions, and an exodus of international capital, leaving EWH's USD return weighed by deteriorating equity and HK real-estate sentiment through this ~32% decline.","body_zh":"重开经济交易从 2023 年 1 月退潮至 2024 年 4 月：中国消费复苏疲弱，通缩风险上升，房地产危机随开发商接连违约而加深。香港自身经济亦面临高利率环境、楼市成交低迷及国际资本外流，EWH 的 USD 回报在这段约 32% 的跌势中因股票与房地产情绪双重恶化而受损。","drivers":["China recovery disappointment: weak consumer spending","Property crisis deepening through 2023","High US rates kept HK borrowing costs elevated via the peg","Capital outflows: international funds cut HK allocations"],"drivers_zh":["中国复苏不及预期：消费疲弱","房地产危机贯穿 2023 年加深","美国高利率经联系汇率令香港借贷成本居高","资本外流：国际基金削减香港配置"],"prev_key":"2023-01","prev_key_chain":["2023-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Disappointing Recovery Drags Market Lower","title_zh":"复苏不及预期拖累市场走低","turn_id":"ewh:peak:2023-01"},"2024-04-17":{"body":"The Hang Seng turned sharply higher from April 2024 as Beijing signalled support, then in late September 2024 the PBOC announced a sweeping package of rate cuts, RRR reductions, and property-sector measures, sparking a rapid surge in the two weeks after the September 24 announcement. The ~42% rally from April to October 2024 was compressed into a short window as investors priced an end to China's multi-year deleveraging cycle.","body_zh":"从 2024 年 4 月起，随着北京释放支持信号，恒生指数急速上涨；2024 年 9 月底人行宣布包括降息、降准及房地产支持在内的一揽子政策，公告后两周内急涨。从 2024 年 4 月至 10 月约 42% 的涨幅被压缩在极短窗口内，市场定价中国多年去杠杆周期即将终结。","drivers":["PBOC September 2024 package: rate cuts, RRR cuts, property support","Fiscal stimulus signals: government bond issuance","Extreme short positioning unwound rapidly","Global rate-cut cycle eased HKD rate pressure"],"drivers_zh":["人行 2024 年 9 月一揽子政策：降息、降准及房地产支持","财政刺激信号：政府债券发行","极端空头头寸快速平仓","全球降息周期缓解港元利率压力"],"prev_key":"2024-04","prev_key_chain":["2024-04"],"status":"exact","title":"China Stimulus Surge & September PBOC Pivot","title_zh":"中国财政刺激与人行 9 月政策转向","turn_id":"ewh:trough:2024-04"},"2024-10-07":{"body":"The October 2024 peak came as policymakers failed to deliver the multi-trillion-yuan stimulus scale the market had priced, triggering a ~24% drawdown into April 2025. Rising US-China trade tensions under escalating US tariffs (US effective rates on Chinese goods reached roughly 145% by April 2025) compounded the pressure, while HK's weak property and consumption data continued to weigh.","body_zh":"2024 年 10 月见顶，因决策层未能兑现市场预期的数万亿人民币刺激规模，触发至 2025 年 4 月约 24% 的回调。美国加征关税导致美中贸易紧张升级（至 2025 年 4 月美国对中国商品实际关税率约 145%），加之香港楼市与消费数据持续疲弱，进一步压制市场。","drivers":["Stimulus underwhelm: October 2024 disappointment","US tariff escalation: ~145% effective rate by April 2025","HK property weakness: depressed transaction volumes","USD strength tightened peg-linked HK conditions"],"drivers_zh":["刺激落差：2024 年 10 月令市场失望","美国关税升级：至 2025 年 4 月实际关税约 145%","香港楼市疲弱：成交低迷","美元强势经联系汇率收紧香港金融条件"],"prev_key":"2024-10","prev_key_chain":["2024-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Stimulus Disappointment Correction","title_zh":"刺激落差引发调整","turn_id":"ewh:peak:2024-10"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"The April 2025 trough coincided with the US-China tariff truce (announced May 12, 2025, cutting reciprocal tariffs from 125% to 10% for 90 days, then extended). EWH rallied ~70% from that low into May 2026 as trade uncertainty eased, the PBOC stayed accommodative, and southbound flows into HK stocks resumed. The move reversed after the May 2026 peak as trade-policy uncertainty and Hong Kong's structural headwinds reasserted; the ETF now trades near 15-year cycle lows on a relative basis versus SPY.","body_zh":"2025 年 4 月低点与美中关税停战（2025 年 5 月 12 日宣布，互征关税由 125% 降至 10%，为期 90 天并随后延续）时间吻合。EWH 从该低点至 2026 年 5 月高点反弹约 70%，贸易不确定性缓解、人行维持宽松、南向资金重新流入港股共同推动。2026 年 5 月见顶后行情逆转，贸易政策不确定性与香港结构性逆风重新主导，ETF 相对标普 500 的强弱比已跌至 15 年周期相对低位。","drivers":["US-China tariff truce May 2025: reciprocal tariffs cut to 10%","Truce extended (Aug & Oct 2025) into November 2026","PBOC accommodative stance held rates and RRR low","Southbound Stock Connect inflows resumed on trade optimism"],"drivers_zh":["2025 年 5 月美中关税停战：互征关税降至 10%","停战于 2025 年 8 月及 10 月延续至 2026 年 11 月","人行维持宽松，利率与存款准备金率保持低位","南向股票通资金在贸易乐观情绪下重新流入"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff Truce Rally & 2026 Reversal","title_zh":"关税停战反弹与 2026 年逆转","turn_id":"ewh:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"EWH sits at a cycle position of 0.3 out of 100, effectively the most washed-out reading in its 15-year window, having peaked in May 2026 and rolled over, with the ETF now below its 200-day moving average. Its 63-day relative strength of -18.1 versus SPY ranks 21st of 24 single countries, among the weakest in the universe, reflecting a flagging Hang Seng and a HKD-peg dynamic that offers USD investors no currency cushion. The post-tariff-truce rally from the April 2025 trough ran +70% into May 2026, but momentum has since reversed as US-China trade uncertainty resurfaces and Hong Kong's economy remains pressured by a multi-year property downturn and high US-linked interest rates transmitted through the peg. The cycle model projects a next trough around October 2026.","now_zh":"EWH 的周期位置仅为 0.3（满分 100），是 15 年窗口内几乎最低的超卖读数——ETF 于 2026 年 5 月见顶后回落，当前已跌破 200 日均线。相对标普 500 的 63 日强弱值为 -18.1，在 24 个单一国家中排名第 21，处于全市场最弱之列，反映出恒生指数走弱与港元与美元联系汇率的双重拖累，USD 投资者缺乏汇率缓冲。从 2025 年 4 月低点至 2026 年 5 月高点的涨幅达 70%，但随着美中贸易不确定性重燃、香港楼市多年低迷及通过联系汇率传导的高利率环境持续，行情已开始逆转。周期模型预计下一个低点约在 2026 年 10 月前后。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewi":{"legs":{"2011-09-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2011-09"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:peak:2011-10"},"2012-01-09":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2012-01"},"2012-03-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:peak:2012-03"},"2012-07-24":{"body":"In late July 2012 Mario Draghi's pledge to do \"whatever it takes\" to preserve the euro collapsed Italian sovereign spreads and turned EWI off its lows. The market had sold off sharply into the speech (a brief ~19% washout), then immediately reversed into a powerful short-covering rally of roughly 58% into early 2013 as flight-from-Italy fears unwound. This trough-and-bounce marks the precise turning point of the European debt crisis for Italian assets.","body_zh":"2012年7月底，马里奥·德拉吉承诺「不惜一切代价」捍卫欧元，意大利主权利差骤降，EWI由低点反转。市场在讲话前已大幅下跌（约19%的短促急挫），随后随着对意大利的恐慌消退，立即反转为强劲的空头回补反弹，至2013年初累计上涨约58%。这一筑底反弹标志着欧债危机对意大利资产的精确转折点。","drivers":["Draghi's pledge collapsed the BTP-Bund spread and removed existential euro risk","Short-covering in heavily-sold Italian banks drove outsized initial gains","Flight-from-periphery flows reversed as contagion fears faded"],"drivers_zh":["德拉吉承诺令BTP-德债利差骤降，消除欧元存亡风险","遭重创的意大利银行股空头回补推动初期涨幅放大","蔓延恐慌消退，外围国家资金外流逆转"],"prev_key":"2012-07","prev_key_chain":["2012-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Draghi 'Whatever It Takes' Bottom","title_zh":"德拉吉「不惜一切」筑底","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2012-07"},"2013-01-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:peak:2013-01"},"2013-04-03":{"body":"From April 2013 into mid-2014 EWI gained about 63% as the ECB eased policy and introduced forward guidance, pulling BTP yields lower and compressing sovereign risk premiums across the periphery. Italian bank stocks, deeply discounted on credit-quality concerns, re-rated meaningfully. EUR/USD traded broadly in the 1.30-1.40 range over this stretch, a roughly neutral currency backdrop for the USD-denominated ETF.","body_zh":"2013年4月至2014年中，EWI上涨约63%。欧央行宽松并引入前瞻指引，推动BTP收益率下行，外围国家主权风险溢价整体收窄。因信贷质量担忧被大幅折价的意大利银行股显著重新定价。期间欧元/美元大体在1.30-1.40区间，对以美元计价的ETF而言汇率背景基本中性。","drivers":["ECB easing and forward guidance anchored BTP yields lower","Peripheral re-rating as existential euro risk receded","Italian bank discount narrowed on a stabilising macro backdrop","EUR broadly range-bound — no significant currency drag"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行宽松与前瞻指引锚定BTP收益率下行","欧元存亡风险消退，外围国家整体重新定价","宏观企稳令意大利银行折价收窄","欧元大体区间震荡，无明显汇率拖累"],"prev_key":"2013-04","prev_key_chain":["2013-04"],"status":"exact","title":"ECB Easing & Periphery Re-Rating","title_zh":"欧央行宽松与外围估值重定价","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2013-04"},"2014-06-09":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:peak:2014-06"},"2015-01-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2015-01"},"2015-06-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:peak:2015-06"},"2016-02-11":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2016-02"},"2016-04-29":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:peak:2016-04"},"2016-06-27":{"body":"After a mid-2016 low driven by the Brexit shock and Italian banking stress, EWI staged a roughly 77% rally into January 2018. ECB asset purchases compressed BTP spreads while globally synchronized growth accelerated through 2017. A recovering EUR/USD over 2017 added a USD tailwind on top of the local equity gains for the USD-denominated ETF.","body_zh":"2016年中受英国脱欧冲击与意大利银行业压力打压触底后，EWI随后反弹约77%至2018年1月。欧央行购债压缩BTP利差，同期2017年全球同步复苏加速。2017年欧元/美元回升，在本地股票涨幅之上为以美元计价的ETF提供了汇率顺风。","drivers":["ECB QE compressed BTP spreads","Globally synchronized growth in 2017 boosted cyclical, financials-heavy markets","A recovering EUR over 2017 added a USD-return tailwind","Italian banking-sector stress stabilised after state interventions"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行QE压缩BTP利差","2017年全球同步复苏提振周期性、金融股占比高的市场","2017年欧元回升为美元回报提供顺风","国家干预后意大利银行业压力趋于稳定"],"prev_key":"2016-06","prev_key_chain":["2016-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-Brexit & ECB-QE Rally","title_zh":"英国脱欧后与欧央行QE反弹","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2016-06"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The December 2018 trough followed Italy's coalition budget standoff with the EU Commission, which had pushed BTP-Bund spreads sharply wider. Once the government softened its budget targets, spreads compressed and EWI climbed about 36% into February 2020. EUR/USD stayed range-bound (roughly 1.10-1.15), keeping the currency component close to neutral.","body_zh":"2018年12月低点源于意大利联合政府与欧盟委员会的预算对峙，曾令BTP-德债利差大幅走阔。政府软化预算目标后，利差收窄，EWI随之上涨约36%至2020年2月。欧元/美元维持在约1.10-1.15区间，汇率因素接近中性。","drivers":["Resolution of the Italy-EU budget standoff compressed BTP spreads","Systemic sovereign risk receded as targets were softened","An improving global-trade backdrop into early 2020 supported risk appetite","EUR/USD range-bound — minimal FX amplification"],"drivers_zh":["意大利与欧盟预算对峙化解，BTP利差收窄","预算目标软化，系统性主权风险消退","2020年初全球贸易环境改善支撑风险偏好","欧元/美元区间震荡，汇率放大效应有限"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Populist Budget Discount Fades","title_zh":"民粹预算折价消退","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"Italy was the first major Western country hit hard by COVID-19, with northern regions locked down by late February 2020. EWI fell about 41% in a matter of weeks — among the steepest drops in European markets — reflecting the local epidemic severity and a global risk-off that re-widened sovereign spreads, with early dollar strength compounding the USD-denominated loss.","body_zh":"意大利是新冠疫情首个重创的西方大国，北部地区于2020年2月底进入封锁。EWI在数周内暴跌约41%，跌幅居欧洲主要市场前列，既反映本地疫情的严峻程度，也叠加了全球避险令主权利差重新走阔；初期美元走强进一步放大以美元计价的损失。","drivers":["Italy was the first Western COVID epicenter — economy locked down Feb-Mar 2020","Global risk-off re-widened the BTP-Bund spread","Early dollar strength amplified the USD-denominated drawdown","Financials and energy — EWI's core sectors — led losses"],"drivers_zh":["意大利成西方新冠首个震中，经济于2020年2-3月封锁","全球避险令BTP-德债利差重新走阔","初期美元走强放大以美元计价跌幅","金融与能源——EWI核心权重板块——领跌"],"prev_key":"2020-02","prev_key_chain":["2020-02"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Shock — Italy Epicenter","title_zh":"新冠冲击——意大利成震中","turn_id":"ewi:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-16":{"body":"From the March 2020 trough EWI surged about 96% over roughly 20 months into November 2021. The ECB's pandemic purchase programme (PEPP) capped BTP spreads, and the EU recovery fund (agreed July 2020) structurally de-risked Italian sovereign debt. Mario Draghi's appointment as prime minister in February 2021 added a credibility premium, while a rallying EUR/USD reinforced the USD-denominated gains.","body_zh":"自2020年3月低点，EWI在约20个月内上涨约96%至2021年11月。欧央行疫情紧急购债计划（PEPP）为BTP利差封顶，2020年7月达成的欧盟复苏基金从结构上降低了意大利主权债务风险。2021年2月德拉吉出任总理增添了公信力溢价，同期欧元/美元走强强化了以美元计价的涨幅。","drivers":["ECB PEPP capped BTP spreads — existential risk removed","EU recovery fund gave Italy a large grant/loan envelope","Draghi PM appointment added an instant credibility premium","A rallying EUR/USD added a USD-return tailwind","Global reflation favoured cyclical, financials-heavy markets"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行PEPP封顶BTP利差，系统性风险消除","欧盟复苏基金为意大利提供大额补贴与贷款额度","德拉吉出任总理，即时增添公信力溢价","欧元/美元走强为美元回报提供顺风","全球再通胀交易青睐周期性、金融股占比高的市场"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"PEPP, NGEU & Draghi Premium","title_zh":"PEPP、NGEU与德拉吉溢价","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2020-03"},"2021-06-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewi:peak:2021-06"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"From October 2022 EWI embarked on a 227.9% rally extending to June 2026 — the dominant feature of the 15-year window. ECB rate hikes hurt bonds but materially widened Italian bank net interest margins, driving a structural re-rating of the heavily-weighted financials. EU recovery-fund disbursements underpinned sovereign credibility, and as the ECB pivoted to cutting rates BTP spreads compressed further. A recovery in EUR/USD off its 2022 parity lows added a USD tailwind on top of the strong local-equity performance. Note: portions of this leg run beyond the reliable-knowledge horizon (end-2025), so the most recent drivers are described in general terms.","body_zh":"2022年10月起，EWI展开幅度高达227.9%的上行走势至2026年6月，是15年数据窗口中最突出的行情。欧央行加息打压债券，但大幅拓宽了意大利银行净息差，推动权重最大的金融股结构性重新定价。欧盟复苏基金拨款巩固了主权公信力，随着欧央行转入降息，BTP利差进一步压缩。欧元/美元自2022年平价低点回升，在强劲的本地股市涨幅之上提供了美元顺风。注：本走势部分时段超出可靠认知范围（2025年底之后），故近期驱动因素仅作概括描述。","drivers":["ECB rate hikes widened Italian bank net interest margins — structural re-rating of financials","EU recovery-fund disbursements anchored BTP spread compression","ECB pivot to rate cuts drove a further spread-compression leg","A recovery in EUR/USD off parity added a cumulative USD tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行加息扩大意大利银行净息差，金融股结构性重新定价","欧盟复苏基金拨款锚定BTP利差收窄","欧央行转入降息，利差进一步压缩","欧元/美元自平价回升，累计贡献美元顺风"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Peak-Rate Re-Rating; 228% Super-Cycle","title_zh":"利率见顶重新定价；228%超级上行周期","turn_id":"ewi:trough:2022-10"}},"now":"EWI sits in Expansion at a mid-cycle position of 56/100, having traced the longest and most powerful up-leg in the 15-year dataset — a 228% rally from the October 2022 trough to the current peak in June 2026. Relative strength vs SPY is essentially flat over the trailing quarter (+0.6%), a notable outcome for a peripheral European market that implies the local re-rating has broadly kept pace with US equities rather than lagging. The ETF remains above its 200-day moving average, but the model projects the next turn to be a trough around November 2026, consistent with a maturing leg this far above the prior base.","now_zh":"EWI目前处于扩张阶段，周期位置56/100，自2022年10月低点至2026年6月已累计上涨228%，是本15年数据集中最长、最强劲的上行走势。过去一个季度相对标普500的超额收益基本为零（+0.6%），对意大利这样的欧洲外围市场而言较为难得，说明其本地重新定价大体跟上了美股而非落后。ETF仍在200日均线以上，但模型预计下一个拐点为约2026年11月的阶段性低点，与这段已远高于此前基底的上行走势趋于成熟的判断一致。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewj":{"legs":{"2011-11-23":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewj:trough:2011-11"},"2012-04-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewj:peak:2012-04"},"2012-06-01":{"body":"Shinzo Abe's December 2012 election win and the BOJ's April 2013 quantitative and qualitative easing programme triggered a sustained yen decline, with USD/JPY moving from roughly 78 toward 125 by mid-2015. Japanese exporters surged as overseas earnings translated into inflated yen profits. USD-denominated EWJ gained about 61% over this leg, roughly half of which was pure currency translation as the yen fell around 36% against the dollar. The rally peaked in early 2015 as the yen stabilised and stretched valuations invited profit-taking.","body_zh":"2012年12月安倍晋三赢得大选，日本银行于2013年4月推出量化质化宽松，触发日元持续贬值，美元兑日元从约78升至2015年中的约125。日本出口商海外收益折算成日元后大幅膨胀，股价飙升。EWJ该阶段以美元计上涨约61%，其中约一半来自纯货币折算收益（日元贬值约36%）。随着日元趋稳、估值偏高引发获利了结，行情于2015年初见顶。","drivers":["BOJ QQE: massive asset-purchase programme","Yen depreciation (USD/JPY: ~78 to ~125)","Exporter earnings boom: autos and electronics","Global risk-on: post-GFC reflation tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["日银QQE：大规模资产购买计划","日元贬值（美元兑日元约78至约125）","出口商盈利激增：汽车与电子","全球风险偏好：金融危机后再通胀顺风"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Abenomics launch ignites yen-fuelled rally","title_zh":"安倍经济学启动，日元贬值点燃行情","turn_id":"ewj:trough:2012-06"},"2015-04-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewj:peak:2015-04"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"After the yen spiked in early 2016 on global risk-off and pushed EWJ lower, a recovery in global growth expectations through early 2018 lifted Japan alongside other risk assets. The yen stabilised broadly in the 110-115 range, a neutral currency backdrop that let the Nikkei's earnings recovery drive USD returns. Trump's late-2016 election added a reflation impulse for global cyclicals, including Japanese industrials and financials. EWJ gained about 62% over this leg, broadly in line with local-currency performance.","body_zh":"2016年初全球避险情绪驱动日元急升，EWJ一度承压；此后随全球增长预期修复，至2018年初日本随其他风险资产同步走高。日元在110-115区间大致企稳，货币背景趋于中性，日经的盈利复苏成为美元回报的主要来源。特朗普2016年底当选带来的再通胀预期提振了全球周期股，包括日本工业与金融板块。EWJ该阶段以美元计上涨约62%，与本地表现大致吻合。","drivers":["Global synchronised growth into 2018","Yen stabilisation in the 110-115 range","Trump reflation: lift to global cyclicals","Japanese corporate earnings recovery"],"drivers_zh":["全球同步增长延续至2018年","日元在110-115区间企稳","特朗普再通胀：提振全球周期股","日本企业盈利复苏"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Global reflation, stable yen supports exporters","title_zh":"全球再通胀，日元企稳支撑出口商","turn_id":"ewj:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewj:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Following the Q4 2018 global equity selloff on US-China trade-war fears and Fed tightening, Japan recovered into late 2019 on easing trade tensions. The BOJ held policy steady under yield-curve control, pegging long yields near zero. EWJ gained about 25% over roughly twelve months — a relatively muted move reflecting limited yen depreciation. The leg ended in late 2019 as the COVID shock began to surface.","body_zh":"2018年第四季度美中贸易战担忧与美联储紧缩引发全球股市大跌，此后日本随贸易摩擦缓和反弹至2019年底。日本银行在收益率曲线控制框架下维持宽松，长端收益率锚定近零。EWJ约12个月内以美元计上涨约25%，幅度相对温和，反映日元贬值有限。随着新冠冲击在2019年底浮现，该阶段行情终止。","drivers":["US-China trade-truce optimism","BOJ YCC: long yields pegged near 0%","Modest yen weakness supporting exporters","Global late-cycle equity recovery"],"drivers_zh":["美中贸易休战乐观情绪","日银YCC：长端收益率锚定近零","日元温和走弱支撑出口商","全球晚周期股市复苏"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Late-cycle bounce on trade truce optimism","title_zh":"贸易休战乐观推动晚周期反弹","turn_id":"ewj:trough:2018-12"},"2019-12-13":{"body":"The COVID-19 pandemic drove a sharp global risk-off from late 2019 through March 2020, and EWJ fell about 28% in USD terms over this short leg. Initial yen strength offered only a partial dollar cushion as fears of global demand destruction overwhelmed Japan's export-heavy index. The decline lasted only about three months before coordinated global stimulus reversed the selloff.","body_zh":"新冠肺炎疫情从2019年底至2020年3月引发全球急速避险抛售，EWJ该阶段以美元计下跌约28%。日元初期升值仅提供有限的美元缓冲，全球需求崩塌的恐慌压垮了日本以出口为主的指数。该跌势仅历时约三个月，全球协调刺激政策随即扭转。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic demand shock","Global risk-off: broad equity selloff","Yen safe-haven bid (partial USD offset)","Export-demand collapse fears"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情需求冲击","全球避险：股市普跌","日元避险买盘（部分美元对冲）","出口需求崩塌担忧"],"prev_key":"2019-12","prev_key_chain":["2019-12"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash: global risk-off hits exporters","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：全球避险冲击出口商","turn_id":"ewj:peak:2019-12"},"2020-03-16":{"body":"Massive global fiscal and monetary stimulus, plus Japan's own emergency spending, lifted the Nikkei toward multi-decade highs by late 2021. The BOJ maintained YCC and near-zero rates throughout, keeping the yen weak enough to support exporter earnings without sparking a currency crisis. EWJ gained about 75% from the March 2020 low through September 2021, tracking the global risk-on regime. With USD/JPY broadly in a 103-110 range for most of the period, local and USD returns were closely aligned.","body_zh":"全球大规模财政与货币刺激叠加日本自身紧急支出，推动日经225于2021年底升至数十年高位。日本银行全程维持收益率曲线控制与近零利率，日元保持温和弱势支撑出口商盈利，同时未触发货币危机。EWJ自2020年3月低点至2021年9月以美元计上涨约75%，紧随全球风险偏好上行。该阶段美元兑日元大致在103-110区间，本地与美元回报高度一致。","drivers":["Global fiscal and monetary stimulus","BOJ YCC: near-zero long yields","Nikkei reaching multi-decade highs","Yen broadly stable: limited FX drag"],"drivers_zh":["全球财政与货币刺激","日银YCC：长端收益率近零","日经升至数十年高位","日元大致平稳：汇率拖累有限"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-COVID reflation: global stimulus lifts cyclicals","title_zh":"新冠后再通胀：全球刺激推升周期股","turn_id":"ewj:trough:2020-03"},"2021-09-15":{"body":"From September 2021 through October 2022 the BOJ refused to follow global central banks into tightening, holding YCC while the Fed hiked aggressively. The policy divergence drove USD/JPY from around 110 toward 150, a level not seen since the early 1990s. With the local Nikkei roughly flat, the yen's collapse meant EWJ fell about 33% in USD terms. This leg illustrates EWJ's central asymmetry: currency drag in a hiking cycle can overwhelm even a stable local equity market.","body_zh":"2021年9月至2022年10月，日本银行拒绝跟随全球央行收紧，坚持收益率曲线控制，而美联储大幅加息。这一政策背离推动美元兑日元从约110升至约150，为1990年代初以来最高水平。日经以日元计大致持平，但日元崩跌导致EWJ以美元计下跌约33%。该阶段清晰揭示EWJ的核心不对称性：加息周期中的货币拖累足以抵消稳定的本地股市。","drivers":["Fed-BOJ policy divergence: Fed hiking, BOJ holding YCC","USD/JPY from ~110 to ~150: multi-decade yen low","Capital outflows from Japan seeking yield","USD drag despite flat local Nikkei"],"drivers_zh":["美联储与日银政策背离：美联储加息，日银坚守YCC","美元兑日元约110至约150：数十年日元低位","资本流出日本追逐收益","本地日经持平但美元回报受拖累"],"prev_key":"2021-09","prev_key_chain":["2021-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Yen collapse erodes USD returns despite flat Nikkei","title_zh":"日元崩跌侵蚀美元回报，日经持平难掩","turn_id":"ewj:peak:2021-09"},"2022-10-20":{"body":"From October 2022 through September 2024 Japan underwent a structural re-rating. The BOJ widened its YCC band from December 2022 and effectively ended yield-curve control and negative rates by March 2024, lifting bond yields and firming the yen off its extremes. TSE-mandated corporate-governance reforms pushed companies toward buybacks and higher returns on equity, drawing record foreign inflows, while Warren Buffett's well-publicised stakes in Japanese trading houses from 2023 amplified global attention. EWJ gained about 55% in USD terms over this two-year leg.","body_zh":"2022年10月至2024年9月，日本经历结构性重估。日本银行自2022年12月起扩大收益率曲线控制区间，并于2024年3月实质上结束YCC与负利率，债券收益率上升，日元从极端低位回稳。东京证券交易所强制推行的公司治理改革推动企业回购、提升股本回报率，吸引创纪录的外资流入；巴菲特自2023年高调增持日本五大商社，进一步放大全球关注。EWJ该阶段以美元计上涨约55%。","drivers":["BOJ YCC widening then exit (Dec 2022-Mar 2024)","TSE corporate-governance reform: buybacks, ROE focus","Warren Buffett Japan trading-house stakes","Yen firming off ~150 extremes","Record foreign inflows into Japanese equities"],"drivers_zh":["日银YCC扩区间至退出（2022年12月-2024年3月）","东证公司治理改革：回购、聚焦ROE","巴菲特增持日本商社","日元从约150极端低位回稳","外资创纪录流入日本股市"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"YCC exit, corporate reform, Buffett spotlight","title_zh":"YCC退出、公司治理改革与巴菲特效应","turn_id":"ewj:trough:2022-10"},"2024-09-26":{"body":"The BOJ's July 2024 hike to 0.25% had already triggered a violent carry-trade unwind, including the Nikkei's worst single session since 1987 (down about 12% on 5 August 2024). The lingering yen-strength and risk-reduction backdrop weighed on EWJ from September 2024 into April 2025, with the ETF falling roughly 15% in USD terms as a firmer yen and softer local equities compressed returns from both sides. The episode underscored how deeply embedded yen-funded leveraged positions had become in global markets.","body_zh":"日本银行2024年7月加息至0.25%已触发剧烈的套息交易平仓，包括日经1987年以来最大单日跌幅（2024年8月5日约下跌12%）。日元走强与风险削减的余波从2024年9月延续至2025年4月，期间EWJ以美元计约下跌15%，日元走强与本地股市走弱从两端压缩回报。这一事件凸显出全球市场中日元融资杠杆头寸之深。","drivers":["Aftermath of BOJ July 2024 hike to 0.25%","Yen carry-trade unwind and risk reduction","Stronger yen compressing USD returns","Softer local equities post-crash"],"drivers_zh":["日银2024年7月加息至0.25%的余波","日元套息交易平仓与风险削减","日元走强压缩美元回报","崩盘后本地股市走弱"],"prev_key":"2024-09","prev_key_chain":["2024-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Carry-unwind aftermath: yen strength caps USD returns","title_zh":"套息平仓余波：日元走强压制美元回报","turn_id":"ewj:peak:2024-09"},"2025-04-07":{"body":"From the April 2025 trough, EWJ has gained roughly 66% through June 2026, among the stronger developed-market runs in this window. The BOJ continued normalising, raising the policy rate to 0.75% in December 2025 in a well-telegraphed move that avoided another carry-trade crisis. Japanese bank stocks surged as positive net interest margins finally materialised after decades of near-zero rates. The July 2025 US-Japan trade framework cut the threatened auto tariff from 25% to 15%, easing pressure on the dominant exporter complex. Yen appreciation as Fed cuts narrowed the rate differential added a USD tailwind for EWJ holders.","body_zh":"自2025年4月低点至2026年6月，EWJ以美元计上涨约66%，是本阶段发达市场中较强劲的行情之一。日本银行持续正常化，于2025年12月以充分预告的方式将政策利率升至0.75%，避免了新一轮套息危机。随着数十年近零利率终结，日本银行股净息差转正，股价大涨。2025年7月美日贸易框架将拟议汽车关税从25%降至15%，缓解了主导出口板块的压力。美联储降息缩窄利差推动日元升值，为EWJ持有者提供额外的美元顺风。","drivers":["BOJ normalisation to 0.75% (Dec 2025)","Bank stocks surge on positive net interest margins","US-Japan trade framework: auto tariff cut 25% to 15% (Jul 2025)","Yen appreciation as Fed cuts narrow the rate differential","Continued foreign inflows on governance-reform momentum"],"drivers_zh":["日银正常化至0.75%（2025年12月）","银行股因净息差转正而大涨","美日贸易框架：汽车关税从25%降至15%（2025年7月）","美联储降息缩窄利差推动日元升值","公司治理改革动能延续，外资持续流入"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Normalisation recovery: banks lead, yen tailwind builds","title_zh":"正常化修复：银行股领涨，日元顺风渐强","turn_id":"ewj:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"EWJ (Japan) is in an Expansion phase at cycle position 55 out of 100 — mid-range, neither washed-out nor stretched, and still above its 200-day moving average. The current leg up from the April 2025 trough has gained roughly 66%, one of the stronger developed-market runs in this window. Relative strength versus SPY over the past 63 days is modestly negative at -1.5%, ranking Japan 6th of 24 markets (upper-middle of the pack). The dominant near-term driver is a gradually firming yen — the BOJ raised its policy rate to 0.75% in December 2025 while Fed cuts narrow the US-Japan rate differential — set against the bank-led domestic re-rating; because EWJ is a USD-listed series, a strengthening yen is now an FX tailwind for dollar holders even as it caps local exporter upside. The cycle model projects a turn toward a trough around November 2026.","now_zh":"EWJ（日本）目前处于扩张阶段，周期位置约55/100，既未过度超卖也未过度拉伸，仍站在200日均线上方。自2025年4月低点以来本轮上涨幅度约66%，是本阶段发达市场中较强劲的行情之一。过去63个交易日相对SPY的强弱为-1.5%，在24个市场中排名第6（居中偏上）。当前核心驱动力是日元温和走强——日本银行于2025年12月加息至0.75%，同时美联储降息缩窄美日利差——叠加银行股领涨的国内重估；由于EWJ以美元计价，日元升值如今对美元持有者构成汇率顺风，但也压制本地出口商的上行空间。周期模型预计本轮扩张将于2026年11月前后转向见顶回落。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewl":{"legs":{"2011-09-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewl:trough:2011-09"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewl:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-25":{"body":"As the eurozone sovereign debt crisis ran through 2011-2012, Switzerland's defensive index and its non-euro safe-haven currency drew capital fleeing peripheral Europe. Novartis and Roche delivered steady earnings while euro-area banks were under stress, and the SNB's EUR/CHF floor of 1.20 (set September 2011) capped FX tail risk, letting Swiss equities participate in the global risk recovery into 2015. This up-leg captured both the European stabilization trade and a multi-year defensive/pharma re-rating, gaining roughly 87% in USD terms.","body_zh":"欧元区主权债务危机贯穿2011至2012年，瑞士防御性指数与非欧元避险货币吸引了逃离欧洲边缘国家的资本。诺华、罗氏在欧元区银行承压期间维持稳定盈利，而瑞央行2011年9月设定的1.20欧元/瑞郎汇率下限封住了汇率尾部风险，使瑞士股市得以参与至2015年的全球风险修复行情。这一上升行情同时受益于欧洲企稳交易与多年防御/制药板块重估，以美元计约上涨87%。","drivers":["SNB EUR/CHF floor caps FX tail risk","Eurozone crisis capital rotation into Swiss defensives","Novartis and Roche steady earnings amid European stress","Global risk recovery 2012-2015 lifts DM equities"],"prev_key":"2011-11","prev_key_chain":["2011-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Euro crisis refuge, pharma premium builds","title_zh":"欧债危机避风港，制药溢价扩张","turn_id":"ewl:trough:2011-11"},"2014-06-10":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewl:peak:2014-06"},"2014-10-16":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewl:trough:2014-10"},"2015-05-14":{"body":"After the SNB scrapped its EUR/CHF floor in January 2015 (a violent franc revaluation that hit Swiss exporters), EWL rolled over from mid-2015 into a February 2016 trough, declining about 21% in USD terms. The drawdown was driven less by FX than by the loss of the policy anchor compounding global deflation fears, an oil collapse, and China hard-landing worries that pressured all developed markets. Currency strength only partly cushioned the local equity decline for USD investors.","body_zh":"瑞央行于2015年1月取消欧元/瑞郎下限（瑞郎剧烈重估，冲击瑞士出口商）后，EWL自2015年年中回落，至2016年2月见谷，以美元计约下跌21%。此次回撤更多源于政策锚点消失叠加全球通缩担忧、油价崩跌及中国硬着陆忧虑——这些因素压制了所有发达市场，而非单纯汇率。瑞郎走强仅部分缓冲了美元投资者承受的本地股市跌幅。","drivers":["Aftermath of SNB floor removal pressures Swiss exporters","Global deflation scare and oil price collapse","China hard-landing fears weigh on developed markets","Loss of policy anchor adds uncertainty"],"prev_key":"2015-05","prev_key_chain":["2015-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-floor hangover meets global deflation scare","title_zh":"取消下限后的余波叠加全球通缩担忧","turn_id":"ewl:peak:2015-05"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"The February 2016 trough marked a broad global low as oil stabilized, China avoided a hard landing, and the Fed paused. Swiss equities recovered with developed markets, gaining roughly 43% in USD terms into a January 2018 peak. Novartis and Roche contributed stable earnings while EUR/CHF stabilization eased competitive pressure on exporters, and a broadly flat CHF versus the dollar let local gains translate well for USD investors.","body_zh":"2016年2月低谷是全球广泛底部，油价企稳、中国避开硬着陆、美联储暂停加息。瑞士股市随发达市场同步反弹，以美元计约上涨43%，至2018年1月见顶。诺华、罗氏贡献稳定盈利，欧元/瑞郎企稳减轻了出口商竞争压力，瑞郎兑美元大体平稳，使本地涨幅较好地传导给美元投资者。","drivers":["Global synchronized recovery 2016-2018","Fed pause removes USD strength headwind","EUR/CHF stabilization eases Swiss exporter pressure","Pharma pipeline confidence supports Novartis and Roche"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Synchronized global recovery, defensive re-rating","title_zh":"全球同步复苏，防御板块重新定价","turn_id":"ewl:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewl:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"After the Q4 2018 global selloff driven by Fed-tightening fears and US-China trade tensions, EWL recovered as investors rotated into defensive, quality-earnings markets, gaining roughly 42% in USD terms into early 2020. Switzerland's healthcare-heavy composition made it a destination for capital seeking earnings visibility amid the 2019 global slowdown, and CHF stability preserved USD returns. The leg ended as COVID-19 disrupted markets in early 2020.","body_zh":"2018年四季度全球股市因美联储紧缩担忧及中美贸易紧张而调整后，EWL随投资者转向防御性、盈利稳定市场而回升，以美元计约上涨42%，至2020年初。瑞士以医疗为主的成分股使其成为2019年全球放缓中寻求盈利可见性资金的目的地，瑞郎稳定也保障了美元回报。该行情随2020年初新冠疫情冲击市场而终结。","drivers":["Rotation into defensive quality after Q4 2018 selloff","2019 global growth slowdown favors low-volatility defensives","CHF stability preserves USD return","Novartis and Roche earnings-visibility premium"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Late-cycle defensive bid, quality outperforms","title_zh":"周期后期防御需求回升，优质资产领跑","turn_id":"ewl:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-19":{"body":"The February-March 2020 panic saw even Switzerland's defensive index sold aggressively as investors liquidated for cash. EWL fell roughly 28% peak-to-trough in USD terms, notably shallower than cyclical peers but still severe. The CHF initially firmed as a safe haven but was partly capped by SNB intervention. Roche and Novartis, though operationally insulated from the shock, were not spared portfolio de-risking flows.","body_zh":"2020年2至3月恐慌中，投资者争相变现，瑞士防御性指数亦遭大力抛售。EWL以美元计从高峰至低谷下跌约28%，明显浅于周期性同类但仍剧烈。瑞郎初期因避险需求走强，但受瑞央行干预部分压制。罗氏、诺华虽在经营层面与冲击相对隔离，仍未能幸免于去风险组合流出。","drivers":["Global pandemic panic liquidation across asset classes","SNB intervenes to limit CHF safe-haven appreciation","Portfolio de-risking overwhelms defensive earnings stability","Drawdown shallow vs cyclicals but still meaningful"],"prev_key":"2020-02","prev_key_chain":["2020-02"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID-19 selloff: defensives sold for cash","title_zh":"新冠抛售：防御股遭现金化清仓","turn_id":"ewl:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From the March 2020 low, EWL rose roughly 80% to a December 2021 peak, driven by the global liquidity surge, vaccine optimism (Roche central to COVID-19 diagnostics), and demand for defensive quality. However, persistent CHF strength against the dollar through 2020-2021 meant USD investors captured less of the local SMI gain than European peers. Nestle benefited from staples demand while the SNB held rates deeply negative, supporting valuations.","body_zh":"从2020年3月低点起，EWL以美元计上涨约80%，至2021年12月高峰，受益于全球流动性泛滥、疫苗乐观情绪（罗氏为新冠检测核心）以及对防御性优质资产的追捧。然而，2020至2021年瑞郎持续对美元走强，使美元投资者所捕获的SMI本地涨幅少于欧洲同类。雀巢受益于必需品需求，瑞央行维持深度负利率也支撑了估值。","drivers":["Global liquidity surge lifts all equities","Roche central to COVID-19 diagnostics demand","Nestle staples demand steady through pandemic","CHF appreciation caps USD-denominated upside vs local SMI gain"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-COVID recovery: pharma leads, CHF headwind","title_zh":"疫情后复苏：制药领涨，瑞郎成阻力","turn_id":"ewl:trough:2020-03"},"2021-12-29":{"body":"The December 2021 to October 2022 drawdown of roughly 29% in USD terms was driven by overlapping forces: the global tightening cycle compressing growth multiples, the SNB's June 2022 rate hike (its first since 2007) tightening domestic conditions, and company-specific headwinds at Nestle (cost inflation) and Roche (COVID-diagnostic normalization). The CHF firmed as the SNB front-ran European peers in normalizing rates, a cross-current for USD investors.","body_zh":"2021年12月至2022年10月，EWL以美元计约下跌29%，由叠加力量驱动：全球紧缩周期压缩成长估值；瑞央行2022年6月加息（自2007年以来首次）收紧国内条件；雀巢（成本通胀）与罗氏（新冠检测需求正常化）各自面临公司层面阻力。瑞郎因瑞央行率先于欧洲同行正常化利率而走强，给美元投资者带来双向干扰。","drivers":["Global rate-tightening cycle compresses growth multiples","SNB surprise June 2022 hike (first since 2007) tightens conditions","Nestle hit by input-cost inflation","Roche COVID-diagnostic normalization removes pandemic tailwind"],"prev_key":"2021-12","prev_key_chain":["2021-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Hawkish pivot and SNB hike weigh on SMI","title_zh":"鹰派转向与瑞央行加息压制SMI","turn_id":"ewl:peak:2021-12"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"From the October 2022 trough through a February 2026 peak, EWL gained roughly 87% in USD terms, matching the 2011-2015 bull leg. Drivers included the global disinflation trade lifting defensive-quality valuations, Novartis pipeline confidence, and the SNB pivoting to rate cuts from March 2024 (it was the first major developed central bank to cut), which eased CHF appreciation pressure and supported multiples. As the leg extends into late-2025/2026, treat the most recent gains as momentum/valuation-driven rather than tied to any single confirmed catalyst.","body_zh":"从2022年10月低谷至2026年2月高峰，EWL以美元计上涨约87%，与2011至2015年牛市行情幅度相当。驱动因素包括全球去通胀交易提振防御性优质资产估值、诺华研发管线信心，以及瑞央行自2024年3月起转向降息（为首家降息的主要发达经济体央行），缓解瑞郎升值压力并支撑估值倍数。鉴于该行情延伸至2025年底/2026年，应将最近涨幅视为由动能/估值驱动，而非系于任何单一已确认催化剂。","drivers":["Global disinflation trade lifts defensive-quality valuations","Novartis pipeline confidence","SNB rate cuts from March 2024 ease CHF pressure and support multiples","Recent 2025-26 gains momentum/valuation-driven (cautious)"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"~87% recovery leg: disinflation and SNB easing","title_zh":"约87%复苏行情：去通胀与瑞央行宽松","turn_id":"ewl:trough:2022-10"},"2023-05-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewl:peak:2023-05"},"2023-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewl:trough:2023-10"}},"now":"EWL (Switzerland) is in an Expansion phase at a cycle position of roughly 40/100, having pulled back from a February 2026 peak and now sitting in the lower half of its current up-leg, neither washed-out nor stretched. A firm safe-haven CHF drags USD-denominated returns for US investors even when local Swiss equities hold relatively stable, since EWL return = local equity x CHF/USD. Over the last 63 days EWL has lagged SPY by about 3.3 percentage points (rank 7 of the country set), a moderate underperformance consistent with the defensive, low-beta character of Swiss large-caps versus high-momentum US tech.","now_zh":"EWL（瑞士）当前处于扩张阶段，周期位置约40/100，已从2026年2月高峰回调，目前处于本轮上升行情的中下半段——既未洗盘充分，也谈不上超买。坚挺的避险瑞郎使以美元计价的EWL承受汇率拖累，即便瑞士本地股市相对稳定，因为EWL回报＝本地股票×瑞郎/美元。过去63日相对标普500落后约3.3个百分点（在国家序列中排第7），属温和落后，与瑞士大盘股低贝塔的防御特性、以及相对高动能美股的差距相符。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewn":{"legs":{"2011-09-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2011-09"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-25":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2011-11"},"2012-03-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2012-03"},"2012-06-01":{"body":"Draghi's July 2012 'whatever it takes' pledge removed eurozone redenomination risk and triggered a broad European re-rating. The Netherlands, with AAA sovereign credit and an open export economy, benefited as risk premia compressed and global growth recovered through 2014-15. ASML's commercial EUV development added a structural technology premium. A weakening euro into this period (EUR/USD fell from the mid-1.30s toward the low 1.20s by 2015) was a currency headwind that partially offset local gains for USD-denominated holders, but the local re-rating dominated. The leg ran ~85% over roughly three years.","body_zh":"2012年7月德拉吉「不惜一切」的承诺消除了欧元区再计价风险，触发欧洲股市大幅重估。荷兰凭借AAA主权信用与开放的出口型经济，受益于风险溢价收缩与2014-2015年全球经济复苏。ASML的EUV商业化研发注入了结构性科技溢价。这一时期欧元走弱（欧元/美元从1.30中段跌向2015年的1.20低段），对美元计价持有人构成货币逆风，部分抵消本地涨幅，但本地重估占据主导。本段行情历时约三年，累计上涨约85%。","drivers":["ECB 'whatever it takes' pledge","Eurozone risk-premium compression","ASML EUV commercialization","Weak euro as partial USD headwind"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Draghi Pledge Ends Eurozone Crisis","title_zh":"德拉吉承诺终结欧元区危机","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2012-06"},"2014-06-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2014-06"},"2014-10-16":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2014-10"},"2015-05-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2015-05"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"After a sharp global risk-off episode in early 2016 (China devaluation fears, oil collapse), coordinated central-bank easing drove a synchronized global reflation trade. The Netherlands outperformed broader Europe as ASML and technology grew in AEX weight. EUR/USD was broadly range-bound to softer over the stretch, a mild currency headwind for USD-denominated holders that local strength offset. The leg produced ~65% through January 2018 before the global reflation trade peaked.","body_zh":"2016年初全球风险规避（中国汇率恐慌、油价崩塌）急剧升温后，主要央行协调宽松推动全球同步再通胀交易。随着ASML及科技股在AEX中权重上升，荷兰表现优于欧洲其他市场。这一阶段欧元/美元大体震荡偏弱，对美元计价持有人构成轻微货币逆风，但被本地强势抵消。本段行情至2018年1月全球再通胀交易见顶，累计上涨约65%。","drivers":["Synchronized global reflation","Coordinated central-bank easing","Rising ASML / tech AEX weight","Soft EUR as mild USD headwind"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Global Sync Recovery, Tech-Weight Tailwind","title_zh":"全球同步复苏，科技权重提供顺风","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"After the Q4 2018 global equity sell-off driven by Fed hikes and US-China trade-war escalation, EWN recovered as the Fed pivoted dovish in early 2019 and ASML delivered record ~EUR 11.8 billion 2019 revenue. ASML's EUV ramp cemented its position as an effectively irreplaceable supplier, sustaining the re-rating. The ~41% leg ended abruptly with the COVID shock in early 2020.","body_zh":"经历2018年四季度美联储加息与中美贸易战升级引发的全球股市抛售后，美联储2019年初转向宽松，EWN随之反弹，同期ASML实现约118亿欧元的创纪录2019年营收。ASML的EUV产能爬坡巩固了其作为近乎无可替代供应商的地位，持续支撑估值重估。这段约41%的涨幅随2020年初新冠冲击戛然而止。","drivers":["Fed dovish pivot 2019","ASML record 2019 revenue","EUV ramp / supplier dominance","Global PMI stabilization"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade-War Trough to Pre-COVID Peak","title_zh":"贸易战低点至新冠前高点","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2018-12"},"2020-02-12":{"body":"The February-March 2020 pandemic sell-off hit EWN for a ~35% drawdown in roughly four weeks. Global supply chains froze, semiconductor demand uncertainty surged, and a USD safe-haven bid amplified losses for euro-area USD-denominated ETFs. The drawdown was somewhat shallower than broader Europe partly because the AEX lacks the bank-heavy composition that weighed on other European indexes.","body_zh":"2020年2月至3月，新冠疫情抛售使EWN在约四周内回撤约35%。全球供应链冻结，半导体需求前景骤然不确定，美元避险买盘放大了欧元区美元计价ETF的跌幅。由于AEX不像其他欧洲指数那样具有沉重的银行股权重，本次回撤幅度略浅于欧洲大部分市场。","drivers":["Pandemic demand freeze","USD safe-haven surge","Global supply-chain disruption","Light bank weight cushioning AEX"],"prev_key":"2020-02","prev_key_chain":["2020-02"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Crash: Sharp but Brief","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：剧烈但短暂","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2020-02"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"The March 2020 low triggered EWN's largest cycle leg in the dataset -- a ~144% rally to September 2021. Global fiscal and monetary stimulus ignited a technology supercycle, with semiconductor demand surging for remote-work, 5G, and automotive chips, and ASML's backlog building rapidly. EUR/USD rallying from ~1.07 toward ~1.22 added a powerful currency kicker for USD-denominated holders. The leg ended as global growth expectations peaked and tightening fears emerged.","body_zh":"2020年3月低点触发了本数据集中EWN最大的一段周期涨幅——至2021年9月累计上涨约144%。全球财政与货币刺激点燃科技超级周期，远程办公、5G及汽车芯片需求激增，ASML订单积压快速攀升。欧元/美元从约1.07升向约1.22，为美元计价持有人提供强劲汇率红利。随着全球增长预期见顶、收紧预期浮现，本段涨幅结束。","drivers":["Global stimulus / tech supercycle","ASML backlog build","EUR/USD rally (~1.07 to ~1.22)","Semiconductor capacity race"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic Recovery: Tech and Chip Supercycle","title_zh":"疫情复苏：科技与芯片超级周期","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2020-03"},"2021-09-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2021-09"},"2022-03-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2022-03"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"After the brutal 2022 bear market -- ECB tightening, the energy crisis from the Russia-Ukraine war, and a surging USD -- European equities bottomed in October 2022. EWN rallied ~54% by July 2023 as European gas prices collapsed from their 2022 peaks, ECB hikes were seen nearing their end, and the euro rebounded from its 2022 parity lows, restoring the currency tailwind. ASML earnings momentum stayed intact through this stretch.","body_zh":"经历欧洲央行加息、俄乌战争引发的能源危机以及美元飙升所导致的2022年惨烈熊市后，欧洲股票于2022年10月触底。随着欧洲天然气价格从2022年高位回落、市场认为欧洲央行加息接近尾声、欧元从2022年平价低点反弹并恢复汇率顺风，EWN至2023年7月累计上涨约54%。这一阶段ASML盈利动能保持完好。","drivers":["European gas-price collapse","ECB near peak-rate expectations","EUR/USD rebound from parity","Resilient ASML earnings"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Inflation Peak Relief Rally","title_zh":"通胀见顶、缓解性反弹","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2022-10"},"2023-07-18":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2023-07"},"2023-10-20":{"body":"A new leg began in October 2023 as the AI infrastructure build-out drove demand for advanced logic chips, feeding ASML's EUV order pipeline. The AEX pushed to successive highs into mid-2024, with ASML at record prices, and a modestly firmer euro added to USD-denominated gains. The leg topped in July 2024 (~47% gain) as the AI-equipment trade ran ahead of near-term order momentum, setting up the subsequent correction.","body_zh":"2023年10月，随着AI基础设施建设推动先进逻辑芯片需求并充实ASML的EUV订单管线，EWN开启新一段约47%的行情。AEX在2024年上半年持续刷新高点，ASML股价屡创纪录，欧元温和走强进一步为美元计价收益加码。本段行情于2024年7月见顶，AI设备交易领先于近期订单动能，为随后的调整埋下伏笔。","drivers":["AI infrastructure buildout","ASML EUV order pipeline","AEX record highs","Modest EUR tailwind"],"prev_key":"2023-10","prev_key_chain":["2023-10"],"status":"exact","title":"AI Chip Demand Drives AEX to Records","title_zh":"AI芯片需求驱动AEX创历史新高","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2023-10"},"2024-07-12":{"body":"From the July 2024 peak, EWN fell ~20% into April 2025. The decisive catalyst came in October 2024, when ASML accidentally released results early showing Q3 net bookings of just EUR 2.6 billion versus expectations near EUR 5 billion and a cut 2025 sales outlook; the shares fell ~15.7% in a single session, their worst drop since IPO, signalling a semiconductor-capex digestion phase. Tariff uncertainty under the new US administration and a firming USD that amplified losses for USD-denominated holders added pressure. The correction was ultimately shallower than feared as ASML's long-cycle backlog provided a floor.","body_zh":"自2024年7月高点，EWN至2025年4月下跌约20%。决定性催化剂出现在2024年10月：ASML意外提前发布业绩，显示三季度净订单仅26亿欧元，远低于约50亿欧元的预期，并下调2025年销售指引；股价单日暴跌约15.7%，为上市以来最大跌幅，标志半导体资本支出进入消化阶段。新届美国政府的关税不确定性，以及美元走强放大美元计价持有人的损失，进一步施压。由于ASML长周期积压订单提供支撑，最终回撤浅于市场最初担忧。","drivers":["ASML Oct 2024 bookings miss (EUR 2.6bn)","Cut 2025 sales outlook","Semiconductor capex digestion","USD firming amplifying losses"],"prev_key":"2024-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-07"],"status":"exact","title":"ASML Order-Shock Correction","title_zh":"ASML订单冲击调整","turn_id":"ewn:peak:2024-07"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From the April 2025 trough, EWN surged ~80% to the June 2026 peak as the AI capex cycle reaccelerated and ASML order momentum recovered. A major leg of the move was currency: the dollar fell sharply in 2025 (DXY roughly -9% on the year, EUR/USD from ~1.04 toward ~1.18, briefly above 1.20 in early 2026), a powerful tailwind for USD-denominated EWN holders on top of local equity strength. At pos 91.4/100 with the model projecting a trough by around October 2026, this leg is statistically late-cycle, so specific forward catalysts are best treated cautiously.","body_zh":"自2025年4月低点，随着AI资本支出周期重新加速、ASML订单动能恢复，EWN至2026年6月顶峰累计上涨约80%。本轮上涨的重要推动来自汇率：2025年美元大幅走弱（DXY全年约-9%，欧元/美元从约1.04升向约1.18，2026年初一度突破1.20），在本地股票强势之上为EWN美元计价持有人提供强劲顺风。当前位置评分91.4/100，模型预测约在2026年10月见底，本段行情在统计意义上已处于周期晚期，具体的前瞻催化因素宜审慎看待。","drivers":["AI capex reacceleration","Recovering ASML order momentum","USD weakness / EUR strength amplifier","Late-cycle positioning"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"AI-Capex Rebound, Dollar-Weakness Amplifier","title_zh":"AI资本支出回暖，美元走弱放大","turn_id":"ewn:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"EWN sits at a cycle Peak with a position score of 91.4 out of 100, highly extended after an ~80% rally from the April 2025 trough -- one of the sharpest developed-market rebounds in this dataset. Relative strength vs. SPY over the trailing 63 days is +6.8%, ranking third globally, driven by AI-related semiconductor demand flowing to ASML and by a sharply weaker dollar that lifted USD-denominated returns through 2025. The model projects a turn to trough around October 2026, so the current stretch carries elevated mean-reversion risk even as momentum remains intact.","now_zh":"EWN目前处于周期顶峰，位置评分高达91.4/100，自2025年4月低点以来累计上涨约80%，为本数据集中发达市场涨幅最大的市场之一。过去63日相对标普500超额收益达+6.8%，全球排名第三，主要受益于AI相关半导体需求传导至ASML，以及2025年美元大幅走弱对美元计价回报的提振。模型预测下一个低点约在2026年10月，因此当前高位区间的均值回归风险不容忽视，尽管动能仍然完好。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewp":{"legs":{"2011-09-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewp:trough:2011-09"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewp:peak:2011-10"},"2012-06-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewp:trough:2012-06"},"2012-07-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewp:peak:2012-07"},"2012-07-24":{"body":"By mid-2012, Spain's 10-year yield had pierced 7.5% (23 July 2012) and the country was on the brink of a sovereign bailout. Mario Draghi's 'whatever it takes' pledge on 26 July 2012, followed by the ECB's Outright Monetary Transactions (OMT) announcement on 6 September, collapsed yields and ignited a +136% rally in EWP to mid-2014. Spanish banks, which had been pricing existential risk, surged as the systemic threat receded and the EU funded a banking-sector recapitalization. EUR/USD was relatively range-bound over this period, so USD-denominated returns broadly tracked the IBEX recovery.","body_zh":"2012年中，西班牙10年期国债收益率突破7.5%（2012年7月23日），国家濒临主权救助边缘。德拉吉2012年7月26日不惜一切代价的承诺，以及欧洲央行9月6日宣布的直接货币交易（OMT）计划，令收益率骤降，推动EWP至2014年中累计上涨约136%。此前已反映系统性风险的西班牙银行股大幅飙升，欧盟同期出资支持银行业资本重组。该阶段欧元/美元区间波动，美元计价回报与IBEX本地涨幅大体一致。","drivers":["Draghi 'whatever it takes' + OMT: Spanish yields fell from 7.5% toward ~5% by spring 2013","EU bank recapitalization backstopped Spanish lenders","Synchronized eurozone recovery 2013-2014","Spain GDP returned to positive growth in 2013-2014"],"drivers_zh":["德拉吉承诺+OMT：西班牙收益率从7.5%回落至2013年春约5%","欧盟银行业资本重组为西班牙银行兜底","2013-2014年欧元区同步复苏","西班牙GDP于2013-2014年重回正增长"],"prev_key":"2012-07","prev_key_chain":["2012-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Draghi Put Ends Sovereign Debt Crisis","title_zh":"德拉吉承诺终结主权债务危机","turn_id":"ewp:trough:2012-07"},"2014-06-09":{"body":"The 2014-2016 down leg (-41%) was a confluence of external shocks amplified by Spain's index composition. The oil-price crash from mid-2014 hit Repsol, and deflation fears slowed ECB normalization. Santander and BBVA, heavily exposed to Brazil and other EM currencies, suffered as the Brazilian real and other EM FX fell sharply against the dollar. The 2015 Greek debt crisis and Syriza standoff with creditors triggered broad eurozone risk-off, and Spain's December 2015 election produced a hung parliament. EUR/USD dropped from ~1.39 to ~1.08 over 2014-2015, compressing USD-denominated EWP returns further.","body_zh":"2014-2016年下跌（约-41%）由多重外部冲击叠加、经IBEX指数结构放大所致。2014年中起油价崩跌冲击雷普索尔，通缩担忧延缓欧洲央行正常化。桑坦德与BBVA在巴西等新兴市场敞口庞大，随着巴西雷亚尔等新兴市场货币兑美元大幅下跌而受压。2015年希腊债务危机与激进左翼党对抗债权人引发欧元区系统性风险，西班牙2015年12月大选后形成悬挂议会。欧元/美元于2014-2015年由约1.39跌至约1.08，进一步压缩了EWP的美元计价回报。","drivers":["Oil-price collapse: Repsol drag, eurozone deflation fears","EM FX stress: BRL and other EM currencies hit Santander/BBVA","Greek crisis 2015: eurozone risk-off","Spanish political deadlock: hung parliament Dec 2015","EUR/USD ~1.39 to ~1.08: USD headwind on returns"],"drivers_zh":["油价崩跌：雷普索尔拖累，欧元区通缩担忧","新兴市场汇率压力：巴西雷亚尔等冲击桑坦德/BBVA","2015年希腊危机：欧元区风险厌恶","西班牙政治僵局：2015年12月悬挂议会","欧元/美元由约1.39跌至约1.08：美元构成回报阻力"],"prev_key":"2014-06","prev_key_chain":["2014-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil Crash, EM Stress & Greek Standoff","title_zh":"油价崩跌、新兴市场压力与希腊对峙","turn_id":"ewp:peak:2014-06"},"2016-02-11":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewp:trough:2016-02"},"2016-04-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewp:peak:2016-04"},"2016-06-27":{"body":"From mid-2016, Spain entered a new expansion (+65%) as the ECB's QE program suppressed yields and improved the bank earnings outlook. Spain resolved its political deadlock with a second election in June 2016, and GDP growth ran above 3%. Global trade re-synchronization and commodity stabilization supported the EM subsidiaries of Spanish banks. The Catalonia independence referendum in October 2017 introduced sharp intra-leg volatility but markets recovered as Madrid imposed direct rule. EUR/USD strengthened notably through 2017 (from ~1.04 to ~1.20), amplifying USD-denominated returns over the leg.","body_zh":"2016年中起，随着欧洲央行量化宽松压低收益率并改善银行盈利前景，西班牙进入新一轮扩张（约+65%）。西班牙于2016年6月二次大选后解除政治僵局，GDP增速超过3%。全球贸易再同步与大宗商品企稳支撑西班牙银行的新兴市场子行。2017年10月加泰罗尼亚独立公投引发阶段性剧烈波动，但随着马德里实施直接管辖后市场收复。2017年欧元/美元显著走强（由约1.04升至约1.20），放大了本阶段美元计价回报。","drivers":["ECB QE: asset purchases + TLTRO liquidity suppressed yields","Spain political resolution: stable government from Jun 2016","GDP above 3%: among the fastest-growing eurozone economies","EUR/USD rise in 2017 (~1.04 to ~1.20) amplified USD returns"],"drivers_zh":["欧洲央行QE：资产购买+TLTRO流动性压低收益率","西班牙政治解局：2016年6月组成稳定政府","GDP超3%：欧元区增速最快经济体之一","2017年欧元/美元上涨（约1.04至1.20）放大美元计价回报"],"prev_key":"2016-06","prev_key_chain":["2016-06"],"status":"exact","title":"ECB QE & Synchronized European Expansion","title_zh":"欧洲央行量化宽松与欧洲同步扩张","turn_id":"ewp:trough:2016-06"},"2018-01-26":{"body":"The down leg from January 2018 to March 2020 compressed EWP by -46% as multiple waves of pressure compounded. Catalonia's unresolved political crisis kept a risk premium on Spanish assets. Global trade tensions in 2018 and simultaneous EM stress (Argentina and Turkey crises heavily impacted BBVA) drove a European derating, while Italy's 2018-2019 budget standoff widened peripheral spreads. The COVID-19 pandemic then delivered the knockout blow: Spain was among Europe's worst-hit economies in spring 2020 and tourism effectively shut down. EUR/USD drifted lower over much of this period, compounding the USD-denominated drawdown.","body_zh":"2018年1月至2020年3月，多轮压力叠加令EWP累计下跌约46%。加泰罗尼亚政治危机悬而未决，持续令西班牙资产承压。2018年全球贸易紧张及同期新兴市场压力（阿根廷与土耳其危机重创BBVA）引发欧洲股市估值下修，2018-2019年意大利预算对峙又扩大外围国利差。新冠疫情最终给予致命一击：西班牙成为欧洲受打击最严重的经济体之一，旅游业几近停摆。欧元/美元在此期间多数时段走低，加剧了美元计价的回撤。","drivers":["Catalonia: unresolved constitutional crisis, risk premium on Spanish assets","EM stress 2018: Argentina/Turkey crises hit BBVA hard","Italy budget standoff: peripheral spread widening","COVID-19: tourism collapse, Spain among Europe's worst-hit"],"drivers_zh":["加泰罗尼亚：宪政危机悬而未决，西班牙资产风险溢价","2018年新兴市场压力：阿根廷/土耳其危机重创BBVA","意大利预算对峙：外围国利差走阔","新冠疫情：旅游业崩溃，西班牙受创最深"],"prev_key":"2018-01","prev_key_chain":["2018-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Catalonia Fallout, EM Stress & COVID Crash","title_zh":"加泰罗尼亚后遗症、新兴市场压力与新冠崩盘","turn_id":"ewp:peak:2018-01"},"2020-03-16":{"body":"From the March 2020 COVID trough, Spain rebounded +75% to June 2021 on ECB pandemic emergency purchases (PEPP), the EU Next Generation recovery fund (Spain a major beneficiary), and the reopening of tourism. Banks recovered as systemic risk evaporated under ECB support. EUR/USD rallied through 2020-2021 (from ~1.07 toward ~1.23), meaningfully amplifying USD-denominated gains versus the IBEX local return. The leg ended as global inflation surprised higher and rate expectations shifted, pressuring the rate-sensitive IBEX into consolidation through mid-2022.","body_zh":"从2020年3月新冠低点起，西班牙依托欧洲央行疫情紧急购债计划（PEPP）、欧盟下一代复苏基金（西班牙为主要受益国）以及旅游业重开，累计反弹约75%至2021年6月。欧洲央行兜底下系统性风险消退，银行股收复失地。2020-2021年欧元/美元升值（由约1.07升向约1.23），显著放大了相对IBEX本地回报的美元计价涨幅。随着全球通胀持续超预期、加息预期升温，利率敏感的IBEX于2022年中进入整固，本阶段结束。","drivers":["ECB PEPP: pandemic emergency bond buying compressed spreads","EU Next Generation Fund: Spain a major recipient","Tourism reopening: services rebound from H2 2020","EUR/USD rally 2020-2021 (~1.07 to ~1.23) amplified USD returns"],"drivers_zh":["欧洲央行PEPP：疫情紧急购债令利差收窄","欧盟下一代基金：西班牙为主要受益国","旅游业重开：2020年下半年起服务业反弹","2020-2021年欧元/美元升值（约1.07至1.23）放大美元计价回报"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"EU Recovery Fund & Tourism Rebound","title_zh":"欧盟复苏基金与旅游反弹","turn_id":"ewp:trough:2020-03"},"2021-05-25":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewp:peak:2021-05"},"2022-03-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewp:trough:2022-03"},"2022-05-27":{"body":"A brief but sharp -26% decline from May to October 2022 as the ECB launched its most aggressive rate-hiking cycle in its history, triggering a derating of European equities. Spain's inflation peaked above 10% in mid-2022 on energy and food prices after the Russia-Ukraine war, squeezing consumer and corporate margins. Banks faced a near-term paradox: higher rates would eventually boost NIM, but credit-quality and growth fears weighed first. EUR/USD fell to ~parity (its lowest in two decades) in September 2022, further compressing USD-denominated EWP returns during the drawdown.","body_zh":"2022年5月至10月短暂但剧烈的下跌（约-26%），源于欧洲央行启动史上最激进的加息周期，引发欧洲股市估值重估。俄乌战争推高能源与食品价格，西班牙通胀于2022年中峰值超过10%，挤压消费者与企业利润。银行股面临近期悖论：更高利率最终将提升净息差，但信贷质量与增长忧虑先行压制。欧元/美元于2022年9月跌至约平价（约二十年低点），进一步压低了EWP美元计价回报。","drivers":["ECB rate shock: most aggressive hiking cycle triggered derating","Energy inflation: Repsol tailwind vs consumer/margin squeeze","EUR/USD to ~parity Sep 2022: multi-decade USD headwind","Russia-Ukraine war: energy-supply uncertainty weighed on Europe"],"drivers_zh":["欧洲央行利率冲击：史上最激进加息周期触发估值重估","能源通胀：雷普索尔顺风 vs 消费者/利润率受压","欧元/美元接近平价（2022年9月）：数十年美元阻力","俄乌战争：能源供应不确定性压制欧洲"],"prev_key":"2022-05","prev_key_chain":["2022-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Inflation Shock & ECB Tightening","title_zh":"通胀冲击与欧洲央行紧缩","turn_id":"ewp:peak:2022-05"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"The +247% advance from October 2022 to June 2026 is the dominant feature of Spain's chart and one of the strongest bull runs among developed-market ETFs. The primary driver was the transformation of Spanish bank profitability: higher ECB rates dramatically expanded net interest margins at Santander, BBVA and CaixaBank, driving large earnings upgrades and dividend increases (in 2025 banks captured the bulk of the IBEX's gains, with Santander up roughly +125% and BBVA +112% on the year). Spain's GDP grew well above the eurozone average, supported by record tourism (~12-13% of GDP), immigration-driven labour supply and EU Next Generation fund spending. EUR/USD recovered from parity toward ~1.10-1.17 by 2024-2025, amplifying USD returns. As of June 2026 the market sits at its cycle peak, with the model projecting a trough around November 2026 as anticipated ECB rate cuts begin to compress bank NIM.","body_zh":"2022年10月至2026年6月累计涨幅约247%，是西班牙图表中最显著的特征，也是发达市场ETF中最强劲的牛市之一。核心驱动是西班牙银行盈利能力的根本性转变：欧洲央行高利率大幅扩张桑坦德、BBVA与CaixaBank的净息差，推动盈利预期大幅上调与股息提升（2025年银行股贡献了IBEX的大部分涨幅，桑坦德全年约+125%、BBVA约+112%）。西班牙GDP增速远超欧元区平均，由创纪录旅游业（约占GDP12-13%）、移民驱动的劳动力供给以及欧盟下一代基金支出支撑。欧元/美元由平价回升至2024-2025年约1.10-1.17，放大美元计价回报。截至2026年6月，市场处于周期高点，模型预测下一个低点约在2026年11月前后，届时预期中的欧洲央行降息将开始压缩银行净息差。","drivers":["Bank NIM surge: ECB rates boosted Santander/BBVA/CaixaBank earnings","Spain GDP well above eurozone average: standout grower","Tourism record: ~12-13% of GDP, post-COVID peak demand","EU Next Gen Fund: infrastructure spending boosted domestic demand","EUR/USD recovery from parity amplified USD-denominated gains"],"drivers_zh":["银行净息差飙升：欧洲央行高利率提振桑坦德/BBVA/CaixaBank盈利","西班牙GDP远超欧元区平均：亮眼增长引擎","旅游业创纪录：约占GDP12-13%，疫后需求达峰","欧盟下一代基金：基础设施支出提振内需","欧元/美元从平价回升放大美元计价涨幅"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Bank NIM Supercycle & Outperformance Era","title_zh":"银行净息差超级周期与跑赢时代","turn_id":"ewp:trough:2022-10"}},"now":"Spain's EWP sits in early Recovery at position 30/100 within the current cycle, pulled back from its June 2026 high but still holding above the 200-day moving average. The 63-day relative strength vs SPY is modestly negative (-0.9), placing it mid-pack among developed-market peers (RS rank 5). The IBEX 35's dominant banks (Santander, BBVA, CaixaBank) drove a roughly +247% advance off the October 2022 low, but the market is consolidating as ECB rate-cut expectations begin to compress the net-interest-margin tailwind. The cycle model projects the next trough around November 2026.","now_zh":"西班牙EWP目前处于复苏早期，周期位置30/100，已自2026年6月高点回落，但仍站稳200日均线上方。过去63日相对SPY强度为-0.9，在发达市场中处于中游（强度排名第5）。IBEX 35中占主导的银行股（桑坦德、BBVA、CaixaBank）推动指数自2022年10月低点累计上涨约247%，但随着欧洲央行降息预期开始压缩净息差优势，市场进入整固。周期模型预测下一个低点约在2026年11月前后。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewq":{"legs":{"2011-09-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2011-09"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-25":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2011-11"},"2012-03-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:peak:2012-03"},"2012-07-24":{"body":"Mario Draghi's July 2012 'whatever it takes' pledge broke the Eurozone sovereign-debt crisis and unlocked a powerful recovery across core and peripheral European equities. French large-caps, deeply discounted on recession and breakup fears, rebounded sharply as ECB credibility was restored and interbank lending normalized. The euro stabilized and then firmed, adding a USD-return layer on top of the local rally. The leg extended into mid-2014 as ECB easing expectations kept credit conditions loose and French exporters benefited from recovering European demand, for a roughly 81% USD gain.","body_zh":"马里奥·德拉吉2012年7月不惜一切代价的承诺打破了欧元区主权债务危机，欧洲核心与外围市场强势反弹。法国大盘股因衰退和欧元区解体恐慌而被深度低估，随着欧央行公信力恢复、同业拆借正常化，股价大幅反弹。欧元企稳走强，为USD计价回报叠加了汇率增益。进入2014年中，欧央行宽松预期持续压低信贷成本，法国出口商受益于欧洲内需复苏，该阶段USD计价涨幅约81%。","drivers":["ECB whatever-it-takes pledge","Eurozone breakup risk removal","EUR/USD stabilization and recovery","French large-cap valuation re-rating"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行不惜一切代价承诺","欧元区解体风险消除","欧元/美元企稳回升","法国大盘股估值重估"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"rekey_shift_days":39,"status":"shifted","title":"Draghi pledge ends Eurozone crisis","title_zh":"德拉吉承诺终结欧元区危机","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2012-07"},"2014-06-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:peak:2014-06"},"2015-01-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2015-01"},"2015-05-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:peak:2015-05"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"The February 2016 trough marked a global risk reset as China fears and the oil crash bottomed. From there, French equities rode a synchronized global reflation wave amplified by continued ECB quantitative easing. Emmanuel Macron's May 2017 presidential victory was the defining local catalyst: his pro-EU centrist platform removed the existential political risk around Marine Le Pen and triggered a broad European-asset re-rating. The euro rallied into early 2018, contributing to the roughly 63% USD-denominated gain in EWQ over this leg.","body_zh":"2016年2月的低点标志着全球风险的重置，中国恐慌与油价暴跌在此见底。此后，法国股市乘上全球再通胀浪潮，欧央行持续QE进一步放大涨幅。2017年5月马克龙赢得总统大选是关键的本土催化剂：其亲欧、中间立场的政策纲领消除了围绕勒庞的欧元区存亡性政治风险，带动欧洲资产全面重估。欧元走强延续至2018年初，推动该阶段EWQ的USD计价涨幅约63%。","drivers":["Macron election removes Le Pen systemic risk","ECB QE continuation","Synchronized global reflation 2016-2017","EUR/USD rally adding USD returns"],"drivers_zh":["马克龙当选消除勒庞系统性风险","欧央行QE延续","2016至2017年全球同步再通胀","欧元/美元走强增益USD回报"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Macron victory, ECB QE reflation trade","title_zh":"马克龙当选，欧央行QE推动再通胀","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Following the global Q4 2018 selloff driven by US-China trade-war escalation and Fed tightening fears, European equities recovered on a Fed pivot and a partial trade truce. France participated in the global recovery, though the Yellow Vest (Gilets Jaunes) protests that erupted in late 2018 added domestic uncertainty and kept French outperformance modest versus the broader European rebound. EUR/USD was broadly range-bound, providing a neutral FX backdrop, so the roughly 32% move was largely a local equity recovery that ran into January 2020.","body_zh":"在2018年第四季度美中贸易战升级和美联储加息恐慌引发全球抛售后，欧洲股市随美联储转向和部分贸易休战而回暖。法国参与了全球复苏行情，但2018年末爆发的黄背心（Gilets Jaunes）抗议运动注入了国内不确定性，制约了法国相对于欧洲整体的超额表现。这一时期欧元/美元基本区间震荡，汇率影响中性，因此约32%的涨幅主要来自本地股市回升，延续至2020年1月。","drivers":["Fed pivot to easing late 2018","Partial US-China trade truce","European earnings recovery","Yellow Vest protests capping local upside"],"drivers_zh":["2018年末美联储转向宽松","美中部分贸易休战","欧洲盈利复苏","黄背心抗议制约本地上行"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-trade-war rebound","title_zh":"贸易战后反弹","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-17":{"body":"The COVID-19 pandemic triggered one of the fastest bear markets in history from January to March 2020. France was acutely exposed given its large tourism, luxury, aerospace, and energy sectors, all hit hard by lockdowns and collapsing global demand. EWQ fell roughly 39% in USD terms over two months, compounded by a euro that initially weakened as global dollar demand surged. ECB emergency bond purchases (PEPP) announced in March 2020 arrested the spiral.","body_zh":"新冠疫情在2020年1至3月引发了史上最快速的熊市之一。法国受创尤深，其旅游、奢侈品、航空航天和能源板块均遭重创，全球需求骤降、封锁措施全面实施。EWQ以USD计价两个月内下跌约39%，加之全球美元需求激增令欧元初期承压，跌幅进一步扩大。欧央行于2020年3月宣布的紧急购债计划（PEPP）最终遏制了下跌螺旋。","drivers":["COVID-19 lockdowns crushing tourism and luxury","Aerospace and energy sector collapse","Global dollar squeeze amplifying EUR weakness","ECB PEPP announcement as floor"],"drivers_zh":["新冠封锁重创旅游与奢侈品","航空航天与能源板块崩塌","全球美元挤兑放大欧元走弱","欧央行PEPP宣布构成底部"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash: global shock, sharp reversal","title_zh":"新冠冲击：全球性猛烈抛售","turn_id":"ewq:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-18":{"body":"The March 2020 low launched one of the sharpest recoveries in French equity history, powered by massive ECB PEPP, the EU Next Generation Recovery Fund agreement in July 2020, and the global vaccine-driven reopening trade. Luxury-goods demand rebounded explosively as Chinese consumption resumed and global savings flowed into high-end spending. EUR/USD rallied from around 1.08 to above 1.22 into early 2021, adding roughly 10-12 points of USD-denominated return on top of strong local CAC 40 performance, for a roughly 109% USD gain into the January 2022 peak.","body_zh":"2020年3月的低点开启了法国股市历史上最强劲的复苏之一，欧央行PEPP大规模购债、欧盟下一代欧洲复苏基金协议（2020年7月）以及全球疫苗驱动的重开放交易共同推动涨势。中国消费复苏带动奢侈品需求爆炸式反弹，全球超额储蓄涌入高端消费领域。欧元/美元从约1.08升至2021年初的1.22上方，为USD计价回报额外贡献约10-12个百分点，叠加CAC 40本身的强劲表现，至2022年1月顶部USD计价涨幅约109%。","drivers":["ECB PEPP and EU Recovery Fund","Vaccine reopening trade","Chinese luxury demand rebound","EUR/USD rally from 1.08 to 1.22"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行PEPP与欧盟复苏基金","疫苗重开放交易","中国奢侈品需求反弹","欧元/美元从1.08升至1.22"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Stimulus surge: COVID recovery and reopening","title_zh":"刺激潮涌：新冠复苏与重开放","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:peak:2021-11"},"2022-03-07":{"body":"Russia's invasion of Ukraine in February 2022 hit France mainly through collapsing European growth expectations and a region-wide energy and power-price shock, compounded by outages across France's nuclear fleet that year. The CAC 40 sold off into September 2022 as the ECB began an aggressive rate-hiking cycle, widening French OAT-Bund spreads. The euro fell toward parity with the USD by mid-2022, a double penalty for USD-denominated EWQ holders as local losses and FX depreciation combined, for a roughly 25% USD drawdown.","body_zh":"2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰主要通过欧洲增长预期崩塌和全欧能源与电价冲击打击法国，并因当年法国核电机组大面积停机而加剧。CAC 40跌至2022年9月，欧央行启动激进加息周期，法德国债利差扩大。欧元兑美元至2022年中跌至平价附近，对EWQ的USD计价持有者形成双重打击——本地下跌与汇率贬值叠加，USD计价回撤约25%。","drivers":["Russia-Ukraine energy and growth shock","ECB aggressive rate hikes","EUR/USD near parity compressing USD returns","French nuclear fleet outages tightening power supply"],"drivers_zh":["俄乌能源与增长冲击","欧央行激进加息","欧元/美元逼近平价压缩USD回报","法国核电机组停机收紧电力供应"],"prev_key":"2022-03","prev_key_chain":["2022-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Ukraine war shock and energy stagflation","title_zh":"乌克兰战争冲击与能源滞胀","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:peak:2022-03"},"2022-09-27":{"body":"The September 2022 trough coincided with peak European energy-crisis fears and the ECB deposit rate moving into restrictive territory. As natural-gas prices fell from their winter 2022-23 highs, European growth proved more resilient than feared and the ECB shifted from pause to an easing cycle in 2024. French equities delivered roughly 100% in USD terms over this nearly four-year leg, aided by a recovering EUR/USD and strong luxury earnings through 2023-2024. The leg peaked in February 2026 as French fiscal risk re-emerged: Macron's 2024 snap election delivered a hung parliament, successive governments fell over budget disputes, and the deficit was flagged above 5% of GDP.","body_zh":"2022年9月的低点与欧洲能源危机恐慌高峰和欧央行存款利率进入限制性区间同步出现。随着天然气价格自2022至23年冬季高位回落，欧洲增长韧性超预期，欧央行于2024年从暂停加息转向降息周期。这近四年的上行阶段法国股市以USD计价涨幅约100%，受益于欧元/美元的修复性上涨以及2023至2024年奢侈品板块的强劲盈利。2026年2月上行腿见顶，法国财政风险重新浮现：马克龙2024年提前选举形成悬浮议会，多届政府因预算争议倒台，财政赤字被警示超过GDP的5%。","drivers":["European energy crisis peak and reversal","ECB rate cycle pause and easing from 2024","Luxury sector earnings strength 2023-2024","EUR/USD recovery aiding USD returns","French political and fiscal risk re-emerging at peak"],"drivers_zh":["欧洲能源危机见顶反转","欧央行加息暂停并自2024年转向宽松","2023至2024年奢侈品盈利强劲","欧元/美元修复增益USD回报","法国政治与财政风险在顶部重现"],"prev_key":"2022-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Inflation peak to ECB pivot: long recovery","title_zh":"通胀见顶至欧央行转向：漫长复苏","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2022-09"},"2024-05-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:peak:2024-05"},"2025-01-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewq:trough:2025-01"}},"now":"EWQ (iShares MSCI France ETF) is in an Expansion phase at cycle position 51.8/100, sitting mid-range after peaking in February 2026 and pulling back modestly. Relative strength vs SPY over the past 63 days is -5.5, making France one of the weakest single-country markets in developed Europe on this measure, weighed down by persistent political and fiscal headwinds that have kept the CAC 40 lagging Germany and Spain even as European equities broadly recovered. The USD-denominated ETF combines local equity performance with EUR/USD dynamics; euro strength provided a tailwind during the long up-leg, but fiscal-deficit concerns and political gridlock following Macron's 2024 snap election have capped upside. The model projects a cyclical trough around August 2026, suggesting the pullback may not yet be complete.","now_zh":"EWQ（iShares MSCI法国ETF）目前处于扩张期，周期位置51.8/100，于2026年2月触顶后小幅回落至中位区间。过去63个交易日相对标普500的强弱指标为-5.5，是发达欧洲单一国家市场中表现最弱的之一——法国政治与财政风险的拖累持续存在，即便欧洲整体回暖，CAC 40依然落后于德国和西班牙。该USD计价ETF同时反映本地股市走势与欧元/美元汇率变动；在漫长的上行阶段中，欧元走强曾带来顺风，但马克龙2024年提前选举后的政治僵局和财政赤字隐忧持续压制法国股市的上行空间。模型预计下一个周期低点约在2026年8月，意味着此轮调整可能尚未结束。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ews":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"body":"The August 2011 global risk-off wave, triggered by the US debt-ceiling downgrade and the eurozone sovereign crisis, hit Asian financials hard. EWS fell about 26% as Singapore's financial-heavy index sold off alongside EM equities, while the SGD softened modestly within its NEER band. The move was swift and externally driven, with no local fundamental deterioration.","body_zh":"2011 年 8 月美国主权评级遭调降叠加欧元区主权危机引发全球风险规避浪潮，亚洲金融股遭受重创。以金融股为主的新加坡指数随新兴市场整体下跌，EWS 急跌约 26%，新加坡元在 NEER 区间内小幅走软。此次下跌迅速且由外部因素驱动，新加坡本地基本面并无明显恶化。","drivers":["US credit downgrade shock","Eurozone contagion to Asian financials","EM broad risk-off deleveraging"],"drivers_zh":["美国主权评级遭调降冲击","欧债危机向亚洲金融股蔓延","新兴市场全面风险规避去杠杆"],"prev_key":"2011-08","prev_key_chain":["2011-08"],"rekey_shift_days":49,"status":"shifted","title":"EM Risk-Off Hits Singapore Banks","title_zh":"新兴市场风险规避冲击新加坡银行股","turn_id":"ews:trough:2011-10"},"2013-05-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ews:peak:2013-05"},"2014-02-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ews:trough:2014-02"},"2014-07-24":{"body":"The 2014-2016 down leg (about -33%) tracked the broad EM selloff as the Fed wound down asset purchases and the USD entered a multi-year bull run. Singapore's trade-dependent economy felt slowing China demand and weaker regional capital flows. The SGD depreciated against the surging dollar, amplifying losses for USD-denominated holders of EWS.","body_zh":"2014 年 7 月至 2016 年 1 月，EWS 下跌约 33%，与新兴市场整体抛售同步，联储退出购债叠加美元进入多年牛市。新加坡贸易导向型经济受中国需求放缓及区域资本流入减弱拖累，新加坡元对强势美元贬值，进一步放大了 EWS 美元持有者的亏损。","drivers":["Fed taper & USD multi-year bull run","China demand deceleration","Weaker regional capital flows","SGD depreciation vs USD"],"drivers_zh":["联储退出购债与美元多年牛市","中国需求放缓","区域资本流入减弱","新加坡元对美元贬值"],"prev_key":"2014-07","prev_key_chain":["2014-07"],"status":"exact","title":"China Slowdown & USD Surge Drag","title_zh":"中国放缓与美元走强双重拖累","turn_id":"ews:peak:2014-07"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"From early 2016 to January 2018, EWS surged about 68% as synchronized global growth, a recovering China and a weaker USD lifted Asian financials and trade-linked names. Singapore banks benefited from improving loan growth and NIM, and the MAS allowed only limited SGD appreciation, adding a modest FX tailwind for USD investors. The broad EM-and-Asia reflation trade was the dominant force.","body_zh":"2016 年初至 2018 年 1 月，受全球同步复苏、中国经济回暖及美元走弱提振，亚洲金融及贸易相关个股上涨，EWS 大涨约 68%。新加坡银行贷款增速与净息差改善，金管局仅允许新加坡元有限升值，为美元投资者提供温和汇率红利。这一阶段以新兴市场及亚洲再通胀交易为主线。","drivers":["Synchronized global growth 2016-2017","USD weakness boosted SGD returns","Singapore bank loan & NIM growth","China reflation spilled into regional trade"],"drivers_zh":["2016—2017 年全球同步增长","美元走弱提升新加坡元美元回报","新加坡银行贷款与净息差增长","中国再通胀向区域贸易扩散"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Reflation & Asia Trade Recovery","title_zh":"再通胀与亚洲贸易复苏","turn_id":"ews:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ews:peak:2018-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"EWS fell about 38% from January to March 2020 as COVID-19 disrupted global trade and triggered a severe risk-off flight. As a major Asian trade and financial hub, Singapore was acutely exposed to collapsing shipping and aviation volumes and weakening credit demand. The SGD fell against the USD safe-haven bid, amplifying the ETF's drawdown in dollar terms.","body_zh":"2020 年 1 月至 3 月，新冠疫情扰乱全球贸易并触发剧烈风险规避，EWS 跌幅约 38%。作为亚洲重要的贸易与金融枢纽，新加坡直接暴露于航运与航空量骤降及信贷需求走弱之中。新加坡元对美元避险买盘走弱，进一步放大了 EWS 的美元计价跌幅。","drivers":["COVID global trade disruption","Risk-off USD safe-haven spike","Weaker bank credit demand","Singapore aviation & logistics shock"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情扰乱全球贸易","美元避险需求飙升","银行信贷需求走弱","新加坡航空与物流受冲击"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"rekey_shift_days":68,"status":"shifted","title":"COVID Crash: Trade Hub Hit Hard","title_zh":"新冠冲击：贸易枢纽受重创","turn_id":"ews:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-08":{"body":"From late 2021 to October 2022, EWS dropped about 29% as the Fed's aggressive rate-hike cycle triggered broad EM outflows and valuation compression. While Singapore banks ultimately benefited from rising NIM, global risk-off dominated price action over this window. The ETF's financials-heavy composition could not offset the macro de-rating of Asia broadly.","body_zh":"2021 年末至 2022 年 10 月，联储激进加息触发新兴市场资金大规模外流及估值压缩，EWS 下跌约 29%。尽管新加坡银行最终受益于净息差上升，但此阶段价格走势由全球风险规避主导。ETF 以金融股为主的结构无法抵消亚洲整体估值重估的拖累。","drivers":["Fed aggressive rate-hike cycle","EM broad multiple compression","Asia risk-off capital outflows","Macro de-rating outweighed bank NIM gains"],"drivers_zh":["联储激进加息周期","新兴市场整体估值压缩","亚洲风险规避资本外流","宏观估值重估盖过银行净息差改善"],"prev_key":"2021-11","prev_key_chain":["2021-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate Shock & EM Outflows","title_zh":"加息冲击与新兴市场资金外流","turn_id":"ews:peak:2021-11"},"2022-10-24":{"body":"The 2022-2026 upcycle (+118%) is the strongest in EWS's 15-year history and remains technically intact as of June 2026 (recovery phase). Higher-for-longer US rates lifted Singapore bank net interest margins and earnings, while a broad recovery in global and regional risk appetite supported the financials-heavy index. The SGD traded in a stable-to-firm range versus the USD, limiting FX drag. As this leg extends into 2026 beyond reliable knowledge, recent strength is best read from the cycle data rather than specific catalysts.","body_zh":"2022 年 10 月至 2026 年 6 月的上涨周期累计涨幅约 118%，是 EWS 15 年窗口中最强的一轮，截至 2026 年 6 月技术形态仍未破（复苏阶段）。美国高息环境提振新加坡银行净息差与盈利，全球与区域风险偏好的广泛回升支撑了以金融股为主的指数。新加坡元对美元维持稳定偏强，汇率拖累有限。由于该段延伸至 2026 年、超出可靠认知范围，近期强势更宜依据周期数据而非具体催化剂解读。","drivers":["Higher-for-longer rates lifted bank NIM","Stronger Singapore bank earnings","Broad recovery in global/regional risk appetite","SGD stability vs USD limiting drag"],"drivers_zh":["高息环境提振银行净息差","新加坡银行盈利改善","全球/区域风险偏好广泛回升","新加坡元对美元稳定，汇率拖累有限"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate Peak Bonanza: Bank NIM Tailwind","title_zh":"利率高峰红利：银行净息差顺风","turn_id":"ews:trough:2022-10"}},"now":"EWS sits in a Recovery phase at position 24.4/100, having pulled back from its June 2026 cycle high while underperforming SPY by 5.8% over the past 63 days. The ETF still trades above its 200-day moving average, so the longer uptrend is intact, but the cycle model projects the next trough near December 2026, suggesting the current pullback phase may have further to run. The managed Singapore dollar has shown no strong appreciation versus USD, limiting the FX tailwind to dollar-denominated returns.","now_zh":"EWS 处于复苏阶段，位置读数 24.4/100，已自 2026 年 6 月的周期高点回落，近 63 日相对标普 500 落后约 5.8 个百分点。ETF 仍站在 200 日均线之上，长期上行趋势未破，但周期模型预计下一个低谷约在 2026 年 12 月，当前回调阶段可能尚未结束。受管理的新加坡元对美元缺乏明显升值动力，也限制了以美元计价 EWS 回报的汇率顺风。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewt":{"legs":{"2011-12-20":{"body":"After the 2011 global growth scare and euro-crisis selloff, Taiwan rebounded as rising smartphone penetration drove a sustained upgrade cycle for TSMC's advanced nodes. The Apple/iPhone supply chain lifted foundry utilisation through 2013-2014, and the TWD broadly firmed as inflows resumed. EWT rose about 65% over roughly three-and-a-half years as chip demand repeatedly beat down-cycle fears.","body_zh":"经历2011年全球增长恐慌与欧债危机抛售后，台湾市场随智能手机渗透率提升带动的台积电先进制程升级周期反弹。苹果/iPhone供应链在2013—2014年间拉动晶圆厂产能利用率，新台币随资本回流整体走强。芯片需求屡超下行预期，EWT在约三年半内上涨约65%。","drivers":["Apple iPhone supply-chain pull","TSMC 28nm node ramp","Emerging-market smartphone demand","TWD firming on inflows"],"prev_key":"2011-12","prev_key_chain":["2011-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis rebound, mobile chip up-cycle","title_zh":"危机后反弹，移动芯片上行周期","turn_id":"ewt:trough:2011-12"},"2015-04-27":{"body":"The June 2015 Chinese equity bubble burst and the PBoC's August 2015 RMB devaluation triggered a broad Asia risk-off that hit Taiwan as a high-beta proxy, while a semiconductor inventory correction emerged after years of mobile-driven over-ordering. The TWD weakened as foreign capital exited, amplifying a USD drawdown of about 30% over roughly four months.","body_zh":"2015年6月A股泡沫破裂及8月人民银行人民币贬值引发亚洲广泛风险规避，台湾作为高贝塔代理市场首当其冲；与此同时，移动端多年过度备货导致半导体库存调整浮现。新台币随外资撤离走弱，进一步放大美元计价跌幅，约四个月内回调约30%。","drivers":["China equity crash & RMB devaluation","Semiconductor inventory glut","TWD depreciation on capital outflows","Global growth scare"],"prev_key":"2015-04","prev_key_chain":["2015-04"],"status":"exact","title":"China shock & semiconductor inventory correction","title_zh":"中国冲击与半导体库存调整","turn_id":"ewt:peak:2015-04"},"2015-08-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewt:trough:2015-08"},"2015-11-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewt:peak:2015-11"},"2016-01-15":{"body":"A coordinated global reflation from early 2016 — stabilising oil, China credit stimulus, and a Fed pause — sparked a broad EM and tech rally. Taiwan benefited from accelerating cloud-infrastructure spend that drove server and HPC chip demand and lifted TSMC's high-margin 16/10nm nodes. The TWD strengthened as risk appetite returned, boosting USD returns; EWT rose more than 80% over two years.","body_zh":"2016年初全球协同再通胀——油价企稳、中国信贷刺激及美联储暂停加息——带动新兴市场与科技股广泛上涨。台湾受益于云基础设施支出加速，服务器与高性能计算芯片需求提升台积电16/10纳米高利润率节点。风险偏好回升推动新台币走强，放大美元回报，EWT两年内上涨逾80%。","drivers":["Cloud & hyperscaler server build-out","TSMC 16/10nm capacity ramp","Global synchronized recovery 2016-2017","TWD strength amplifying USD returns"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Server & HPC demand, synchronized global recovery","title_zh":"服务器与高性能计算需求，全球同步复苏","turn_id":"ewt:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewt:peak:2018-01"},"2019-01-03":{"body":"As the US-China trade war intensified through 2018, Taiwanese semiconductor and electronics firms benefited from supply-chain diversification away from mainland China, with customers shifting orders to Taiwan-based fabs and EMS providers as a hedge. EWT rose about 40% from early 2019 to early 2020 with USD/TWD relatively stable, and the leg ended as COVID-19 risk emerged in early 2020.","body_zh":"随着美中贸易战2018年升级，台湾半导体与电子企业受益于供应链自大陆转移的多元化需求，客户将订单转向台湾晶圆厂及EMS供应商以对冲风险。从2019年初至2020年初，EWT上涨约40%，美元/台币汇率相对稳定；随着2020年初新冠风险浮现，这一涨势结束。","drivers":["US-China trade-war supply-chain diversification","Pull-forward semiconductor orders","Stable TWD vs USD","5G pre-cycle inventory build"],"prev_key":"2019-01","prev_key_chain":["2019-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade-war supply-chain rerouting tailwind","title_zh":"贸易战供应链转移带来的顺风","turn_id":"ewt:trough:2019-01"},"2020-01-13":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewt:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-19":{"body":"From the March 2020 COVID low, Taiwan staged one of its strongest multi-year up-cycles in the 15-year window. The pandemic turbocharged demand for PCs, servers, 5G smartphones, and data-centre capacity, all funnelled through TSMC's advanced nodes, with revenue and margins reaching record levels through 2021. The TWD appreciated materially on surging inflows, amplifying USD returns; EWT more than doubled in under two years (~141%).","body_zh":"从2020年3月新冠低点起，台湾开启了15年窗口内最强劲的多年上行周期之一。疫情大幅刺激PC、服务器、5G智能手机及数据中心需求，均流经台积电先进制程节点，2021年营收与利润率升至历史新高。新台币随资本大量流入明显升值，放大美元回报，EWT在不足两年内涨幅超过一倍（约141%）。","drivers":["5G smartphone cycle","Remote-work PC/server demand surge","TSMC record margin expansion","TWD appreciation on foreign inflows"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID rebound: 5G & remote-work chip supercycle","title_zh":"疫情后反弹：5G与远程办公芯片超级周期","turn_id":"ewt:trough:2020-03"},"2022-01-04":{"body":"The Fed's aggressive 2022 rate-hiking cycle, combined with a classic semiconductor inventory correction as post-pandemic over-ordering reversed, drove Taiwan into a bear market. TSMC trimmed guidance as customers burned excess inventory, and the TWD weakened against the USD, adding to the drawdown. EWT fell about 39% peak-to-trough into October 2022.","body_zh":"美联储2022年激进加息周期，叠加疫情期间过度备货逆转引发的经典半导体库存调整，将台湾推入熊市。台积电下调展望，客户消化积压的过量库存，新台币对美元走弱进一步放大跌幅。EWT从峰值至2022年10月底部累计下跌约39%。","drivers":["Fed rate-hike cycle compressing tech multiples","Semiconductor inventory glut unwinding","TSMC guidance cuts","TWD depreciation amplifying USD drawdown"],"prev_key":"2022-01","prev_key_chain":["2022-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Rate shock & chip inventory-glut bear market","title_zh":"加息冲击与芯片库存过剩熊市","turn_id":"ewt:peak:2022-01"},"2022-10-24":{"body":"From the October 2022 trough, EWT rose about 82% to a mid-2024 peak as the generative-AI build-out created a new demand up-cycle. TSMC became the indispensable manufacturer for Nvidia, AMD, and hyperscaler custom silicon, driving N3/N5 node utilisation and record ASPs. Foreign inflows returned and the TWD partly retraced its 2022 losses; the leg ended in July 2024 amid rotation concerns.","body_zh":"从2022年10月底部起，EWT在生成式AI建设带来新需求上行周期的背景下上涨约82%至2024年中高点。台积电成为英伟达、AMD及超大规模云厂商定制芯片不可或缺的制造商，推动N3/N5节点产能利用率与平均售价创历史新高。外资回流，新台币部分收复2022年跌幅；该涨势于2024年7月在板块轮动担忧中结束。","drivers":["Generative-AI compute demand","TSMC N3/N5 node ramp for Nvidia/AMD","Hyperscaler custom-silicon orders","Partial TWD recovery"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"AI era begins: TSMC at the centre of the cycle","title_zh":"AI时代开启：台积电站上周期核心","turn_id":"ewt:trough:2022-10"},"2022-11-30":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewt:peak:2022-11"},"2022-12-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewt:trough:2022-12"},"2024-07-10":{"body":"EWT corrected about 26% from the July 2024 peak to April 2025. The selloff accelerated in early April 2025 when Trump's reciprocal-tariff announcement (a 32% rate on Taiwan) triggered a global risk-off; the TAIEX fell 9.7% in a single session on April 8, its largest one-day drop on record, as Taiwan reopened after a holiday. DeepSeek's efficiency claims had earlier raised doubts about the pace of AI capex, and TWD softness compounded the USD loss.","body_zh":"EWT从2024年7月高峰至2025年4月回调约26%。2025年4月初特朗普宣布对等关税（对台湾32%税率）引发全球风险规避，加速跌势；台湾加权指数在假期后复市，4月8日单日暴跌9.7%，为有记录以来最大单日跌幅。此前DeepSeek的效率说法已引发对AI资本开支节奏的质疑，新台币走弱进一步放大美元计价跌幅。","drivers":["US reciprocal-tariff shock (April 2025)","DeepSeek AI-efficiency concerns","Global risk-off de-risking","TWD weakness compounding USD loss"],"prev_key":"2024-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Mid-cycle AI pause and tariff shock","title_zh":"AI周期中段暂停与关税冲击","turn_id":"ewt:peak:2024-07"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From the April 2025 trough, EWT surged roughly 185% to the current peak as AI-infrastructure spending re-accelerated. TSMC posted strong revenue growth on robust AI-chip demand and crossed the US$2 trillion market-cap mark in February 2026, a first for Taiwan. Easing US-Taiwan tariff tensions restored foreign inflows and firmed the TWD, amplifying the USD move. As a leg ending mid-2026 — beyond reliably verifiable detail — the magnitude is taken from the cycle series and specific forward catalysts are kept cautious.","body_zh":"从2025年4月底部起，EWT在AI基础设施支出重新加速的背景下大涨约185%至当前高峰。台积电在强劲AI芯片需求下实现可观营收增长，并于2026年2月突破2万亿美元市值，为台湾首次。美台关税紧张缓和，外资回流并推动新台币走强，放大美元计价涨幅。该涨势延续至2026年中、超出可靠核实范围，故涨幅取自周期序列，对前瞻催化剂保持审慎表述。","drivers":["AI-infrastructure re-acceleration","Strong TSMC AI-chip revenue growth","TSMC crosses US$2T market cap (Feb 2026)","Easing US-Taiwan tariff tensions; firmer TWD"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"AI up-cycle resumes, record highs","title_zh":"AI上行周期重启，创历史新高","turn_id":"ewt:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"EWT sits at a cycle Peak (pos 89.9/100), near the top of its 15-year range, with Taiwan's market at record highs powered by the AI-driven semiconductor up-cycle anchored by TSMC. Relative strength vs SPY is strongly positive at +30.3% over the last 63 trading days, the second-strongest reading in the global coverage universe (rank 2 of 24). As a USD ETF, the return blends a powerful local-equity move with a broadly stable-to-firmer TWD. Total return is up ~564% since 2011 — the highest in the universe — so the market is stretched rather than washed out; the cycle projection points to a prospective trough around February 2027.","now_zh":"EWT目前处于周期高峰（位置89.9/100），接近15年区间顶部，台湾股市在以台积电为核心的AI半导体上行周期推动下创历史新高。过去63个交易日相对SPY的超额收益达+30.3%，位居全球覆盖市场（24个中第2）第二强。作为美元ETF，其回报同时反映强劲的本地股市表现与整体稳定偏强的新台币汇率。自2011年以来累计总回报约564%——为全球最高——故当前处于估值偏高而非超卖状态；周期模型预测约在2027年2月见底。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewu":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewu:trough:2011-10"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewu:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-25":{"body":"From late 2011 through July 2014, EWU rose 61.2% in USD terms as the eurozone sovereign debt crisis peaked and receded following Draghi's whatever it takes pledge in July 2012. The Bank of England held rates low and UK growth recovered, while the FTSE 100's commodity-heavy composition benefited from a still-buoyant commodity cycle. Sterling held relatively firm against the dollar, so the USD return tracked local equity gains without a major FX drag.","body_zh":"从2011年末至2014年7月，EWU以美元计上涨61.2%，欧元区主权债务危机在德拉基2012年7月不惜一切承诺后触顶回落。英格兰银行维持低利率，英国增长逐步复苏，富时100的大宗商品重仓股也受益于仍具韧性的大宗商品周期。英镑兑美元保持相对稳定，使美元收益与本地涨幅基本同步，汇率拖累有限。","drivers":["Draghi whatever it takes pledge removed eurozone tail risk","Bank of England low rates underpinned equities","Commodity cycle supported FTSE 100 energy and mining stocks","Sterling stability amplified local gains for USD investors"],"drivers_zh":["德拉基不惜一切承诺消除欧元区尾部风险","英格兰银行低利率支撑股市","大宗商品周期支撑富时100能源和矿业股","英镑稳定令美元投资者充分享受本地涨幅"],"prev_key":"2011-11","prev_key_chain":["2011-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis recovery, BoE QE tailwind","title_zh":"危机后复苏，英国央行量化宽松助力","turn_id":"ewu:trough:2011-11"},"2014-06-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewu:peak:2014-06"},"2015-01-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewu:trough:2015-01"},"2015-05-14":{"body":"From May 2015 to February 2016, EWU fell 25.9% in USD terms as Chinese growth fears triggered a global commodity rout that hit the FTSE 100's energy and mining heavyweights hard, with Brent crude falling below USD 30 per barrel in early 2016. Sterling also began softening as the EU referendum was scheduled and the campaign loomed, compounding equity losses for USD investors.","body_zh":"2015年5月至2016年2月，EWU以美元计下跌25.9%，中国增长担忧引发全球大宗商品抛售，重创富时100的能源和矿业权重股，布伦特原油在2016年初跌破每桶30美元。与此同时，随着脱欧公投确定举行、选战临近，英镑开始走软，进一步放大了美元投资者的股票亏损。","drivers":["China growth scare triggered global commodity selloff","Oil price collapse hit FTSE 100 energy majors","Approaching EU referendum began pressuring sterling","Weak GBP compounded losses for USD-denominated ETF"],"drivers_zh":["中国增长恐慌引发全球大宗商品抛售","油价暴跌冲击富时100能源巨头","脱欧公投临近开始压制英镑","弱英镑加大了美元计价ETF的损失"],"prev_key":"2015-05","prev_key_chain":["2015-05"],"status":"exact","title":"China slowdown and oil collapse weigh","title_zh":"中国放缓与油价崩跌压制行情","turn_id":"ewu:peak:2015-05"},"2016-02-11":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewu:trough:2016-02"},"2016-06-23":{"body":"From the June 2016 referendum low to January 2018, EWU recovered 42.9% in USD terms. The FTSE 100's large overseas earners saw their reported profits boosted by the weaker pound, and a synchronized global reflation through 2017, alongside firmer commodity prices, lifted the index. As sterling stabilized and partially retraced its post-vote drop, the FX headwind eased for USD investors.","body_zh":"从2016年6月公投低点至2018年1月，EWU以美元计回升42.9%。富时100中大量海外营收企业的报告利润因英镑走弱而获提振，2017年全球同步再通胀以及大宗商品价格回稳共同推升指数。随着英镑企稳并部分收复公投后跌幅，美元投资者面临的汇率逆风缓解。","drivers":["Weak pound boosted FTSE 100 overseas earners' reported profits","Synchronized global reflation through 2017 lifted equities","Firmer commodity prices supported energy and mining names","Sterling stabilized, easing the FX headwind for USD investors"],"drivers_zh":["弱英镑提振富时100海外营收企业的报告利润","2017年全球同步再通胀推升股市","大宗商品价格回稳支撑能源和矿业股","英镑企稳，缓解美元投资者的汇率逆风"],"prev_key":"2016-06","prev_key_chain":["2016-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Weak-pound earnings boost and global reflation","title_zh":"弱英镑提振盈利与全球再通胀","turn_id":"ewu:peak:2016-06"},"2016-06-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewu:trough:2016-06"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewu:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"From December 2018 to December 2019, EWU rose 25.0% in USD terms. Global equities recovered from the late-2018 Fed-tightening selloff after the US-China trade truce at the G20 and the Fed's pivot to rate cuts. UK sentiment improved when Boris Johnson's Conservatives won a roughly 80-seat majority in the December 2019 election on a Get Brexit Done platform, with sterling and domestic stocks rallying on the result as years of hung-parliament paralysis appeared resolved.","body_zh":"2018年12月至2019年12月，EWU以美元计上涨25.0%。美中贸易休战与美联储政策转向降息推动全球股市从2018年末下跌中回升。英国本地情绪则在约翰逊领导的保守党以完成脱欧为纲领于12月大选赢得约80席多数后改善，英镑和国内股票应声上涨，数年悬峙议会的僵局看似已告终结。","drivers":["US-China trade truce and Fed rate-cut pivot lifted global risk","Boris Johnson roughly 80-seat majority resolved Brexit paralysis","GBP and domestic stocks rallied on election clarity","Hung-parliament uncertainty lifted"],"drivers_zh":["美中贸易休战与美联储降息转向提振全球风险情绪","约翰逊约80席多数大胜打破脱欧僵局","政治明朗化推动英镑和国内股票上涨","悬峙议会的不确定性消除"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade truce rally, Brexit election clarity","title_zh":"贸易休战反弹，大选解除脱欧僵局","turn_id":"ewu:trough:2018-12"},"2019-12-16":{"body":"From December 2019 to March 2020, EWU fell 42.5% in USD terms. The COVID-19 pandemic triggered a synchronized global risk-off event; the FTSE 100's heavy energy and financial weighting made it especially vulnerable as oil prices collapsed alongside the Saudi-Russia price war. Sterling fell sharply in the global dash for dollars, compounding the equity decline into one of the steepest short-term drawdowns in the ETF's history.","body_zh":"2019年12月至2020年3月，EWU以美元计重挫42.5%。新冠疫情引发全球同步风险规避，富时100的能源和金融重仓使其尤为脆弱，沙特-俄罗斯价格战推动油价崩溃更是雪上加霜。全球抢购美元浪潮中英镑大幅下跌，进一步放大股票跌幅，造就了该ETF历史上最急剧的短期回撤之一。","drivers":["COVID-19 global risk-off triggered synchronized DM selloff","Oil price collapse hit FTSE 100 energy heavyweights","Saudi-Russia price war coincided with demand destruction","Flight to USD compressed sterling, amplifying ETF losses"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情引发全球同步风险规避","油价崩溃重创富时100能源权重股","沙特-俄罗斯价格战与需求崩塌同步爆发","抢购美元压低英镑，放大ETF跌幅"],"prev_key":"2019-12","prev_key_chain":["2019-12"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash amplified by dollar flight","title_zh":"新冠暴跌因抢购美元而加剧","turn_id":"ewu:peak:2019-12"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From March 2020 to February 2022, EWU surged 89.7% in USD terms. Massive fiscal and monetary stimulus, an early UK vaccine rollout, and a strong commodity rebound on the reopening of global supply chains lifted the FTSE 100, with energy majors and miners leading. Sterling recovered as the UK growth outlook improved, augmenting the USD return for foreign investors.","body_zh":"2020年3月至2022年2月，EWU以美元计大涨89.7%。大规模财政与货币刺激、英国较早推进的疫苗接种，以及全球供应链重开带动的大宗商品强劲反弹共同推升富时100，能源巨头和矿商领涨。英镑随英国增长前景改善而回升，进一步提升了外国投资者的美元收益。","drivers":["Massive global fiscal and monetary stimulus post-COVID","Early UK vaccine rollout supported domestic recovery","Commodity rebound lifted FTSE 100 energy and mining stocks","Sterling recovery added to USD returns"],"drivers_zh":["后新冠时代大规模全球财政与货币刺激","英国较早推进疫苗接种支撑国内复苏","大宗商品反弹提振富时100能源和矿业股","英镑回升增厚美元收益"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Vaccine-led recovery and commodity rebound","title_zh":"疫苗驱动复苏与大宗商品回升","turn_id":"ewu:trough:2020-03"},"2020-06-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewu:peak:2020-06"},"2020-10-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewu:trough:2020-10"},"2022-02-09":{"body":"From February 2022 to September 2022, EWU fell 24.9% in USD terms. Surging global inflation triggered aggressive rate hikes, and the UK suffered a unique additional shock: Liz Truss's September 2022 mini-budget of unfunded tax cuts sent gilt yields spiking, forced emergency Bank of England bond purchases, and pushed sterling to a historic low near 1.035 against the dollar in late September. The twin gilt and GBP collapse inflicted a severe USD-denominated loss even though the FTSE 100 itself was partly insulated by its overseas commodity revenues.","body_zh":"2022年2月至2022年9月，EWU以美元计下跌24.9%。全球通胀飙升引发激进加息，英国还遭受独特的额外冲击：特拉斯9月提出的无资金来源减税迷你预算令英国国债收益率飙升，迫使英格兰银行紧急购债干预，英镑也于9月底跌至约1.035的历史低位。英国国债与英镑的双重崩溃给美元计价收益带来重创，尽管富时100本身因海外大宗商品收入而部分绝缘。","drivers":["Global inflation surge and aggressive central bank rate hikes","Truss mini-budget sent gilt yields spiking","GBP/USD hit historic low near 1.035 in late September 2022","BoE emergency gilt-purchase intervention"],"drivers_zh":["全球通胀飙升与央行激进加息","特拉斯迷你预算令英国国债收益率飙升","GBP/USD在2022年9月底触及约1.035的历史低位","英格兰银行紧急购买英国国债干预市场"],"prev_key":"2022-02","prev_key_chain":["2022-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Truss mini-budget: gilt and pound crisis","title_zh":"特拉斯迷你预算：英国国债与英镑危机","turn_id":"ewu:peak:2022-02"},"2022-09-27":{"body":"From September 2022 to February 2026, EWU gained 117.5% in USD terms, its largest sustained advance in the 15-year window. The gilt crisis was resolved rapidly after Truss resigned and a new government restored fiscal credibility; sterling rebounded sharply off its lows. Elevated commodity prices supported the FTSE 100 through 2022-2023, and as UK inflation cooled the rate backdrop eased. Into 2025 a softer dollar provided an additional FX tailwind that compressed the structural UK discount, lifting USD returns above local equity gains before the February 2026 peak.","body_zh":"2022年9月至2026年2月，EWU以美元计上涨117.5%，是过去15年最大的持续性涨势。特拉斯辞职、新政府恢复财政公信力后，英国国债危机迅速化解，英镑从低位大幅反弹。2022至2023年间高企的大宗商品价格支撑富时100；随着英国通胀降温，利率环境趋于宽松。进入2025年，美元走软提供了额外的汇率顺风，收窄了英国结构性折价，令美元收益率在2026年2月见顶前超越本地股票涨幅。","drivers":["Truss exit and restored fiscal credibility lifted GBP and gilts","Elevated commodity prices 2022-2023 supported FTSE 100","Cooling UK inflation eased the rate backdrop","Softer dollar into 2025 added an FX tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["特拉斯离任与财政公信力修复推动英镑和英国国债回升","2022至2023年高企的大宗商品价格支撑富时100","英国通胀降温缓解利率环境","2025年美元走软形成汇率顺风"],"prev_key":"2022-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis stabilization and multi-year recovery","title_zh":"危机后稳定与多年复苏","turn_id":"ewu:trough:2022-09"}},"now":"EWU sits at the extreme low end of its cycle range (position 1.3 out of 100), the most washed-out reading among tracked developed markets despite still trading above its 200-day average. The ETF peaked in February 2026 and has since lagged, with relative strength of -9.2% versus SPY over the past 63 trading days, ranking 16th of all markets. The FTSE 100's defensive, commodity, and financial tilt has not been enough to offset sterling softness and a global rotation toward US and Asian equities; the cycle model projects a trough around July 2026.","now_zh":"EWU目前处于周期区间的极低端（位置1.3/100），是被追踪的发达市场中最被抛售的标的，尽管仍位于200日均线上方。该ETF于2026年2月见顶后表现落后，过去63个交易日相对标普500的强度为-9.2%，在所有追踪市场中排名第16。英镑走软与全球资金转向美股及亚洲股市，抵消了富时100能源、金融等防御性板块的支撑；周期模型预计将在2026年7月前后触底。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"eww":{"legs":{"2011-09-22":{"body":"From September 2011 Mexico entered a multi-year bull run as Enrique Pena Nieto's presidential campaign and 2012 election win ignited expectations of structural reforms in energy, telecom, and labor. The US manufacturing cycle was firming and the peso held broadly steady against the dollar, supporting USD returns on EWW. The 65.5% gain over roughly 19 months reflected both solid local equity performance and a stable currency, making it one of Mexico's better sustained EM rallies of the decade.","body_zh":"自2011年9月起，随着培尼亚·涅托的总统竞选及2012年当选点燃市场对能源、电信和劳动力结构性改革的预期，墨西哥进入多年牛市。美国制造业周期回暖，比索兑美元大体稳定，支撑了EWW的美元回报。约19个月内65.5%的涨幅既体现本地股市稳健表现，也得益于稳定的汇率，是墨西哥本十年较好的持续性新兴市场行情之一。","drivers":["Structural reform optimism under Pena Nieto","Stable MXN against the dollar","US manufacturing recovery demand","EM risk-on inflows"],"drivers_zh":["培尼亚·涅托执政下的结构性改革预期","比索兑美元保持稳定","美国制造业复苏需求","新兴市场风险偏好资金流入"],"prev_key":"2011-09","prev_key_chain":["2011-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Pena Nieto reform optimism rally","title_zh":"培尼亚·涅托改革预期驱动上涨","turn_id":"eww:trough:2011-09"},"2013-04-11":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:peak:2013-04"},"2013-06-20":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:trough:2013-06"},"2014-09-05":{"body":"Brent crude collapsed from above $100 in mid-2014 to below $30 by early 2016, hammering Mexico's fiscal accounts given that oil historically supplied roughly a third of public-sector revenue. The peso depreciated sharply, sliding from around 13 per USD in 2014 toward 19-20 per USD by late 2016 — a move that drove EWW's 37.6% USD-denominated decline even as local equities held up better in peso terms. Trump's surprise election in November 2016 added a further shock, with the peso falling roughly 11-13% within days on fears of NAFTA termination.","body_zh":"2014年中至2016年初，布伦特原油从逾100美元/桶崩跌至30美元以下，重创墨西哥财政——石油历史上约占公共部门收入三分之一。比索大幅贬值，从2014年约13比索兑1美元滑向2016年底约19-20比索，这一走势推动EWW以美元计价下跌37.6%，即便以比索计价的本地股市跌幅相对较小。2016年11月特朗普意外当选带来额外冲击，市场担忧NAFTA终止，比索数日内下跌约11-13%。","drivers":["Oil price collapse draining fiscal revenues","Sharp MXN depreciation","US rate normalization reducing EM inflows","Trump election NAFTA shock"],"drivers_zh":["油价崩跌侵蚀财政收入","比索大幅贬值","美国利率正常化减少新兴市场资金流入","特朗普当选引发NAFTA冲击"],"prev_key":"2014-09","prev_key_chain":["2014-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Oil crash and peso rout","title_zh":"油价崩跌与比索暴跌","turn_id":"eww:peak:2014-09"},"2016-01-21":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:trough:2016-01"},"2016-03-30":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:peak:2016-03"},"2017-01-19":{"body":"After the post-election panic, EWW recovered sharply through mid-2017 as it became clear the US was seeking to renegotiate rather than scrap NAFTA. The peso stabilized and partially retraced its Trump-shock losses, boosting USD returns on EWW. The 39.5% gain through August 2017 was largely a currency-normalization trade compounded by resilient local consumption, before renegotiation uncertainty reasserted itself later in the year.","body_zh":"选举冲击后的恐慌情绪消退，随着美国明确寻求重谈而非废除NAFTA，EWW在2017年中前大幅反弹。比索企稳并部分回吐特朗普冲击跌幅，推升EWW美元回报。至2017年8月止录得39.5%涨幅，主要是汇率正常化行情叠加本地消费韧性，此后重谈不确定性在年内再度压制市场。","drivers":["Peso stabilization and partial recovery","NAFTA framed as renegotiation, not termination","EM risk appetite recovery","Domestic consumption resilience"],"drivers_zh":["比索企稳并部分回升","NAFTA定位为重谈而非废除","新兴市场风险偏好回升","本地消费韧性"],"prev_key":"2017-01","prev_key_chain":["2017-01"],"status":"exact","title":"NAFTA relief rally, peso stabilizes","title_zh":"NAFTA前景缓和，比索趋稳反弹","turn_id":"eww:trough:2017-01"},"2017-08-25":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:peak:2017-08"},"2018-06-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:trough:2018-06"},"2018-08-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:peak:2018-08"},"2018-11-26":{"body":"After AMLO won Mexico's July 2018 election and the USMCA was signed in late November 2018, trade and political uncertainty eased. Investors took comfort in USMCA continuity while Banxico's high policy rates limited further peso depreciation. EWW rallied 32.2% through January 2020, aided by relative peso stability and steady US demand for Mexican manufactured goods.","body_zh":"2018年7月AMLO赢得大选，同年11月底USMCA签署，贸易与政治不确定性缓解。USMCA延续性令投资者安心，墨西哥央行的高政策利率也抑制了比索进一步贬值。至2020年1月，EWW累计上涨32.2%，受益于比索相对稳定及美国对墨西哥制造品的持续需求。","drivers":["USMCA signed, removing termination risk","Banxico high real rates supporting MXN","US demand for Mexican goods","Reduced political tail risk post-election"],"drivers_zh":["USMCA签署消除终止风险","墨西哥央行高实际利率支撑比索","美国对墨西哥商品的需求","选后政治尾部风险下降"],"prev_key":"2018-11","prev_key_chain":["2018-11"],"status":"exact","title":"USMCA certainty lifts market","title_zh":"USMCA落地提振市场信心","turn_id":"eww:trough:2018-11"},"2019-04-17":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:peak:2019-04"},"2019-08-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:trough:2019-08"},"2020-01-17":{"body":"The COVID-19 pandemic triggered a 47.7% drawdown from January to March 2020, among the sharpest of any country ETF in this window. The peso collapsed to record lows near 25 per USD, compounding local equity losses. Mexico was additionally exposed as a delayed fiscal response and disrupted tourism and remittance flows coincided with the global manufacturing halt.","body_zh":"新冠疫情从2020年1月至3月触发高达47.7%的回撤，是同期各国ETF中跌幅最大之一。比索崩跌至约25比索兑1美元的历史低位，放大了本地股市跌幅。此外，财政应对迟缓、旅游业与汇款收入受扰，叠加全球制造业停摆，令墨西哥所受冲击尤为严重。","drivers":["COVID-19 global demand shock","MXN collapse to record lows near 25/USD","Delayed fiscal response","Tourism and remittance revenue disruption"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情全球需求冲击","比索崩跌至约25兑1美元历史低位","财政应对迟缓","旅游业与汇款收入受扰"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash, peso collapse","title_zh":"新冠冲击，比索急剧崩跌","turn_id":"eww:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"EWW surged 128.7% from March 2020 to April 2022 as the global reopening trade benefited Mexico's export-oriented manufacturing base. US-China trade tensions accelerated nearshoring interest, with FDI picking up and industrial-park vacancy rates falling. The peso recovered meaningfully from its crisis lows, amplifying USD returns, as Mexico's role in US supply chains expanded and it moved toward becoming the US's largest trading partner.","body_zh":"从2020年3月至2022年4月，EWW累计上涨128.7%，全球重开行情令墨西哥以出口为导向的制造业基地受益。美中贸易紧张加速近岸转移意愿，外商直接投资回升，工业园区空置率下降。比索从危机低点显著回升，放大了美元回报；墨西哥在美国供应链中的地位上升，并逐步迈向美国最大贸易伙伴。","drivers":["Global reopening boosts Mexican manufacturing exports","US-China tensions accelerate nearshoring FDI","MXN recovery from crisis lows","Mexico's rising role in US supply chains"],"drivers_zh":["全球重开提振墨西哥制造业出口","美中紧张加速近岸直接投资","比索从危机低点回升","墨西哥在美国供应链中地位上升"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-COVID reopening and nearshoring boom","title_zh":"疫后重开与近岸制造业热潮","turn_id":"eww:trough:2020-03"},"2022-04-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eww:peak:2022-04"},"2022-09-26":{"body":"From September 2022 to April 2024, EWW rallied 68.1% on the widely-followed nearshoring theme. The peso appreciated to multi-year highs as Mexico's current account was supported by strong manufacturing FDI and record remittances, while Banxico's real rates stayed among the highest in EM. The rally was concentrated in industrial, financial, and consumer names tied to supply-chain relocation, and MXN strength was a major additive to USD returns.","body_zh":"从2022年9月至2024年4月，EWW上涨68.1%，近岸制造业主题广受关注。比索升至多年高位，得益于制造业外商直接投资强劲及创纪录的汇款收入支撑经常账户，同时墨西哥央行实际利率仍居新兴市场前列。行情集中于与供应链转移相关的工业、金融和消费板块，比索走强对美元回报贡献显著。","drivers":["Nearshoring FDI wave drives industrial investment","MXN appreciation to multi-year highs","Record remittance inflows support current account","Banxico high real rates attract carry flows"],"drivers_zh":["近岸直接投资浪潮带动工业投资","比索升至多年高位","创纪录汇款流入支撑经常账户","墨西哥央行高实际利率吸引套利资金"],"prev_key":"2022-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Nearshoring secular rally, strong peso","title_zh":"近岸制造业长线牛市，比索走强","turn_id":"eww:trough:2022-09"},"2024-04-08":{"body":"EWW fell 31.2% from April to December 2024. Claudia Sheinbaum's June 2024 landslide, which handed the ruling Morena coalition a qualified majority capable of passing constitutional reforms, spooked markets over a controversial judicial overhaul. The peso slid roughly 4% the day after the result and continued weakening over subsequent weeks (the iShares Mexico ETF itself closed about 10% lower in one session), with MXN weakness the primary driver of EWW's USD loss even as local equities fell less in peso terms.","body_zh":"2024年4月至12月，EWW下跌31.2%。2024年6月谢因鲍姆压倒性胜选，使执政的莫雷纳联盟获得可通过宪法改革的合格多数，市场对争议性司法改革感到不安。选举结果次日比索下跌约4%，并在随后数周持续走弱（iShares墨西哥ETF本身单日收跌约10%），比索走弱是EWW美元跌幅的主要驱动力，即便以比索计价的本地股市跌幅较小。","drivers":["Morena qualified majority raises reform risk","MXN sell-off after the election result","Judicial reform uncertainty deters FDI","Nearshoring thesis challenged by policy risk"],"drivers_zh":["莫雷纳合格多数加剧改革风险","选举结果后比索下挫","司法改革不确定性打压外商投资","政策风险动摇近岸主题"],"prev_key":"2024-04","prev_key_chain":["2024-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Election shock and nearshoring doubt","title_zh":"大选冲击与近岸预期动摇","turn_id":"eww:peak:2024-04"},"2024-12-30":{"body":"EWW bounced 80.5% from December 2024 to February 2026 in a sharp recovery from deeply oversold levels, helped by a partly stabilizing peso and relief that the most extreme reforms were not immediately enacted. But the second Trump administration's 2025 tariff actions created an overhang: 25% IEEPA tariffs on Mexican imports were imposed in early 2025, with USMCA-compliant goods later carved out, leaving recurring escalation risk. The move reads as a relief rally within a challenged medium-term backdrop rather than a new structural bull market; the market has since rolled back into a trough reading.","body_zh":"从2024年12月至2026年2月，EWW从深度超卖水平急剧反弹80.5%，受比索部分企稳及最极端改革未立即落地的宽慰提振。但特朗普第二任期2025年的关税行动构成压制：2025年初依IEEPA对墨西哥进口加征25%关税，其后对USMCA合规商品予以豁免，但反复升级的风险犹存。此轮上涨更像是中期承压背景下的技术性救援反弹，而非新一轮结构性牛市；此后市场已回落至谷底读数。","drivers":["Technical rebound from deeply oversold cycle low","MXN partial stabilization","Most extreme reforms not immediately enacted","Trump 2025 tariff actions create a recurring overhang"],"drivers_zh":["从深度超卖周期低点技术性反弹","比索部分企稳","最极端改革未立即落地","特朗普2025年关税行动构成持续压制"],"prev_key":"2024-12","prev_key_chain":["2024-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Technical rebound, tariff clouds build","title_zh":"技术性反弹，关税阴云聚集","turn_id":"eww:trough:2024-12"}},"now":"EWW reads as a cycle Trough (pos 4.5/100): after an 80%-plus rebound that peaked in February 2026, the ETF has rolled over and given back enough ground to register a fresh oversold cycle low, though it still sits above its 200-day average. It has lagged SPY by roughly 8 percentage points over the past 63 days, pressured by a softer Mexican peso and the tariff overhang from the second Trump administration. The nearshoring optimism that powered the 2022-2024 rally has cooled as USMCA-compliance friction and judicial-reform uncertainty weigh on fresh foreign direct investment. At this depth the tape is washed out, but a firmer peso or tariff de-escalation would be needed to confirm a new up-leg.","now_zh":"EWW当前处于周期谷底（位置4.5/100）：在一轮逾80%的反弹于2026年2月见顶后，该ETF回落并跌出新的超卖周期低点读数，但仍位于200日均线上方。过去63个交易日中，它相对标普500跑输约8个百分点，受比索走软及特朗普第二任期关税阴云施压。此前2022至2024年间支撑行情的近岸制造业热潮已降温，USMCA合规摩擦及司法改革不确定性打压了新增外商直接投资。从周期深度看技术面已超卖，但若缺乏比索企稳或关税缓和，新一轮上升行情难以确认。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewy":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"body":"After the August-September 2011 global equity rout (Eurozone debt crisis and US credit-rating downgrade), risk assets rebounded. Korea's export-oriented, memory-heavy economy benefited and EWY gained about 46% in USD terms into early 2013. The KRW stabilized and gradually firmed as capital returned to Asian EM, supporting the dollar-translated gain.","body_zh":"2011年8-9月欧债危机及美国主权评级下调引发全球股市暴跌后，风险资产开启反弹。韩国出口导向、内存权重高的经济体受益，EWY美元涨幅约46%，延续至2013年初。随着资金回流亚洲新兴市场，韩元企稳并逐步走强，支撑了美元换算收益。","drivers":["Global risk-on rebound","Memory/export recovery","KRW stabilization","Asian EM capital inflows"],"drivers_zh":["全球风险偏好回升","内存/出口复苏","韩元企稳","亚洲新兴市场资金流入"],"prev_key":"2011-10","prev_key_chain":["2011-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-Euro-crisis global recovery","title_zh":"欧债危机后全球复苏","turn_id":"ewy:trough:2011-10"},"2013-01-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewy:peak:2013-01"},"2013-06-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewy:trough:2013-06"},"2014-07-30":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewy:peak:2014-07"},"2015-08-24":{"body":"From the August 2015 trough (around the China yuan-devaluation shock), EWY advanced about 89% through January 2018 -- the largest pre-AI upcycle. The core driver was a DRAM/NAND shortage supercycle: tight supply sent memory prices to multi-year highs through 2017, powering record Samsung earnings. Synchronized global expansion and a reflation trade lifted EM assets, while a firming KRW added a currency tailwind.","body_zh":"自2015年8月低点（约人民币贬值冲击前后）起，EWY涨幅约89%，延续至2018年1月，是AI时代之前最大的上升周期。核心驱动力是DRAM/NAND供给短缺超级周期：供给偏紧推动内存价格在2017年涨至多年高位，带动三星创纪录盈利。全球经济同步扩张与再通胀交易推升新兴市场资产，韩元走强亦提供汇率顺风。","drivers":["DRAM/NAND shortage supercycle","Record Samsung earnings","Global synchronized expansion","KRW firming"],"drivers_zh":["DRAM/NAND供给短缺超级周期","三星创纪录盈利","全球同步经济扩张","韩元走强"],"prev_key":"2015-08","prev_key_chain":["2015-08"],"status":"exact","title":"DRAM/NAND supercycle, KOSPI strength","title_zh":"DRAM/NAND超级周期，KOSPI走强","turn_id":"ewy:trough:2015-08"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewy:peak:2018-01"},"2019-08-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewy:trough:2019-08"},"2020-01-13":{"body":"From January to March 2020, EWY fell roughly 39% as the COVID-19 pandemic triggered a global risk-off liquidation. Korea was among the first countries outside China to report significant community spread (late February 2020), adding to the panic. The KRW depreciated against the dollar as EM capital fled to safety, magnifying the local KOSPI decline in USD terms.","body_zh":"2020年1月至3月，新冠疫情引发全球风险规避式清仓，EWY跌幅约39%。韩国是中国以外最早出现大规模社区传播的国家之一（2020年2月下旬），加剧了恐慌。新兴市场资金出逃避险，韩元对美元贬值，将KOSPI本地跌幅放大为美元层面更深的回撤。","drivers":["COVID pandemic shock","EM capital flight","KRW depreciation","Global liquidity stress"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情冲击","新兴市场资本外逃","韩元贬值","全球流动性承压"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash, EM capital flight","title_zh":"新冠暴跌，新兴市场资本外逃","turn_id":"ewy:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From the March 2020 trough, EWY surged about 149% into January 2021, driven by a historic domestic retail-participation wave (Korean retail investors, the self-styled 'ants'/gaeimi), massive global fiscal and monetary stimulus, and a work-from-home tech-demand boom that lifted server DRAM and NAND. The KRW recovered sharply as the dollar weakened, amplifying EWY's USD returns beyond the KOSPI's own gains.","body_zh":"自2020年3月低点起，EWY大涨约149%，延续至2021年1月。驱动因素包括史无前例的国内散户参与浪潮（自称\"蚂蚁\"的韩国散户）、全球大规模财政与货币刺激，以及居家办公带动的科技需求爆发，提振服务器DRAM与NAND。随着美元走弱，韩元大幅回升，EWY美元收益率超越KOSPI本地涨幅。","drivers":["Domestic retail 'ants' wave","Global stimulus / low rates","Server DRAM & NAND demand","KRW recovery on weak dollar"],"drivers_zh":["国内散户\"蚂蚁\"浪潮","全球刺激/低利率","服务器DRAM与NAND需求","美元走弱下韩元回升"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID recovery, retail wave, chip demand","title_zh":"新冠复苏、散户浪潮与芯片需求","turn_id":"ewy:trough:2020-03"},"2021-01-08":{"body":"EWY fell roughly 50% from January 2021 to September 2022 as headwinds compounded. Memory demand normalized after the pandemic boom while supply expanded, starting a multi-quarter inventory correction. The Fed pivoted aggressively to rate hikes from early 2022, driving dollar strength and EM outflows -- the KRW weakened toward multi-year lows near 1,440/USD, directly cutting EWY's dollar returns. Samsung's earnings fell as DRAM and NAND prices declined into 2022-2023.","body_zh":"2021年1月至2022年9月，EWY累计下跌约50%，多重逆风叠加。内存需求在疫情高峰后正常化，同期供给扩张，开启多季度库存去化。美联储自2022年初激进加息，推动美元走强、新兴市场资金外流——韩元贬至1440/美元附近的多年低位，直接侵蚀EWY美元收益。随着DRAM与NAND价格在2022-2023年下行，三星盈利下滑。","drivers":["Memory inventory downcycle","Fed tightening / dollar surge","KRW to multi-year lows","EM capital outflows"],"drivers_zh":["内存库存去化周期","美联储紧缩/美元飙升","韩元贬至多年低位","新兴市场资本外流"],"prev_key":"2021-01","prev_key_chain":["2021-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Memory downcycle, Fed tightening bear","title_zh":"内存下行周期叠加美联储紧缩熊市","turn_id":"ewy:peak:2021-01"},"2022-09-30":{"body":"From the September 2022 trough, EWY gained about 51% into mid-2024 as the memory inventory cycle bottomed. Samsung and SK Hynix cut production in early 2023 to normalize inventory, and the late-2022 emergence of generative AI seeded demand for high-bandwidth memory (HBM) used in AI accelerators. A modestly weaker dollar provided a partial KRW tailwind, though Korea lagged some EM peers as the HBM ramp took time to reach earnings.","body_zh":"自2022年9月低点起，EWY反弹约51%，延续至2024年中，内存库存周期触底是主要背景。三星与SK海力士于2023年初减产以正常化库存，而2022年底生成式AI的兴起为AI加速器所需的高带宽内存（HBM）播下需求种子。美元温和走弱提供部分韩元顺风，但因HBM产能爬坡需时间反映至盈利，韩国一度跑输部分新兴市场同侪。","drivers":["Memory inventory bottoming","Production cuts (Samsung/SK Hynix)","Early HBM/AI demand","Partial dollar weakening"],"drivers_zh":["内存库存触底","三星/SK海力士减产","HBM/AI需求萌芽","美元小幅走弱"],"prev_key":"2022-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Memory trough recovery, HBM/AI seeds","title_zh":"内存触底复苏，HBM/AI萌芽","turn_id":"ewy:trough:2022-09"},"2024-07-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewy:peak:2024-07"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From April 2025, EWY surged about 216% into February 2026, the most explosive leg in its history, as an AI-driven HBM supercycle made SK Hynix and Samsung core suppliers to the generative-AI buildout and helped reverse the long-standing 'Korea discount.' Political stabilization after the December 2024 martial-law crisis and subsequent impeachment removed a major overhang, and the KRW recovered from its martial-law lows, compounding USD gains. The KOSPI set successive record highs as global institutions re-rated Korea as an AI-infrastructure play.","body_zh":"自2025年4月起，EWY大涨约216%直至2026年2月，成为其历史上最剧烈的一轮上涨。AI驱动的高带宽内存超级周期使SK海力士与三星成为生成式AI基础设施的核心供应商，并推动长期\"折价\"逆转。2024年12月戒严危机及随后弹劾后政治局势企稳，消除重大不确定性，韩元从戒严低点回升，进一步放大美元收益。KOSPI接连创历史新高，全球机构将韩国重估为\"AI基础设施标的\"。","drivers":["HBM chip supercycle (AI buildout)","'Korea discount' re-rating","Political stabilization post-crisis","KRW recovery amplifying USD returns"],"drivers_zh":["高带宽内存超级周期（AI基础设施）","\"韩国折价\"重估","危机后政治局势企稳","韩元回升放大美元收益"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"AI HBM supercycle, KOSPI to records","title_zh":"AI高带宽内存超级周期，KOSPI创新高","turn_id":"ewy:trough:2025-04"},"2026-02-27":{"body":"After the record AI rally, EWY pulled back about 23% from February to March 2026 as stretched valuations met profit-taking. With Samsung and SK Hynix together over half of index market cap, the index's extreme two-stock concentration amplified the drawdown. A modestly weaker KRW added to the USD-level decline. This was a sharp but contained correction within an ongoing uptrend rather than a cycle break.","body_zh":"在创纪录的AI行情后，EWY自2026年2月至3月回调约23%，估值拉伸遭遇获利了结。由于三星与SK海力士合计占指数市值逾半，极端的两只个股集中度放大了回撤。韩元温和走弱进一步加大美元层面跌幅。此为上行趋势中急促但有限的修正，而非周期反转。","drivers":["Profit-taking after extreme run-up","Stretched valuations","Two-stock concentration amplifying drawdown","Mild KRW weakness"],"drivers_zh":["极端涨幅后获利了结","估值拉伸","两只个股集中度放大跌幅","韩元温和走弱"],"prev_key":"2026-02","prev_key_chain":["2026-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Profit-taking pullback","title_zh":"获利了结回调","turn_id":"ewy:peak:2026-02"},"2026-03-30":{"body":"From the March 2026 trough, EWY rebounded about 88% into June 2026, retracing the pullback and extending to new highs on continued strength in the AI/HBM memory theme. The magnitude and speed -- nearly doubling in three months -- reflect the index's extreme concentration in two memory names, which leverages moves in both directions. As of late June 2026 the index sits at position 79.9 in Peak territory with the leg looking mature; the dominant risk is a turn in memory pricing/earnings expectations given how much of the index rides on two stocks.","body_zh":"自2026年3月低点起，EWY反弹约88%至2026年6月，收复回调并延伸至新高，AI/HBM内存主题持续强势。近三个月几乎翻倍的幅度与速度，折射出指数高度集中于两只内存龙头、双向放大波动的特征。截至2026年6月下旬，位置值79.9处于顶峰区间，本轮波段已显成熟；主要风险在于内存定价/盈利预期出现转折，因指数走势高度依赖两只个股。","drivers":["Continued AI/HBM memory strength","KOSPI record momentum","Extreme two-stock concentration amplifying moves","Mature-leg / memory-cycle risk"],"drivers_zh":["AI/HBM内存持续强势","KOSPI创纪录动能","两只龙头高度集中放大波动","波段成熟/内存周期风险"],"prev_key":"2026-03","prev_key_chain":["2026-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Re-acceleration to fresh highs","title_zh":"再加速创新高","turn_id":"ewy:trough:2026-03"}},"now":"EWY sits at a cycle Peak with position 79.9/100, having rebounded roughly 88% off its March 2026 trough in just three months -- one of the fastest re-accelerations in its history. It is the top relative-strength performer in the country-ETF universe, outpacing SPY by nearly 40 percentage points over the trailing 63 days, driven by an AI-memory (HBM) upcycle that has made SK Hynix and Samsung -- together more than half of KOSPI market cap -- the focal point of global flows. That same concentration is the key fragility: with two semiconductor names dominating the index, the upside is leveraged but so is the downside if memory earnings expectations wobble. Currency is a permanent amplifier -- KRW strength boosts EWY's USD return, while KRW weakness (as during the December 2024 martial-law shock, when the won fell toward 1,440-1,480/USD) cuts into dollar performance.","now_zh":"EWY目前处于周期顶峰，位置值79.9/100，自2026年3月低点以来仅三个月便反弹约88%，是其历史上最急速的再加速之一。该ETF是国家ETF体系中相对强度排名第一的市场，过去63个交易日跑赢SPY近40个百分点，核心驱动力是AI内存（HBM）上行周期——SK海力士与三星合计占KOSPI市值逾半，成为全球资金汇聚的焦点。这一高度集中正是关键脆弱点：两只半导体龙头主导指数，使涨幅被杠杆化放大，但内存盈利预期一旦动摇，跌幅亦会被同等放大。汇率是永久性放大器——韩元升值提升EWY美元回报，而韩元贬值（如2024年12月戒严冲击期间韩元贬至约1440-1480/美元）则侵蚀美元收益。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ewz":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2011-10"},"2012-03-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2012-03"},"2013-08-21":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2013-08"},"2013-10-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2013-10"},"2014-02-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2014-02"},"2014-09-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2014-09"},"2015-03-13":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2015-03"},"2015-05-08":{"body":"From May 2015, EWZ fell 52% to January 2016 as Operation Car Wash (Lava Jato) engulfed Petrobras and the ruling PT, triggering Brazil's deepest recession in decades. Commodity prices were collapsing simultaneously — iron ore and crude oil both near multi-year lows — while the BRL lost roughly a third of its value against the dollar over 2015, compounding USD losses far beyond the local-equity damage. This combined political implosion, commodity bust, and currency crisis into one of the deepest troughs of the modern EWZ era.","body_zh":"2015年5月起，随着洗车行动（Lava Jato）吞噬巴西国家石油公司与劳工党，并引发巴西数十年来最严重的经济衰退，EWZ下跌52%至2016年1月。与此同时，大宗商品价格齐跌——铁矿石与原油均在多年低位——而雷亚尔在2015年对美元贬值约三分之一，使美元计价损失远超本币跌幅。政治崩塌、大宗商品熊市与货币危机同步来袭，构成现代EWZ史上最深的底部之一。","drivers":["Petrobras / Lava Jato political crisis","Iron ore & crude oil multi-year lows","BRL devaluation of roughly one-third in 2015","Deep Brazilian recession"],"drivers_zh":["巴西国家石油公司/洗车行动政治危机","铁矿石与原油处多年低位","2015年雷亚尔对美元贬值约三分之一","巴西深度经济衰退"],"prev_key":"2015-05","prev_key_chain":["2015-05"],"status":"exact","title":"Lava Jato collapse, BRL rout, deep trough −52%","title_zh":"洗车行动冲击、雷亚尔崩跌、深度底部 −52%","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2015-05"},"2016-01-21":{"body":"From the January 2016 low, EWZ surged 184% into January 2018 — one of the largest EM country rallies of the decade. The catalyst was two-fold: the Dilma Rousseff impeachment process building from early 2016 sparked a political re-rating as markets priced in a more market-friendly Temer government, and commodity prices recovered as oil rebounded from sub-$30 and iron ore bottomed. The BRL recovered sharply from its 2015–16 lows, adding a currency tailwind to an already-surging local equity market.","body_zh":"从2016年1月低点起，EWZ大涨184%至2018年1月，是当时十年来规模最大的单一新兴市场国家行情之一。催化剂来自两方面：迪尔玛弹劾程序从2016年初推进，市场对更亲市场的特梅尔政府提前定价，引发政治重新估值；与此同时，原油从30美元以下反弹、铁矿石见底，大宗商品价格复苏。雷亚尔从2015–16年低位急剧回升，在本币股市已强劲上涨的基础上再添汇率顺风。","drivers":["Dilma impeachment → Temer market-reform expectations","Crude oil rebound from sub-$30","Iron ore price recovery","BRL sharp reversal from 2015–16 lows"],"drivers_zh":["迪尔玛遭弹劾→特梅尔市场改革预期","原油从30美元以下反弹","铁矿石价格复苏","雷亚尔从2015–16年低位急剧回升"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Temer reform hope + commodity revival, +184%","title_zh":"特梅尔改革预期+大宗商品复苏，大涨184%","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2018-01"},"2018-09-13":{"body":"After a consolidation, EWZ rose from September 2018 through January 2020, gaining 65%. Jair Bolsonaro's October 2018 election — running on a pro-privatisation, pension-reform platform with Paulo Guedes as economy minister — drove a sharp re-rating in the closing months of 2018. The follow-through into 2019 was supported by passage of the landmark pension reform in late 2019 and continued global EM risk-on, while a relatively stable BRL let local equity gains flow through to USD investors.","body_zh":"经历一段盘整后，EWZ从2018年9月升至2020年1月，累计上涨65%。博索纳罗在2018年10月当选——以推进私有化、养老金改革及任命盖德斯为经济部长为竞选纲领——驱动2018年末的剧烈重新定价。2019年底里程碑式养老金改革顺利通过、全球新兴市场风险偏好持续回暖共同支撑了后续涨势，而雷亚尔相对稳定，令美元投资者充分享受到本币股市涨幅。","drivers":["Bolsonaro election win","Paulo Guedes pro-market reform agenda","Pension reform passed late 2019","Relatively stable BRL allowing equity gains to flow through"],"drivers_zh":["博索纳罗赢得大选","盖德斯亲市场改革议程","2019年底养老金改革获批","雷亚尔相对稳定，美元涨幅充分传导"],"prev_key":"2018-09","prev_key_chain":["2018-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Bolsonaro election rally, +65%","title_zh":"博索纳罗当选行情，大涨65%","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2018-09"},"2020-01-02":{"body":"EWZ fell 57% from January to March 2020, one of the steepest COVID selloffs among major country ETFs. Brazil's heavy index weight in Petrobras and Vale meant the early-March crude-oil price war (Saudi Arabia vs Russia) and the broad commodity-demand shock hit the index particularly hard. The BRL sold off to record lows against the dollar, amplifying local-equity losses substantially in USD terms.","body_zh":"EWZ从2020年1月至3月暴跌57%，是主要国家ETF中新冠抛售最惨烈的之一。巴西国家石油公司与淡水河谷在指数中占比高，意味着3月初爆发的原油价格战（沙特对俄罗斯）与广泛的大宗商品需求冲击对指数形成沉重打击。雷亚尔对美元抛售至历史低位，在美元计价层面大幅放大本币股市跌幅。","drivers":["Global COVID panic + EM capital flight","Crude oil price war (Saudi vs Russia) hit Petrobras","BRL at record lows vs USD","Commodity-demand shock"],"drivers_zh":["全球新冠恐慌+新兴市场资本外流","原油价格战冲击巴西国家石油公司","雷亚尔对美元触及历史低位","大宗商品需求冲击"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash: −57%","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：暴跌57%","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From the March 2020 panic low, EWZ rallied 109% through June 2021. The recovery was powered by a synchronised global commodity upturn — iron ore surged toward and above $200/tonne and crude oil recovered strongly — directly boosting Vale and Petrobras, the two pillars of the index. Global reflation and a weaker USD supported EM, while later Selic hikes added carry appeal as the cycle matured.","body_zh":"从2020年3月恐慌低点起，EWZ反弹109%至2021年6月。此轮复苏由全球同步大宗商品回升驱动——铁矿石飙升至200美元/吨上下乃至以上，原油强劲回升——直接提振淡水河谷与巴西国家石油公司这两大指数支柱。全球再通胀与美元走弱支撑新兴市场，随着周期成熟，后续Selic加息进一步增添套息吸引力。","drivers":["Iron ore surge toward/above $200/tonne","Crude oil strong recovery","Global reflation / USD weakness","Rising Selic adding carry appeal"],"drivers_zh":["铁矿石飙升至200美元/吨上下乃至以上","原油强劲复苏","全球再通胀/美元走弱","Selic加息增添套息吸引力"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Commodity supercycle recovery, +109%","title_zh":"大宗商品超级周期复苏，反弹109%","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2020-03"},"2021-06-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2021-06"},"2022-01-05":{"body":"A 49% bounce from December 2021 through April 2022 occurred as commodity prices spiked — the Russia-Ukraine war lifted crude and agricultural commodities in early 2022 — and Petrobras paid exceptional dividends. The move was constrained by rising 2022 election uncertainty, as markets began pricing the prospect of a Lula return and potential fiscal loosening, with the BRL caught between commodity support and political risk premium.","body_zh":"2021年12月至2022年4月，EWZ反弹49%，彼时大宗商品价格飙升——俄乌战争于2022年初拉动原油与农产品价格——巴西国家石油公司派发超额股息。然而，2022年大选不确定性上升（市场开始为卢拉回归及潜在财政松动定价）以及雷亚尔在商品支撑与政治风险溢价之间的拉锯，共同制约了此轮反弹幅度。","drivers":["Russia-Ukraine war lifted crude & agri commodities","Petrobras exceptional dividend yield","BRL supported by commodity terms of trade","Rising Lula election uncertainty capping upside"],"drivers_zh":["俄乌战争拉动原油与农产品价格","巴西国家石油公司超额股息","大宗商品贸易条件支撑雷亚尔","卢拉大选不确定性上升压制上行空间"],"prev_key":"2021-12","prev_key_chain":["2021-12"],"rekey_shift_days":21,"status":"shifted","title":"Commodity-driven pre-election bounce, +49%","title_zh":"大宗商品驱动的选前反弹，+49%","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2022-01"},"2022-04-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2022-04"},"2022-07-14":{"body":"From July 2022 through December 2023, EWZ gained 57% in a post-election relief dynamic: Lula won, but markets judged early cabinet appointments as more orthodox than feared and the BRL stabilised. A high Selic rate anchored the BRL at attractive carry levels, drawing EM fund inflows. This was primarily an EM beta rally with a BRL tailwind rather than a domestic growth story.","body_zh":"从2022年7月至2023年12月，EWZ累计上涨57%，呈现大选落地后的释然反弹：卢拉胜选，但早期内阁任命较市场担忧更为温和，雷亚尔趋于稳定。高Selic利率以具吸引力的套息水平锁定雷亚尔，吸引新兴市场基金流入。这主要是一轮叠加雷亚尔顺风的新兴市场贝塔行情，而非本土增长故事。","drivers":["Lula cabinet more orthodox than feared","High Selic anchoring BRL carry","Global EM inflows / EM beta rally","BRL stabilisation"],"drivers_zh":["卢拉内阁任命比预期更为温和","高Selic稳定雷亚尔套息吸引力","全球新兴市场资金流入/贝塔行情","雷亚尔趋于稳定"],"prev_key":"2022-07","prev_key_chain":["2022-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-election relief + EM beta rally, +57%","title_zh":"大选落地反弹+新兴市场贝塔，涨57%","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2022-07"},"2022-10-21":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2022-10"},"2023-03-23":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2023-03"},"2023-12-19":{"body":"From December 2023 through December 2024, EWZ fell 31% as Brazil's fiscal framework deteriorated. The Lula government repeatedly strained its spending rules, gross government debt rose toward 90% of GDP, and the BRL depreciated about 27% against the dollar — the worst-performing major EM currency of 2024, hitting its weakest level since the real's 1994 launch. The Selic was hiked sharply but failed to arrest the slide, as markets read high rates alongside widening deficits as a toxic mix.","body_zh":"从2023年12月至2024年12月，EWZ下跌31%，巴西财政框架恶化。卢拉政府多次令支出规则承压，政府总债务逼近GDP的90%，雷亚尔对美元贬值约27%——成为2024年表现最差的主要新兴市场货币，并触及1994年雷亚尔启用以来最弱水平。Selic利率大幅上调，但未能阻止下滑，因市场将高利率与扩大的赤字并存视为毒性组合。","drivers":["Lula fiscal overspending, primary deficit widening","BRL roughly −27% in 2024, worst major EM currency","Government debt rising toward 90% of GDP","High Selic failing to halt currency slide"],"drivers_zh":["卢拉政府超支，基本赤字扩大","2024年雷亚尔约贬值27%，为主要新兴市场最弱货币","政府债务逼近GDP的90%","高Selic未能阻止货币下滑"],"prev_key":"2023-12","prev_key_chain":["2023-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal credibility crisis, BRL −27%, −31%","title_zh":"财政公信力危机、雷亚尔暴贬，跌31%","turn_id":"ewz:peak:2023-12"},"2024-12-18":{"body":"From December 2024 through April 2026, EWZ surged 96% — driven predominantly by external factors rather than domestic improvement. A broad USD-weakening phase and renewed rotation into high-carry EM currencies lifted the BRL, turbocharging USD-denominated returns off a deeply oversold base. With the domestic fiscal picture still unresolved, the rally was largely perception- and carry-driven rather than reform-grounded; the sharp reversal from April 2026 (the current trough) reflects the fragility of that external foundation. Specific late-stage catalysts in this window fall beyond reliable knowledge and are not asserted here.","body_zh":"从2024年12月至2026年4月，EWZ大涨96%——主要由外部因素而非国内改善驱动。广泛的美元走弱阶段叠加资金重新轮入高套息新兴市场货币，提振雷亚尔，在深度超卖的基础上令美元计价回报倍增。由于国内财政状况仍未解决，这轮行情以预期与套息驱动为主，缺乏实质改革支撑；2026年4月起的急剧回调（当前所处低谷）反映出这一外部基础的脆弱性。此窗口内的具体后段催化剂超出可靠认知范围，故不作断言。","drivers":["USD broad weakening phase","BRL carry rebound as EM flows returned","Deeply oversold starting base","External-driven rally, fiscal picture unresolved"],"drivers_zh":["美元整体走弱阶段","新兴市场资金回流，雷亚尔套息回升","深度超卖的起涨基础","外部驱动行情，财政状况未解决"],"prev_key":"2024-12","prev_key_chain":["2024-12"],"status":"exact","title":"USD weakness + carry rebound, +96%","title_zh":"美元走弱+套息回归，大涨96%","turn_id":"ewz:trough:2024-12"}},"now":"EWZ sits deep in a Trough at position 5.8/100, having reversed sharply off its April 2026 peak after a powerful prior advance. Its 63-day relative strength versus SPY is −18.5, among the weakest readings in the universe (RS rank 22 of 24), and total return over the 15-year window is roughly −9.5% in USD terms, underscoring how punishing the currency drag has been. The structural pattern is familiar: the preceding Dec-2024 to Apr-2026 leg (+96%) was driven largely by global USD weakness and a BRL carry rebound rather than domestic reform, and EWZ remains hostage to commodity prices, Brazil's fiscal credibility, and a procyclical real.","now_zh":"EWZ深陷周期低谷，当前位置仅为5.8/100，从2026年4月峰值急剧反转，此前曾大幅上涨。过去63日相对SPY的强弱为−18.5，属本数据库最弱之列（强弱排名第22/24位）；15年观察窗口内以美元计的累计总回报约为−9.5%，凸显汇率阻力的侵蚀力度。其结构性特征一如既往：此前2024年12月至2026年4月的涨势（+96%）主要由全球美元走弱与雷亚尔套息回归驱动，而非国内改革；EWZ仍受制于大宗商品价格、巴西财政公信力及顺周期的雷亚尔。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"eza":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:trough:2011-10"},"2013-01-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:peak:2013-01"},"2013-06-20":{"body":"From mid-2013 through April 2015, EZA gained 42% as global EM stabilized after the initial Fed taper shock and commodity prices partially recovered. The JSE benefited from gold and platinum demand, but the rand stayed structurally weak as South Africa's current account deficit widened, so USD-based returns were capped even as local equities performed.","body_zh":"2013年中至2015年4月，美联储缩债冲击后全球新兴市场逐步企稳，大宗商品价格阶段性回升，EZA累计上涨42%。约翰内斯堡交易所受黄金与铂金需求提振，但南非经常账户赤字扩大使兰特持续承压，以美元计价的回报因此受到抑制。","drivers":["EM stabilization post-taper","Gold & PGM demand recovery","JSE resource sector bid","Structural ZAR weakness offsetting local gains"],"drivers_zh":["缩债冲击后新兴市场企稳","黄金与铂族金属需求回升","约翰内斯堡资源股买盘","兰特结构性走弱抵消本地涨幅"],"prev_key":"2013-06","prev_key_chain":["2013-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-Taper Tantrum Commodity Lift","title_zh":"缩债恐慌后大宗商品提振","turn_id":"eza:trough:2013-06"},"2014-09-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:peak:2014-09"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"From January 2016 to January 2018, EZA surged 107%. The rand recovered sharply as commodity prices rebounded and global EM saw a sustained risk-on wave. The key domestic catalyst was Cyril Ramaphosa's election as ANC president in December 2017, which unleashed a 'Ramaphoria' — markets priced in a governance and investment-climate transformation after the Zuma era, lifting both the JSE and the rand into early 2018.","body_zh":"2016年1月至2018年1月，EZA以美元计价大涨107%。大宗商品价格反弹、全球新兴市场持续风险偏好推动兰特强势回升。关键国内催化剂是拉马福萨于2017年12月当选非国大主席，市场随即定价治理改善与投资环境重建的预期（即\"拉马福里亚\"行情），约翰内斯堡交易所与兰特均走高。","drivers":["Commodity cycle rebound","Global EM risk-on","Ramaphoria — Ramaphosa ANC leadership","ZAR recovery from extreme undervaluation"],"drivers_zh":["大宗商品周期反弹","全球新兴市场风险偏好","\"拉马福里亚\"——拉马福萨执掌非国大","兰特从极度低估区间回升"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Ramaphoria Rally — 107% Up Leg","title_zh":"\"拉马福里亚\"行情——上涨107%","turn_id":"eza:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"body":"From January to October 2018, EZA fell 37% as the initial Ramaphosa euphoria gave way to the reality of slow institutional reform. A broader EM selloff driven by rising US interest rates and a strengthening dollar compounded domestic concerns, with the rand depreciating again. South Africa entered a technical recession in mid-2018 and commodity prices weakened.","body_zh":"2018年1月至10月，EZA下跌37%。围绕拉马福萨的初始乐观情绪消退，机构改革推进缓慢的现实令市场失望。美联储加息与美元走强引发新兴市场整体抛售，叠加国内担忧，兰特再度贬值。南非于2018年年中陷入技术性衰退，大宗商品价格同步走弱。","drivers":["EM-wide USD strength selloff","ZAR depreciation resumes","South Africa technical recession","Reform pace disappointment"],"drivers_zh":["美元走强引发新兴市场整体抛售","兰特再度贬值","南非进入技术性衰退","改革推进速度令市场失望"],"prev_key":"2018-01","prev_key_chain":["2018-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-Ramaphoria Correction","title_zh":"\"拉马福里亚\"后的回调","turn_id":"eza:peak:2018-01"},"2018-10-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:trough:2018-10"},"2019-04-18":{"body":"From April 2019 through March 2020, EZA lost 52.5% — a protracted decline combining domestic structural deterioration with the COVID-19 shock. Eskom's chronic load-shedding constrained GDP growth, fiscal deficits widened, and South Africa's sovereign credit was cut toward sub-investment grade. The March 2020 COVID crash delivered the final sharp leg down, with USD losses magnified by a rand that fell toward all-time lows near R19 per dollar.","body_zh":"2019年4月至2020年3月，EZA下跌52.5%，跌势持久。埃斯科姆电力公司长期限电拖累南非GDP增长，财政赤字扩大，主权信用评级逼近投机级。2020年3月新冠疫情引发的崩盘构成最后一跌，兰特跌至接近19兑1美元的历史低位，进一步放大了美元计价损失。","drivers":["Eskom load-shedding crushing growth","Sovereign credit rating cuts toward junk","COVID-19 risk-off crash","ZAR at historic lows"],"drivers_zh":["埃斯科姆限电重创增长","主权评级遭下调逼近垃圾级","新冠疫情引发全球避险崩盘","兰特触及历史低位"],"prev_key":"2019-04","prev_key_chain":["2019-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Pre-COVID Decline into the Crash","title_zh":"新冠前的下行与崩盘","turn_id":"eza:peak:2019-04"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From March 2020 to June 2021, EZA surged 140% as global risk assets rebounded on unprecedented fiscal and monetary stimulus. Gold, platinum and iron-ore prices spiked, providing a powerful tailwind for JSE resource stocks. The rand recovered strongly from its historic lows, adding a large FX gain to USD returns. South Africa's equity market retraced the COVID selloff and more, though structural issues — load-shedding, very high unemployment — remained unresolved.","body_zh":"2020年3月至2021年6月，EZA大涨140%。全球史无前例的财政与货币刺激推动风险资产反弹，黄金、铂金、铁矿石价格大幅飙升，为约翰内斯堡交易所资源股提供强劲动力。兰特从历史低位强劲回升，贡献了可观的汇率增益。尽管限电与极高失业率等结构性问题依然悬而未决，南非股市仍完整收复并超越了新冠期间的跌幅。","drivers":["Global stimulus risk-on","Gold, platinum, iron ore price spike","ZAR recovery from historic lows","EM commodity demand rebound"],"drivers_zh":["全球刺激政策推动风险偏好","黄金、铂金、铁矿石价格飙升","兰特从历史低位强势反弹","新兴市场大宗商品需求复苏"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Recovery — 140% Rebound","title_zh":"新冠后强劲反弹——上涨140%","turn_id":"eza:trough:2020-03"},"2021-06-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:peak:2021-06"},"2021-11-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:trough:2021-11"},"2022-04-01":{"body":"From April to October 2022, EZA fell 35% as the Fed's aggressive rate-hiking cycle drove a global EM selloff and a strong dollar. South Africa faced its own fiscal pressures from Eskom debt-bailout costs and elevated social spending, while load-shedding hit record stages. Commodity prices pulled back from their post-COVID peaks, removing a key prop for JSE resource stocks.","body_zh":"2022年4月至10月，EZA下跌35%。美联储激进加息推动美元走强，引发全球新兴市场资产抛售。南非面临埃斯科姆债务救助成本攀升与高额社会支出的财政压力，限电程度创历史纪录。大宗商品价格从新冠后高点回落，约翰内斯堡资源股失去重要支撑。","drivers":["Fed tightening global EM selloff","USD strength vs ZAR","Eskom load-shedding at record severity","Commodity price pullback"],"drivers_zh":["美联储紧缩引发新兴市场抛售","美元走强打压兰特","埃斯科姆限电创历史严重程度","大宗商品价格从高位回调"],"prev_key":"2022-04","prev_key_chain":["2022-04"],"status":"exact","title":"EM Tightening & SA Fiscal Squeeze","title_zh":"新兴市场紧缩与南非财政压力","turn_id":"eza:peak:2022-04"},"2022-10-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:trough:2022-10"},"2023-01-13":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:peak:2023-01"},"2023-05-30":{"body":"From May 2023 to February 2026, EZA gained 160% — the largest up leg in the briefing window. The ANC's loss of its parliamentary majority in the May 2024 elections led to a Government of National Unity (GNU) with the business-friendly DA and other parties, triggering a major re-rating of South African assets: the JSE surged, the rand firmed, and the credit outlook improved (JPMorgan double-upgraded SA to overweight). Higher gold and platinum prices augmented equity gains through 2025.","body_zh":"2023年5月至2026年2月，EZA大涨160%，是本数据窗口内最大单边上升行情。2024年5月大选中非国大失去议会多数席位，随后与亲商的民主联盟等政党组建国家团结政府（GNU），南非资产迎来重大重新定价：约翰内斯堡交易所大涨、兰特走强、信用展望改善（摩根大通将南非上调至超配）。黄金与铂金价格走高，进一步推升2025年的股票回报。","drivers":["GNU formation & ANC majority loss","ZAR recovery on political re-rating","Gold & PGM price uptrend","Improved sovereign credit outlook"],"drivers_zh":["国家团结政府成立、非国大失去多数席位","政治重新定价推动兰特回升","黄金与铂族金属价格上行","主权信用展望改善"],"prev_key":"2023-05","prev_key_chain":["2023-05"],"status":"exact","title":"GNU Re-rating — 160% Up Leg","title_zh":"国家团结政府重新定价——上涨160%","turn_id":"eza:trough:2023-05"},"2024-09-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:peak:2024-09"},"2025-04-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eza:trough:2025-04"},"2026-02-27":{"body":"From February to March 2026, EZA fell 23.3% as the extended GNU re-rating rally lost momentum from a stretched, near-peak cycle position. Investors rotated out of high-beta EM exposure and the rand weakened, amplifying USD-denominated losses. The drawdown was sharp but brief, leaving the market at an extreme washed-out reading near its cycle trough. Note this leg ends after this analysis's reliable-knowledge horizon; the magnitude and direction are taken from the briefing, and no specific external catalyst is asserted.","body_zh":"2026年2月至3月，EZA下跌23.3%。多年的GNU重新定价行情在接近周期高位、估值拉伸的背景下动能耗尽。投资者从高贝塔新兴市场敞口中撤出，兰特走弱，放大了美元计价损失。此次回落幅度较大但持续时间短，市场周期位置已跌至极度超卖区间。需注意此段超出本分析的可靠知识范围，幅度与方向取自数据简报，未对具体外部催化剂作出断言。","drivers":["GNU rally momentum exhaustion","Stretched near-peak cycle position","ZAR weakening on EM risk-off","High-beta EM rotation out"],"drivers_zh":["GNU行情动能耗尽","接近周期高位、估值拉伸","新兴市场避险推动兰特走弱","高贝塔新兴市场资产遭抛售"],"prev_key":"2026-02","prev_key_chain":["2026-02"],"status":"exact","title":"GNU Rally Exhaustion","title_zh":"GNU行情动能耗尽","turn_id":"eza:peak:2026-02"}},"now":"EZA sits at a cycle position of 1.7 out of 100 — essentially a multi-year trough — after peaking in February 2026 and selling off sharply into a March 2026 low. The ETF is below its 200-day moving average and has trailed SPY by 13.7 percentage points over the past 63 days, reflecting both a JSE equity pullback and renewed rand weakness against the dollar. The drawdown caps the exhaustion of the long 2023-2026 GNU re-rating rally, the largest up-leg in this market's 15-year record. The cycle model projects the next inflection as a potential turn higher around September 2026, consistent with this market's history of sharp mean-reversion off washed-out troughs.","now_zh":"EZA当前周期位置仅为1.7/100，接近多年低点——2026年2月触顶后急剧回落，并于2026年3月探底。目前仍处于200日均线下方，过去63个交易日相对标普500跑输13.7个百分点，反映出约翰内斯堡证券交易所股市下跌与兰特对美元走弱的双重压力。此次回落标志着2023至2026年国家团结政府（GNU）重新定价行情的动能耗尽——那是该市场15年记录中最大的单边上升行情。周期模型预计下一个拐点为2026年9月前后可能出现的向上转折，这与该市场在极度超卖低点后往往强劲均值回归的历史一致。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"fxi":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"body":"After the 2011 global growth scare and EM selloff, FXI bottomed in October 2011. The subsequent +45% move into January 2013 was driven by PBOC policy easing — reserve-requirement and interest-rate cuts through 2012 — and stabilizing global growth. The CNY was broadly stable against the USD, so local gains translated relatively cleanly into USD ETF returns. FXI's heavy SOE financials and energy weighting meant it tracked China's credit-driven infrastructure rebound closely.","body_zh":"2011年全球增长恐慌与新兴市场抛售后，FXI于2011年10月触底。随后至2013年1月录得约+45%涨幅，主要受央行政策宽松驱动——2012年多次下调存款准备金率和利率，全球增长也趋于稳定。该时期人民币兑美元基本平稳，本地涨幅较为顺畅地转换为美元ETF回报。FXI高度集中于国有金融和能源股，因此紧密跟踪了中国信贷驱动的基建复苏。","drivers":["PBOC RRR and rate cuts through 2012","Global risk-on after EU debt crisis","CNY broadly stable; clean USD translation","SOE financials/energy track infrastructure rebound"],"prev_key":"2011-10","prev_key_chain":["2011-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis base; SOE recovery","title_zh":"危机后筑底；国企复苏","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2011-10"},"2012-02-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2012-02"},"2012-06-25":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2012-06"},"2013-01-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2013-01"},"2013-06-25":{"body":"From June 2013 to April 2015 FXI gained roughly +75% as China's onshore market built toward a dramatic retail-driven mania. The Shanghai Composite nearly doubled in the year before mid-2015, fueled by monetary easing, state-media promotion of equities, and an explosion in margin borrowing. FXI — weighted toward Hong Kong-listed H-shares rather than onshore A-shares — lagged the pure A-share mania but still rallied as foreign capital flooded Hong Kong-listed Chinese names. The CNY was broadly stable to slightly firmer, providing a small tailwind to USD returns.","body_zh":"2013年6月至2015年4月，FXI上涨约+75%，境内市场逐步酝酿出剧烈的散户驱动狂热。2015年年中前一年，上证综指近乎翻倍，由货币宽松、官方媒体力推股市及融资余额爆炸式增长共同推动。FXI以港股H股为主要配置，相对纯A股狂热有所滞后，但外资涌入香港中资股仍带来可观涨幅。人民币总体平稳略偏强，为美元回报提供了微弱顺风。","drivers":["PBOC easing plus onshore margin-debt explosion","State-media equity promotion","Foreign capital inflows to H-shares","Broadly stable CNY; small FX tailwind"],"prev_key":"2013-06","prev_key_chain":["2013-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Liquidity-fueled run into the 2015 bubble","title_zh":"流动性驱动，升至2015年泡沫顶峰","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2013-06"},"2015-04-27":{"body":"The roughly -45% decline from April 2015 to February 2016 came in two waves. First, the onshore A-share bubble burst in June 2015 as margin calls cascaded and government circuit-breaker interventions failed. Second, in August 2015 the PBOC executed a surprise CNY devaluation of roughly 2% — the largest single move in years — adding an FX loss on top of the equity loss for USD holders. China hard-landing fears amplified the selloff. FXI's H-share structure absorbed both the Hong Kong equity rout and the CNY translation hit.","body_zh":"2015年4月至2016年2月约-45%的下跌分两波展开。首先，境内A股泡沫于2015年6月因融资平仓连锁反应而破裂，政府熔断机制干预宣告失败。其次，2015年8月央行突然将人民币贬值约2%——数年来最大单次贬值——对美元持有者叠加了汇率损失。对中国经济硬着陆的担忧进一步放大抛售。FXI的H股结构同时承受了港股下跌和人民币折算双重冲击。","drivers":["A-share margin bubble collapse, June 2015","PBOC surprise CNY devaluation, August 2015","China hard-landing growth fears","Circuit-breaker failure magnified panic"],"prev_key":"2015-04","prev_key_chain":["2015-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Bubble bursts; CNY shock amplifies losses","title_zh":"泡沫破裂；人民币贬值放大跌幅","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2015-04"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"FXI nearly doubled (+100%) from February 2016 to January 2018 alongside a globally synchronized growth upturn, a stabilizing then modestly firmer CNY, and anticipation of MSCI's inclusion of China A-shares (announced June 2017, effective 2018). China's credit impulse re-accelerated in 2016-2017 under supply-side reforms and infrastructure spending, supporting earnings for the SOE-heavy basket. The post-2016 global reflation trade (commodities and EM bid) also lifted China.","body_zh":"2016年2月至2018年1月，FXI接近翻倍（+100%），与全球同步经济复苏、人民币企稳后温和走强以及MSCI纳入中国A股预期（2017年6月宣布，2018年生效）相伴。中国信贷脉冲在供给侧改革和基建支出推动下于2016-2017年重新加速，支撑了以国企为主的成分股盈利。2016年后的全球再通胀交易（大宗商品和新兴市场走强）也提振了中国。","drivers":["Globally synchronized growth, 2016-2017","CNY stabilization then mild appreciation","MSCI A-share inclusion anticipation","China credit impulse re-acceleration; supply-side reform"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Recovery; reflation and MSCI inclusion bid","title_zh":"复苏；再通胀与入摩预期提振","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2018-01"},"2020-03-16":{"body":"After the February-March 2020 Covid crash, FXI rallied +64% into February 2021. China was the first major economy to contain the virus and restart production, giving its export sector a lead. Fiscal stimulus, PBOC liquidity, and surging global demand for Chinese manufactured goods drove an earnings recovery, while internet giants appreciated as digital adoption accelerated. The CNY appreciated meaningfully against the USD from mid-2020 into early 2021, adding an FX tailwind on top of the equity gains.","body_zh":"2020年2月至3月新冠崩盘后，FXI反弹约+64%至2021年2月。中国是最先控制疫情并重启生产的主要经济体，出口部门获得先机。财政刺激、央行流动性及全球对中国制造商品需求激增推动盈利复苏，互联网巨头亦随数字化加速上涨。2020年中至2021年初人民币兑美元明显升值，为美元投资者在股票涨幅之上带来汇率顺风。","drivers":["China first-out-of-Covid production restart","Global demand surge for Chinese manufactured goods","PBOC liquidity plus fiscal stimulus","CNY appreciation vs USD; FX tailwind"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Covid rebound: SOE and tech catch-up","title_zh":"新冠反弹：国企与科技股补涨","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2020-03"},"2021-02-17":{"body":"The roughly -50% decline from February 2021 to March 2022 was triggered by Beijing's sweeping regulatory campaign across internet platforms, education, and property. Alibaba, Tencent, Meituan, and Didi faced large fines, de-listings, or operational restrictions. The collapse of Evergrande from mid-2021 exposed systemic stress in the property sector, with contagion across developers. The CNY held relatively firm, offering little cushion — losses were almost entirely equity-driven rather than FX-driven, and foreign institutional capital exited Chinese equities at scale.","body_zh":"2021年2月至2022年3月约-50%的跌幅，由北京对互联网平台、教育及房地产的全面监管整治引发。阿里巴巴、腾讯、美团、滴滴遭遇巨额罚款、退市或经营限制。恒大自2021年年中起崩塌，暴露房地产行业的系统性压力，风险蔓延至全行业开发商。人民币相对坚挺，几乎未提供缓冲——损失几乎完全来自股票而非汇率，外资机构资金大规模撤离中国股市。","drivers":["Regulatory crackdown: tech, education, property","Evergrande collapse; property sector systemic stress","Foreign capital flight from Chinese equities","CNY stable — losses were equity-driven, not FX"],"prev_key":"2021-02","prev_key_chain":["2021-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Regulatory crackdown and property crisis","title_zh":"监管重拳与房地产危机","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2021-02"},"2022-03-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2022-03"},"2022-04-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2022-04"},"2022-10-31":{"body":"FXI surged +62% from October 2022 to January 2023 in one of its sharpest short-term moves. The October 2022 trough coincided with peak zero-Covid pessimism, Xi Jinping's consolidation of power at the 20th Party Congress, and deeply depressed valuations. The December 2022 pivot — abandoning zero-Covid and announcing reopening — catalyzed global capital to re-enter, with Hong Kong-listed shares (FXI's primary weight) leading as offshore money re-priced the reopening dividend.","body_zh":"FXI从2022年10月至2023年1月飙升约+62%，是历史上最剧烈的短期反弹之一。2022年10月低谷恰逢清零悲观情绪顶峰、习近平在二十大巩固权力以及估值极度低估。2022年12月政策急转弯——放弃清零并宣布重开——催化全球资本重新入场，以FXI主要权重的港股领涨，离岸资金重新定价重开红利。","drivers":["Zero-Covid policy reversal, December 2022","20th Party Congress overhang cleared","Deep valuation compression at the trough","Offshore re-pricing of reopening"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Zero-Covid exit rally","title_zh":"清零政策退出反弹","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2022-10"},"2023-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2023-01"},"2024-01-22":{"body":"After the failed 2023 reopening rally faded, FXI built a base from January 2024 and rallied +86% into March 2025. The decisive catalyst was the September 2024 PBOC package: cuts to the reserve-requirement ratio and policy rates, plus two new market-support tools — a roughly RMB 500bn securities/fund/insurer swap facility and a roughly RMB 300bn relending window for share buybacks. The Politburo signaled fiscal follow-through, and onshore national-team funds provided a price floor. Early-2025 optimism around domestic AI (DeepSeek) added a narrative tailwind.","body_zh":"2023年重开行情熄火后，FXI从2024年1月起筑底，并在至2025年3月间累计上涨约+86%。决定性催化剂是2024年9月央行一揽子政策：下调存款准备金率与政策利率，并推出两项市场支持工具——约5000亿元面向券商/基金/保险的互换便利及约3000亿元支持回购的再贷款。政治局发出财政跟进信号，境内国家队基金提供价格托底。2025年初围绕国内AI（DeepSeek）的乐观情绪进一步提供叙事顺风。","drivers":["PBOC September 2024 rate/RRR cuts plus market-support facilities","National-team buying; policy put reinstated","Politburo fiscal stimulus signal","DeepSeek AI narrative; tech re-rating"],"prev_key":"2024-01","prev_key_chain":["2024-01"],"status":"exact","title":"PBOC stimulus and national-team buying","title_zh":"央行刺激与国家队护盘","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2024-01"},"2024-10-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2024-10"},"2025-01-10":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2025-01"},"2025-03-17":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2025-03"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"After the April 2025 tariff shock initially hit Chinese equities, FXI rebounded and climbed +43% to its October 2025 peak. The recovery was supported by DeepSeek's early-2025 model release demonstrating competitive AI at lower compute cost, igniting a re-rating of Chinese tech, and by Xi Jinping's February 2025 meeting with private-sector tech leaders signaling a thaw after the crackdown era. Continued policy support and resilient exports rounded out the move, with a broadly stable CNY keeping USD returns roughly in line with local gains.","body_zh":"2025年4月关税冲击初期重创中国股市后，FXI反弹并至2025年10月峰值累计上涨约+43%。复苏受DeepSeek于2025年初发布模型驱动——该模型以较低算力成本实现有竞争力的AI性能，引发中国科技股重新估值；同时2025年2月习近平与民营科技领袖会面，标志着整治时代后的缓和。持续的政策支持与韧性出口共同推动行情，人民币总体稳定使美元回报与本地涨幅大体一致。","drivers":["DeepSeek AI re-rating of Chinese tech","Xi-private sector reconciliation signal, February 2025","Ongoing policy support; export resilience","Broadly stable CNY"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"AI re-rating into the October 2025 peak","title_zh":"AI重估行情推升至2025年10月峰值","turn_id":"fxi:trough:2025-04"},"2025-10-02":{"body":"From the October 2025 peak through June 2026, FXI fell about 23.5%, retracing toward the bottom of its multi-year range. Renewed US-China trade friction and a firmer USD weighed on Chinese equities and the renminbi, while lingering property-sector strain limited the traction of domestic stimulus. The drawdown left FXI at an extreme low (position 0.3/100) with relative strength versus SPY ranked near the bottom of the cross-market field. From these washed-out levels, the cycle model projects a potential turn toward a new peak around December 2026.","body_zh":"从2025年10月峰值至2026年6月，FXI下跌约23.5%，回落至多年区间底部附近。美中贸易摩擦再起及美元走强拖累中国股市与人民币，房地产行业的持续压力也限制了国内刺激的效果。此轮回撤令FXI跌至极端低位（位置0.3/100），相对标普500强度在跨市场中接近垫底。从这一超卖水平出发，周期模型预测下一个峰值或于2026年12月前后出现。","drivers":["Renewed US-China trade tensions","Firmer USD pressures the USD-denominated ETF","Property-sector strain limits stimulus efficacy","Extreme washout; cycle model projects a turn"],"prev_key":"2025-10","prev_key_chain":["2025-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade tensions drag to the June 2026 trough","title_zh":"贸易摩擦拖累至2026年6月低谷","turn_id":"fxi:peak:2025-10"}},"now":"FXI sits at an extreme trough (position 0.3/100), having shed roughly 23.5% from its October 2025 peak amid renewed US-China trade tensions and a firmer USD that weighed on both Chinese equities and the renminbi. Relative strength versus SPY is deeply negative at -22.1, ranking it 23rd of 24 markets — a stark divergence as US equities held up while China rolled over. The ETF trades below its 200-day moving average. The cycle model projects a potential turn toward a new peak around December 2026, implying the market may be trying to base near these washed-out levels.","now_zh":"FXI处于极端低谷（位置0.3/100），自2025年10月峰值以来下跌约23.5%，受美中贸易摩擦再起及美元走强拖累，中国股市与人民币同步承压。相对强度较标普500指数大幅落后（-22.1，在24个市场中排名第23），与美股的韧性形成鲜明分化。ETF现位于200日均线下方。周期模型预测下一个峰值或于2026年12月前后出现，暗示市场可能正在这一超卖水平附近尝试筑底。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"inda":{"legs":{"2012-02-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:trough:2012-02"},"2013-02-01":{"body":"When the Fed signaled QE tapering in May 2013, India was branded one of the 'Fragile Five' EM economies, with a large current account deficit (~4.8% of GDP) and heavy reliance on foreign flows. FIIs sold Indian equities and the rupee fell nearly 20% against the dollar by August 2013, compounding INDA's 29.8% USD drawdown. The RBI defended the currency with emergency measures, including tighter short-term liquidity and a special FCNR swap window, adding to domestic pressure.","body_zh":"2013年5月美联储释放缩减购债信号后，印度因经常账户赤字庞大（约占GDP的4.8%）、高度依赖外资流入而被列为\"脆弱五国\"之一。FII抛售印度股票，卢比兑美元至2013年8月累计贬值近20%，放大了INDA以美元计价的29.8%跌幅。印度储备银行通过紧急措施捍卫货币，包括收紧短期流动性及推出专项FCNR外汇掉期窗口，加剧了国内压力。","drivers":["Fed taper signal triggered an EM-wide FII exodus","INR fell nearly 20%, roughly doubling the USD drawdown vs local equity losses","Large current account deficit made India acutely vulnerable","RBI emergency liquidity tightening added domestic pressure"],"drivers_zh":["美联储缩债信号引发新兴市场FII集体出逃","卢比贬值近20%，使美元跌幅约为本地股市跌幅的两倍","庞大的经常账户赤字使印度格外脆弱","印储行紧急收紧流动性叠加国内压力"],"prev_key":"2013-02","prev_key_chain":["2013-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Taper tantrum rupee crash","title_zh":"缩债恐慌引发卢比暴跌","turn_id":"inda:peak:2013-02"},"2013-08-28":{"body":"From the August 2013 trough, India staged a 76.6% USD rally into March 2015, one of the strongest EM recoveries of the cycle. The rupee stabilized and the current account deficit narrowed as RBI credibility was restored under new Governor Raghuram Rajan. The key catalyst was the May 2014 general election, which delivered Narendra Modi and the BJP a decisive majority, driving a re-rating on hopes of infrastructure investment, fiscal consolidation, and business-friendly reform. Improving global risk appetite added an EM tailwind.","body_zh":"从2013年8月底部起，印度以美元计价上涨76.6%至2015年3月，是该周期内最强的新兴市场复苏之一。随着新行长拉古拉姆·拉詹重建印储行公信力，卢比企稳、经常账户赤字收窄。关键催化剂是2014年5月大选，莫迪与人民党赢得决定性多数，市场对基础设施投资、财政整顿及商业友好型改革的预期推动估值重估。全球风险偏好改善提供了新兴市场顺风。","drivers":["May 2014 Modi/BJP election win triggered an earnings and valuation re-rating","RBI credibility restored under Rajan; INR stabilized","Current account deficit narrowed, reducing fragility","Improving global risk appetite supported EM inflows"],"drivers_zh":["2014年5月莫迪/人民党大选获胜引发盈利与估值重估","拉詹领导下印储行公信力恢复，卢比企稳","经常账户赤字收窄，脆弱性降低","全球风险偏好改善支撑新兴市场资金流入"],"prev_key":"2013-08","prev_key_chain":["2013-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Modi wave and EM re-rating rally","title_zh":"莫迪浪潮与新兴市场重估反弹","turn_id":"inda:trough:2013-08"},"2015-03-03":{"body":"India's 28.7% drawdown from March 2015 to February 2016 came alongside a broad EM rout driven by the China growth scare, a commodity-price collapse, and anticipation of the first Fed rate hike since 2006. FIIs rotated out of EM broadly and the rupee weakened. Domestic reform momentum slowed as key legislation, including GST, faced delays, eroding the growth premium that had supported the prior rally.","body_zh":"从2015年3月至2016年2月，印度下跌28.7%，与中国增长恐慌、大宗商品价格崩溃及美联储自2006年来首次加息预期所引发的新兴市场整体抛售同步。FII广泛撤出新兴市场，卢比走弱。随着包括GST在内的关键立法受阻，莫迪改革动能放缓，此前支撑涨势的增长溢价有所消退。","drivers":["China growth scare and commodity rout hit EM broadly","Start of the Fed rate-hike cycle triggered EM outflows","Domestic reform delays (incl. GST) dampened the growth premium","INR weakness compounded the USD drawdown"],"drivers_zh":["中国增长恐慌与大宗商品暴跌对新兴市场造成整体冲击","美联储开启加息周期引发新兴市场资金外流","国内改革受阻（含GST）削弱增长溢价","卢比走弱放大美元跌幅"],"prev_key":"2015-03","prev_key_chain":["2015-03"],"status":"exact","title":"EM selloff, China scare, Fed hike","title_zh":"新兴市场抛售、中国恐慌与加息压力","turn_id":"inda:peak:2015-03"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"A 29.9% recovery from February to September 2016 tracked a global EM rebound as the Fed signaled it would slow its hiking pace. Oil prices recovered off their early-2016 lows, easing India's import-cost and current-account pressure and supporting the rupee. Reform expectations also firmed as the GST constitutional amendment advanced, though the leg ended before the November 2016 demonetization shock.","body_zh":"2016年2月至9月，随着美联储暗示放缓加息步伐，全球新兴市场反弹，印度上涨29.9%。油价从2016年初低点回升，缓解了印度的进口成本与经常账户压力并支撑卢比。随着GST宪法修正案推进，改革预期回暖；但此段行情在2016年11月去货币化冲击之前结束。","drivers":["Fed signaling a slower hiking pace reversed EM outflows","Oil recovery eased India's import cost and current-account pressure","GST constitutional amendment progress lifted reform credibility","INR stabilized as the dollar softened"],"drivers_zh":["美联储暗示放缓加息节奏逆转新兴市场资金外流","油价回升缓解印度进口成本与经常账户压力","GST宪法修正案推进提升改革公信力","美元走软，卢比企稳"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"EM bounce, Fed pause, oil recovery","title_zh":"新兴市场反弹、美联储暂停与油价回升","turn_id":"inda:trough:2016-02"},"2016-09-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:peak:2016-09"},"2016-11-21":{"body":"Despite the shock of the November 2016 demonetization, which withdrew 86% of currency in circulation overnight, India rallied 49.4% from November 2016 to January 2018. Markets looked past the near-term GDP hit and repriced longer-term formalization benefits: GST launched in July 2017, corporate earnings recovered, and FII flows returned. A broadly risk-on global backdrop and supportive EM flows provided an additional tailwind.","body_zh":"尽管2016年11月去货币化政策（一夜之间撤回86%的流通现金）引发震荡，印度仍从2016年11月至2018年1月上涨49.4%。市场越过短期GDP冲击，对长期正规化红利进行重估：GST于2017年7月正式落地，企业盈利回升，FII资金回流。整体偏向风险偏好的全球环境与新兴市场资金流入提供了额外顺风。","drivers":["GST launch in July 2017 marked a major structural-reform milestone","Demonetization cash shock was absorbed; corporate earnings recovered","FII flows returned amid a risk-on global backdrop","Supportive EM flows added to USD returns"],"drivers_zh":["2017年7月GST正式落地，标志重大结构性改革里程碑","去货币化现金冲击被消化，企业盈利回升","在偏风险偏好的全球环境下FII资金回流","新兴市场资金流入为美元回报提供支撑"],"prev_key":"2016-11","prev_key_chain":["2016-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-demonetization reform re-rating","title_zh":"去货币化后的改革重估上涨","turn_id":"inda:trough:2016-11"},"2018-01-23":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:peak:2018-01"},"2018-10-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:trough:2018-10"},"2019-06-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:peak:2019-06"},"2019-08-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:trough:2019-08"},"2020-01-17":{"body":"India's 43.3% drawdown from January to March 2020 was driven by the global COVID-19 panic selloff. India imposed one of the world's strictest lockdowns in late March 2020, amplifying domestic concerns on top of the global risk-off. FII outflows were severe and the rupee weakened sharply, so USD investors absorbed losses larger than the local-currency decline. The drawdown was rapid, running peak to trough in roughly eight weeks.","body_zh":"2020年1月至3月，印度下跌43.3%，由全球新冠疫情恐慌性抛售驱动。印度于2020年3月底实施全球最严格的封锁措施之一，在全球风险规避之上叠加国内担忧。FII大规模外流，卢比急剧贬值——美元投资者承受的损失超过本地货币跌幅。此次回撤迅速，从峰值到谷底约历时八周。","drivers":["Global COVID panic triggered a simultaneous EM equity and currency selloff","India's strict lockdown amplified domestic concerns","FII outflows were among the largest and fastest on record for India","INR depreciation pushed USD losses beyond the local-equity decline"],"drivers_zh":["全球新冠恐慌同步引发新兴市场股票与货币抛售","印度严格封锁叠加国内担忧","FII外流规模和速度为印度历史之最","卢比贬值使美元损失超过本地股市跌幅"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID shock: equity and rupee collapse","title_zh":"新冠冲击：股市与卢比双崩","turn_id":"inda:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"India's 152.8% USD rally from March 2020 to January 2022 was the largest leg in its 15-year window, driven by unprecedented global liquidity (Fed near-zero rates and QE), a surge in domestic retail participation, a strong corporate-earnings recovery off a low base, and the vaccination-led reopening. The rupee was broadly stable to modestly firmer versus the dollar through much of 2021, supporting USD total returns. Financials, tech, and consumer names led, reinforced by India's digitization and financial-inclusion story.","body_zh":"从2020年3月至2022年1月，印度以美元计价上涨152.8%，是其15年窗口内最大的一段涨势，由史无前例的全球流动性（美联储近零利率与量化宽松）、国内散户参与激增、企业盈利从低基数强劲复苏以及疫苗推动的经济重启共同驱动。卢比在2021年大部分时间内对美元大体稳定至温和走强，支撑美元总回报。金融、科技与消费板块领涨，印度数字化与普惠金融叙事进一步强化了行情。","drivers":["Global zero-rate QE powered EM risk assets, including India","A domestic retail-investor surge created a new demand base","Corporate earnings recovered strongly off a low COVID base","Broadly stable-to-firmer INR supported USD total returns"],"drivers_zh":["全球零利率量化宽松推动包括印度在内的新兴市场风险资产","国内散户大规模涌入形成新增需求基础","企业盈利从新冠低基数强劲复苏","卢比大体稳定至走强，支撑美元总回报"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Massive post-COVID bull run","title_zh":"新冠后大规模牛市","turn_id":"inda:trough:2020-03"},"2021-11-12":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:peak:2021-11"},"2022-03-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:trough:2022-03"},"2022-04-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:peak:2022-04"},"2022-06-17":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:trough:2022-06"},"2022-09-12":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:peak:2022-09"},"2023-03-15":{"body":"India rallied 55.9% from March 2023 to September 2024, bucking the broader EM tide on a rare combination of strong GDP growth (7%-plus prints), improving earnings, and political stability. India was widely seen as a beneficiary of supply-chain diversification away from China, drawing selective FII inflows even as much of EM struggled. The RBI managed the rupee relatively tightly, limiting USD-return leakage, though the currency drifted gradually weaker over the period.","body_zh":"从2023年3月至2024年9月，印度上涨55.9%，逆新兴市场大势而行，凭借强劲GDP增长（7%以上）、盈利改善及政治稳定脱颖而出。印度被广泛视为供应链\"去中国化\"多元化的受益者，在多数新兴市场举步维艰之际吸引了选择性FII流入。印储行对卢比进行了相对严格的管理，限制了美元回报损耗，尽管卢比在此期间缓慢走弱。","drivers":["7%-plus GDP growth made India a standout in a slowing EM universe","Supply-chain diversification narrative drove selective FII inflows","RBI FX management kept INR depreciation gradual, limiting USD drag","Domestic capex and financials drove earnings outperformance"],"drivers_zh":["7%以上的GDP增速使印度在放缓的新兴市场中脱颖而出","供应链多元化叙事驱动选择性FII流入","印储行汇率管理使卢比贬值保持渐进，限制美元拖累","国内资本开支与金融板块驱动盈利超预期"],"prev_key":"2023-03","prev_key_chain":["2023-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Resilient bull amid global tightening","title_zh":"全球紧缩背景下的韧性牛市","turn_id":"inda:trough:2023-03"},"2024-09-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"inda:peak:2024-09"},"2025-03-03":{"body":"INDA put in a brief 16.9% USD bounce from March to June 2025, a partial relief rally within a choppy stretch rather than a durable new uptrend. Per the cycle model this leg marked a local high before the subsequent correction, so it is best read as a counter-trend rebound that failed to hold rather than as a sustained re-rating.","body_zh":"INDA于2025年3月至6月以美元计价短暂反弹16.9%，是震荡阶段中的局部修复性反弹，而非持续的新上升趋势。按周期模型，此段为后续调整前的局部高点，更应理解为未能延续的逆势反弹，而非持续性的估值重估。","drivers":["Counter-trend relief bounce within a choppy stretch","Marked a local cycle high ahead of the subsequent drawdown","Did not develop into a durable uptrend"],"drivers_zh":["震荡阶段中的逆势修复性反弹","为后续回撤前的局部周期高点","未能演变为持续的上升趋势"],"prev_key":"2025-03","prev_key_chain":["2025-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Brief relief bounce","title_zh":"短暂的修复性反弹","turn_id":"inda:trough:2025-03"},"2025-06-27":{"body":"India fell 18.7% in USD terms from June 2025 to March 2026 in a valuation-and-flow reset typical of an India top: a stretched starting point met a less supportive global backdrop, FII appetite faded, and the rupee softened, compounding the USD drawdown. This was a relatively shallow, orderly correction by India's historical standards rather than a crisis-scale crash. (Note: figures beyond late 2025 are model-derived; specific catalyst details for this window are not independently confirmed.)","body_zh":"从2025年6月至2026年3月，印度以美元计价下跌18.7%，是典型的印度顶部式估值与资金重置：偏高的起点遭遇不那么有利的全球环境，FII偏好减弱，卢比走软，放大了美元跌幅。按印度历史标准，这是一次相对温和、有序的调整，而非危机级别的暴跌。（注：2025年末之后的数据为模型推导，本窗口具体催化剂细节未经独立证实。）","drivers":["Stretched starting valuations left India vulnerable to a reset","Fading FII appetite pressured equities and the rupee together","INR softness compounded the USD drawdown","Shallow, orderly correction rather than a crisis-scale crash"],"drivers_zh":["偏高的起始估值使印度易受重置冲击","FII偏好减弱同时压制股市与卢比","卢比走软放大美元跌幅","相对温和、有序的调整，而非危机级别暴跌"],"prev_key":"2025-06","prev_key_chain":["2025-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Valuation reset and EM-cycle drawdown","title_zh":"估值修正与新兴市场周期回撤","turn_id":"inda:peak:2025-06"}},"now":"India (INDA) is in an Expansion phase after troughing in March 2026, but sits at only 39.1/100 of its cycle range and remains below its 200-day moving average -- the recovery is young and the market has not yet reclaimed the ground lost in the 2025-2026 correction. Relative strength versus SPY is firmly negative over the past 63 days (-8.2%), ranking 14th among tracked markets, consistent with an EM laggard still in catch-up mode against US equities. The model's projected next turn is a peak around November 2026, implying roughly a five-month expansion window from here, though the below-200d, low-cycle-position read argues for confirmation before pressing the recovery.","now_zh":"印度（INDA）于2026年3月触底后进入扩张阶段，但当前周期位置仅为39.1/100，仍位于200日均线下方——复苏尚处早期，市场尚未收复2025至2026年调整中失去的失地。相对于SPY的63日相对强度明显为负（-8.2%），在被跟踪市场中排名第14，符合一个仍在追赶美股的新兴市场落后者特征。模型预计下一个转折点（峰值）约在2026年11月，意味着从当前起约有五个月的扩张窗口；但鉴于价格仍处200日均线下方、周期位置偏低，宜在确认后再追高复苏。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"tur":{"legs":{"2011-12-19":{"body":"After the 2011 global risk-off sell-off, Turkey rode a broad EM recovery. The lira was relatively stable in 2012-2013, so the strong local equity rally translated almost fully into a 98.7% USD gain. Robust domestic demand, low real rates, and global appetite for high-yield EM debt fueled the move. The leg ended when the Fed's May 2013 taper-tantrum signal triggered a sharp TRY sell-off and EM capital outflows.","body_zh":"2011年全球避险抛售后，土耳其随新兴市场整体复苏。2012至2013年间里拉相对稳定，本地股市的强劲涨幅几乎完整转化为98.7%的美元回报。旺盛的国内需求、低实际利率及全球对高收益新兴市场债券的追捧共同推动行情。2013年5月美联储释放缩减购债信号后，里拉急跌、新兴市场资本外流，这一段行情终结。","drivers":["Broad EM risk-on recovery","TRY stability amplifying local gains","Low global rates driving EM carry demand","Strong Turkish domestic credit growth"],"drivers_zh":["新兴市场整体风险偏好回升","里拉稳定放大本地涨幅","全球低利率推动新兴市场套息需求","国内信贷扩张强劲"],"prev_key":"2011-12","prev_key_chain":["2011-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis EM bounce, TRY stable","title_zh":"危机后新兴市场反弹，里拉相对稳定","turn_id":"tur:trough:2011-12"},"2013-05-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2013-05"},"2013-08-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:trough:2013-08"},"2013-09-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2013-09"},"2014-02-03":{"body":"After the taper tantrum and a late-2013 domestic corruption scandal, TUR staged a 53% rebound from depressed levels. The CBRT's emergency rate hike in January 2014 (one-week repo to 10%) defended the lira and restored some credibility, while EM risk appetite partly recovered. The bounce was short-lived as geopolitical tension and renewed lira weakness reasserted by mid-2014.","body_zh":"经历缩债恐慌与2013年底国内腐败丑闻的双重打击后，TUR从低位反弹53%。土央行于2014年1月紧急加息（一周回购利率升至10%）以捍卫里拉，部分恢复市场信心，新兴市场风险偏好亦有所回暖。但好景不长，地缘政治紧张与里拉再度走弱于2014年中卷土重来，行情消退。","drivers":["Emergency CBRT rate hike stabilizing the lira","Post-taper EM stabilization","Local equity oversold bounce","Temporary compression of political risk premium"],"drivers_zh":["土央行紧急加息稳定里拉","缩债恐慌后新兴市场趋稳","本地股市超卖反弹","政治风险溢价短暂收窄"],"prev_key":"2014-02","prev_key_chain":["2014-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-taper stabilization, brief relief","title_zh":"缩债恐慌后短暂企稳反弹","turn_id":"tur:trough:2014-02"},"2014-07-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2014-07"},"2015-09-09":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:trough:2015-09"},"2015-11-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2015-11"},"2016-01-21":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:trough:2016-01"},"2016-04-20":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2016-04"},"2017-01-11":{"body":"The 2016-2017 global reflation trade and recovering commodity prices lifted EM broadly, with Turkey gaining 61.2% in USD terms. A softer dollar boosted USD-denominated EM returns, and the lira stabilized temporarily. The leg ran into late 2017, ending as lira weakness and inflation concerns resurfaced.","body_zh":"2016至2017年全球再通胀交易与大宗商品价格回升推动新兴市场普涨，土耳其以美元计上涨61.2%。美元走弱推升美元计价的新兴市场回报，里拉阶段性企稳。行情延续至2017年底，随里拉贬值与通胀担忧重现而终结。","drivers":["Global reflation trade lifting EM","Softer dollar boosting USD-denominated EM returns","Commodity price recovery supporting EM current accounts","Temporary lira stabilization"],"drivers_zh":["全球再通胀交易提振新兴市场","美元走弱推升美元计价EM回报","大宗商品价格回升改善新兴市场经常账户","里拉阶段性企稳"],"prev_key":"2017-01","prev_key_chain":["2017-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Global reflation, EM carry revival","title_zh":"全球再通胀，新兴市场套息回归","turn_id":"tur:trough:2017-01"},"2017-09-01":{"body":"Turkey's chronic current-account deficit and reliance on short-term external financing collided with rising US rates and a stronger dollar. The lira sold off persistently from late 2017, and the crisis intensified in August 2018 when a US-Turkey diplomatic rift and sanctions triggered a 40%+ TRY crash within weeks. The ETF fell 58.1% in USD — far deeper than local equity losses, with FX the dominant driver — and Turkey entered recession by end-2018.","body_zh":"土耳其长期的经常账户赤字与对短期外债的高度依赖，在美国加息、美元走强背景下积重难返。里拉自2017年底持续贬值，2018年8月美土外交冲突与制裁令TRY数周内暴跌逾40%，危机全面爆发。ETF以美元计下跌58.1%，远超本地股市跌幅，汇率为主导因素；土耳其于2018年底陷入衰退。","drivers":["TRY collapse — 40%+ in weeks amid US-Turkey rift and sanctions","Rising US rates draining EM carry","Current account deficit exceeding 6% of GDP","Political interference in CBRT undermining credibility"],"drivers_zh":["美土冲突与制裁下里拉数周内暴跌逾40%","美国加息抽走新兴市场套息资金","经常账户赤字超过GDP的6%","政治干预央行损害公信力"],"prev_key":"2017-09","prev_key_chain":["2017-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Lira crisis: external debt spiral","title_zh":"里拉危机：外债螺旋式恶化","turn_id":"tur:peak:2017-09"},"2018-08-13":{"body":"With the lira in free fall, the CBRT raised its policy rate aggressively to 24% in September 2018, sparking a sharp short-covering rally. Cheap valuations after the 58% USD crash drew contrarian buyers, the lira stabilized, and global EM steadied after 2018's broad sell-off. The move recovered roughly half the prior crash (52.4% up into early 2019) before fading as structural imbalances persisted.","body_zh":"里拉持续暴跌之际，土央行于2018年9月大幅加息至24%，触发空头回补反弹。58%的美元跌幅令估值极度低廉，吸引逆向买家入场，里拉企稳，全球新兴市场经历2018年广泛抛售后逐步止跌。此轮反弹收复约一半前期跌幅（至2019年初上涨52.4%），随后随深层结构性失衡延续而消退。","drivers":["CBRT emergency 24% rate hike stabilizing the lira","Deep oversold valuation after the USD crash","Global EM stabilization in late 2018","Short-covering in a heavily shorted market"],"drivers_zh":["土央行紧急加息至24%稳定里拉","美元暴跌后估值极度超卖","2018年末全球新兴市场趋稳","重度做空市场的空头回补"],"prev_key":"2018-08","prev_key_chain":["2018-08"],"status":"exact","title":"Emergency rate hike stabilization bounce","title_zh":"紧急加息触底反弹","turn_id":"tur:trough:2018-08"},"2019-01-30":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2019-01"},"2019-05-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:trough:2019-05"},"2020-01-21":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-20":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:trough:2020-03"},"2020-07-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2020-07"},"2020-10-30":{"body":"After a volatile 2019-2020 marked by renewed lira stress and the COVID shock, TUR rallied 68.6% from October 2020. A late-2020 change in CBRT leadership raised hopes for a return to monetary orthodoxy; the central bank hiked rates, attracting carry flows, and the lira appreciated meaningfully in this window — making FX a contributor rather than a headwind. The leg ended in early 2021 when the orthodox pivot was reversed.","body_zh":"经历2019至2020年里拉再度承压与新冠冲击的动荡期后，TUR自2020年10月反弹68.6%。2020年底央行换帅，市场对货币政策回归正统燃起希望，央行加息吸引套息资金，里拉在此阶段明显升值，使汇率因素难得成为正贡献而非阻力。随着2021年初正统转向被逆转，行情终结。","drivers":["CBRT leadership change signaling policy orthodoxy","Lira appreciation adding to USD returns","Carry inflows on rising policy rates","Global EM risk-on post-COVID recovery"],"drivers_zh":["央行换帅带来政策回归正统预期","里拉升值为美元回报加分","加息吸引套息资金流入","新冠后全球新兴市场风险偏好回升"],"prev_key":"2020-10","prev_key_chain":["2020-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Policy-orthodoxy hope, lira rebound","title_zh":"政策正统化预期，里拉回升","turn_id":"tur:trough:2020-10"},"2021-02-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2021-02"},"2021-12-17":{"body":"Erdogan pressured the CBRT to cut rates aggressively from late 2021 despite spiraling inflation. The lira collapsed sharply against the dollar, yet Borsa Istanbul soared as Turks and institutions piled into equities as an inflation hedge. TUR gained 128% in USD terms into January 2023 — a rare outcome where local equity appreciation was so extreme it outpaced severe FX drag. The leg ended as inflation and FX-reserve pressures peaked.","body_zh":"埃尔多安自2021年底向央行施压，在通胀飙升之际仍持续大幅降息。里拉对美元剧烈贬值，但伊斯坦布尔证交所急剧飙升——土耳其居民与机构大举涌入股市对冲通胀。TUR至2023年1月以美元计涨幅高达128%，这一罕见结果源于本地股市涨幅之猛烈，足以抵消严峻汇损。随通胀与外汇储备压力见顶，行情终结。","drivers":["Borsa Istanbul as inflation hedge — explosive local gains","Aggressive rate cuts despite very high inflation","Severe FX drag offset by extreme local equity surge","Intermittent global EM risk appetite support"],"drivers_zh":["博尔萨伊斯坦布尔成为通胀对冲工具，本地涨幅惊人","通胀高企之际仍激进降息","严峻汇损被本地股市极端涨幅抵消","全球新兴市场风险偏好阶段性支撑"],"prev_key":"2021-12","prev_key_chain":["2021-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Unorthodox cuts fuel equity surge","title_zh":"非正统降息催生股市暴涨","turn_id":"tur:trough:2021-12"},"2022-04-20":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2022-04"},"2022-07-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:trough:2022-07"},"2023-01-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"tur:peak:2023-01"},"2023-06-22":{"body":"After the May 2023 elections, Erdogan's re-election was followed by a surprising pivot to orthodoxy: Mehmet Simsek returned as finance minister and the CBRT began aggressive rate hikes, eventually above 40%. This restored international investor confidence; the lira weakened in a more controlled fashion, and foreign inflows returned. The 62.4% USD gain into July 2024 reflected recovering local equities and a lower FX-volatility premium.","body_zh":"2023年5月大选后埃尔多安连任，随即出人意料地转向正统：穆罕默德·希姆谢克回任财长，土央行开启激进加息，利率最终升至40%以上。这一转变重拾国际投资者信心，里拉以更可控节奏贬值，外资回流。至2024年7月62.4%的美元涨幅，既反映本地股市企稳回升，也体现汇率波动溢价收窄。","drivers":["Orthodox pivot — Simsek appointment and CBRT hikes above 40%","Lower lira volatility reducing FX risk premium","Foreign-investor re-engagement on carry and reform","Recovering local equities"],"drivers_zh":["回归正统——希姆谢克就任与央行加息至40%以上","里拉波动率下降，汇率风险溢价收窄","套息与改革叙事吸引外资重返","本地股市企稳回升"],"prev_key":"2023-05","prev_key_chain":["2023-05"],"rekey_shift_days":38,"status":"shifted","title":"Post-election orthodox pivot","title_zh":"选后政策转向正统","turn_id":"tur:trough:2023-06"},"2024-05-21":{"body":"The 31.6% down leg from July 2024 to May 2025 reflected stalling disinflation with inflation still very high, renewed political and geopolitical concerns, and a stretch of broad EM underperformance versus US equities. The lira ground lower on the persistent current-account deficit, and foreign capital that had re-engaged post-election began rotating back out as the policy-easing path advanced.","body_zh":"2024年7月至2025年5月间31.6%的下跌，源于通胀仍高企、去通胀进程停滞，政治与地缘担忧重现，以及新兴市场相对美股整体走弱三重压力叠加。里拉在经常账户持续赤字下缓慢走低，选后重返的外资随宽松路径推进而开始流出。","drivers":["Disinflation stalling with inflation still elevated","EM underperformance vs US equities","Lira grinding lower on persistent current-account deficit","Foreign capital rotating out as easing advanced"],"drivers_zh":["通胀仍高企，去通胀停滞","新兴市场相对美股走弱","里拉在经常账户持续赤字下缓慢走低","宽松推进之际外资流出"],"prev_key":"2024-07","prev_key_chain":["2024-07"],"rekey_shift_days":55,"status":"shifted","title":"Disinflation stall, capital rotation out","title_zh":"去通胀停滞，资本流出","turn_id":"tur:peak:2024-05"},"2025-06-20":{"body":"From the May 2025 trough, TUR gained 49.6% in USD terms into a May 2026 peak amid a broader EM risk-on environment and renewed carry interest. The ETF then rolled into a Downturn phase; positioning sits mid-cycle at 54.8/100, and the model projects the next trough around October 2026. With this window extending past reliable verification, the read here is quantitative rather than catalyst-specific.","body_zh":"自2025年5月低点起，TUR至2026年5月见顶，以美元计上涨49.6%，受新兴市场整体风险偏好回暖与套息需求回升推动。此后ETF转入下行阶段；当前位置处于周期中段54.8/100，模型预测下一低点约在2026年10月。鉴于该窗口已超出可靠核实范围，此处以量化判断为主，不强行归因具体催化剂。","drivers":["Broad EM risk-on tailwind into 2026","Renewed carry interest on positive real rates","Recovery from the May 2025 trough","Subsequent rotation into a Downturn phase (model-based)"],"drivers_zh":["2026年前新兴市场整体风险偏好顺风","正实际利率下套息需求回升","自2025年5月低点回升","随后转入下行阶段（基于模型）"],"prev_key":"2025-05","prev_key_chain":["2025-05"],"rekey_shift_days":36,"status":"shifted","title":"Carry recovery, then Downturn","title_zh":"套息回暖，随后转入下行","turn_id":"tur:trough:2025-06"}},"now":"TUR is in Downturn phase at position 54.8/100, having peaked in May 2026 — mid-cycle, neither washed-out nor overextended. The ETF is down roughly 10% relative to SPY over the past 63 days, ranking 17th of 24 single-country markets tracked. Despite local Istanbul indices repeatedly hitting nominal record highs on lira-depreciation mechanics, the USD-denominated ETF shows a net negative 15-year window return (about -4%), underscoring how chronic TRY devaluation erodes USD-investor gains. The model projects the next trough around October 2026.","now_zh":"TUR目前处于下行阶段，位置指数54.8/100，于2026年5月见顶——处于周期中段，既未超卖也未明显过热。过去63个交易日相对SPY下跌约10%，在24个被跟踪的单一国家市场中排名第17。尽管伊斯坦布尔本地股指因里拉持续贬值而屡创名义新高，但以美元计价的ETF在15年窗口内总回报为负（约-4%），凸显土耳其里拉长期贬值对美元投资者收益的侵蚀。模型预测下一个低点约在2026年10月。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"aaxj":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"body":"After the 2011 global growth scare driven by the European sovereign debt crisis and the US debt-ceiling standoff, Asian equities bottomed in October 2011. The subsequent 64.2% advance to April 2015 was supported by China's still-robust GDP growth, PBOC easing, and regional export demand. The US dollar traded broadly sideways through much of 2012-2014, keeping currency conditions neutral-to-favourable for USD-denominated investors. The leg topped in 2015 as China's domestic equity bubble inflated and then burst, with the August 2015 CNY devaluation triggering a sharp repricing of Asian FX and equities.","body_zh":"2011年欧洲主权债务危机与美国债务上限僵局引发全球增长恐慌，亚洲股市于2011年10月触底。随后至2015年4月累计上涨64.2%，中国仍然稳健的GDP增速、中国人民银行的宽松政策以及区域出口需求共同支撑了这波行情。2012至2014年间美元总体横盘，为以美元计价的投资者提供了中性偏有利的货币环境。这段行情于2015年见顶，中国国内股市泡沫膨胀后破裂，同年8月人民币贬值引发亚洲汇率与股市的剧烈重定价。","drivers":["China GDP growth and PBOC easing","Sideways USD providing a neutral-to-favourable FX backdrop","Regional export demand","Post-crisis global risk-on recovery"],"prev_key":"2011-10","prev_key_chain":["2011-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-crisis Asian recovery","title_zh":"危机后亚洲复苏","turn_id":"aaxj:trough:2011-10"},"2015-04-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"aaxj:peak:2015-04"},"2015-08-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"aaxj:trough:2015-08"},"2015-10-23":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"aaxj:peak:2015-10"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"Following the January 2016 trough driven by China hard-landing fears and CNY devaluation anxiety, AAXJ rallied 84.4% into January 2018. The recovery was fuelled by a genuine upturn in global trade volumes, China's 2016 stimulus, and a weakening dollar as the Fed's hiking cycle proved shallower than feared. Asian technology — Chinese internet platforms and Korean/Taiwanese chipmakers benefiting from a memory upcycle — led the outperformance, while firmer Asian currencies added an FX tailwind to USD returns.","body_zh":"2016年1月受中国硬着陆恐惧与人民币贬值焦虑拖累触底后，AAXJ至2018年1月累计反弹84.4%。全球贸易量真实回升、中国2016年的刺激政策，以及美联储加息幅度不及预期导致美元走弱，共同推动了这波复苏。亚洲科技板块——中国互联网平台与受存储芯片上行周期提振的台韩芯片企业——引领超额表现，亚洲货币走强为美元回报贡献了汇率顺风。","drivers":["China stimulus in 2016","Weak USD and broad EM liquidity easing","China internet and Korea/Taiwan memory upcycle","Global trade volume recovery"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Synchronized global reflation surge","title_zh":"全球同步再通胀浪潮","turn_id":"aaxj:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"aaxj:peak:2018-01"},"2018-10-29":{"body":"After the January 2018 top, escalating US-China tariff conflict and the resulting USD strength dragged AAXJ through a protracted correction. The October 2018 trough marked peak trade-war pessimism, with the CNY having weakened sharply and Asian tech deeply beaten down. The subsequent 29.2% advance into January 2020 was a relief rally rather than a fresh bull market: a late-2018 trade truce, the Fed's early-2019 pivot to pausing hikes, and some CNY stabilisation allowed multiples to partially recover, though the move was modest relative to prior legs.","body_zh":"2018年1月见顶后，中美关税冲突升级以及由此引发的美元走强将AAXJ拖入漫长调整。2018年10月的低点标志着贸易战悲观情绪的高峰，人民币大幅走弱，亚洲科技股遭到深度抛售。随后至2020年1月29.2%的反弹属于技术性修复而非全新牛市：2018年底贸易休战、美联储2019年初转向暂停加息以及人民币趋稳，推动估值部分修复，但涨幅相对于前几轮行情较为温和。","drivers":["US-China trade truce in late 2018","Fed pivot to a rate pause in early 2019","CNY stabilisation after sharp depreciation","Partial EM multiple recovery"],"prev_key":"2018-10","prev_key_chain":["2018-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade-war truce relief bounce","title_zh":"贸易战休战的修复反弹","turn_id":"aaxj:trough:2018-10"},"2020-01-13":{"body":"The COVID-19 pandemic triggered a rapid 29.5% drawdown from January to March 2020 as China became the initial epicentre and regional supply chains seized up. The shock was sharp but brief: Asian governments responded quickly, and China's factory closures proved shorter than feared. The USD initially surged on safe-haven demand, amplifying losses for USD investors in Asian assets, before the Fed's emergency rate cuts and QE reversed the dollar.","body_zh":"新冠疫情从2020年1月至3月引发了29.5%的急速下跌，中国成为最初的震中，区域供应链陷入停摆。冲击虽剧烈但持续时间较短：亚洲各国政府迅速行动，中国工厂停产的影响短于预期。美元初期因避险需求飙升，放大了以美元计价的亚洲资产损失，随后美联储紧急降息与量化宽松使美元方向逆转。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic with China as initial epicentre","Global supply chain disruption","USD safe-haven surge amplifying losses","Rapid policy response limiting duration"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash — sharpest drawdown on record","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击——最急速的下跌","turn_id":"aaxj:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The March 2020 trough launched a 91.9% advance into February 2021, the fastest and largest recovery leg in the 15-year window. Fed QE, US fiscal stimulus, and a falling dollar fuelled heavy EM inflows. China's V-shaped industrial recovery led the region, while Korean and Taiwanese chipmakers benefited from a work-from-home electronics demand surge. The leg topped in February 2021 just as Beijing began signalling regulatory pressure on its internet and fintech giants, with the November 2020 cancellation of Ant Group's IPO serving as the first major warning shot.","body_zh":"2020年3月低点触发了一轮91.9%的涨幅，直至2021年2月，是15年窗口内最快、最大的复苏行情。美联储量化宽松、美国财政刺激以及美元下跌催生了大量新兴市场资金流入。中国工业产出V形复苏引领区域，台韩芯片企业受益于居家办公带动的电子产品需求激增。行情恰在北京开始释放对互联网与金融科技巨头监管压力信号时见顶，2020年11月蚂蚁集团IPO被叫停成为第一声重要警报。","drivers":["Fed QE and USD depreciation fuelling EM inflows","China V-shaped industrial recovery","Work-from-home electronics demand for Taiwan/Korea chips","Regulatory signals on China tech triggering the top"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-COVID reflation and China tech peak","title_zh":"疫后再通胀与中国科技顶部","turn_id":"aaxj:trough:2020-03"},"2021-02-17":{"body":"The 44.5% decline from February 2021 to October 2022 was the deepest bear leg in AAXJ's 15-year history. China's sweeping crackdowns across education, gaming, ride-hailing and internet platforms erased large amounts of market cap from the index's biggest constituents. Simultaneously, the Fed's inflation-fighting hiking cycle from early 2022 strengthened the dollar, with CNY and KRW both depreciating. China's zero-COVID policy extended the pain through most of 2022 by disrupting supply chains and suppressing demand, while energy inflation weighed on India and Southeast Asia.","body_zh":"从2021年2月至2022年10月下跌44.5%，是AAXJ 15年历史中最深的熊市行情。中国对教育、游戏、网约车及互联网平台的大规模整顿从指数最大权重股中抹去了巨额市值。与此同时，美联储自2022年初启动的抗通胀加息周期推强美元，人民币与韩元均明显贬值。中国坚持动态清零政策延续了整个2022年大部分时间的痛苦，供应链持续受扰，消费需求被压制，而能源通胀则打击了印度和东南亚。","drivers":["China tech and private-sector regulatory crackdown","Fed hiking cycle strengthening USD vs Asian currencies","China zero-COVID disrupting supply chains and demand","Energy inflation pressuring India and SE Asia"],"prev_key":"2021-02","prev_key_chain":["2021-02"],"status":"exact","title":"China regulatory bear — the deepest leg","title_zh":"中国监管熊市——最深的下行","turn_id":"aaxj:peak:2021-02"},"2022-10-24":{"body":"October 2022 marked the trough for both US rate expectations and Chinese regulatory/COVID pessimism. China announced its pivot away from zero-COVID in late 2022, delivering a reopening rally that lifted the index's largest weight, while Taiwan and Korea semiconductors recovered as the global memory inventory correction cleared through 2023-2024. The 54.7% advance to October 2024 was steady but uneven: India contributed consistent gains while China disappointed on the durability of its recovery, capping the index's outperformance vs SPY.","body_zh":"2022年10月同时标志着美国利率预期与中国监管/疫情悲观情绪的触底。中国于2022年底宣布退出动态清零政策，引发重开行情，提振了指数中权重最大的成分；随着2023至2024年间全球存储库存去化，台湾和韩国半导体回升。至2024年10月54.7%的涨幅稳健但参差不齐：印度贡献了持续收益，而中国复苏的可持续性令市场失望，制约了指数相对标普500的超额表现。","drivers":["China zero-COVID exit and reopening rally","Fed rate expectations peaking and stabilising","Global memory inventory correction clearing","India steady structural growth contribution"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"EM reopening and semis upcycle","title_zh":"新兴市场重开与半导体上行周期","turn_id":"aaxj:trough:2022-10"},"2023-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"aaxj:peak:2023-01"},"2023-10-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"aaxj:trough:2023-10"},"2024-10-07":{"body":"The 19.7% decline from October 2024 to April 2025 reflected two convergent shocks: post-US-election fears of tariff escalation under the incoming administration, which hit China-exposed names hardest, and the fading of China's September 2024 stimulus euphoria as follow-through measures disappointed. The TWD and KRW weakened on trade uncertainty, amplifying USD-denominated losses, while India also corrected from the stretched valuations built up during its 2023-2024 bull run.","body_zh":"2024年10月至2025年4月下跌19.7%，反映了两股力量的汇聚：美国大选后市场对新政府关税升级的担忧对涉华标的打击最重，以及中国2024年9月刺激政策的亢奋情绪因后续跟进措施不及预期而消退。贸易不确定性导致台币与韩元走弱，放大了美元计价的损失；印度也从2023至2024年牛市中累积的高估值大幅回调。","drivers":["Tariff escalation fears under the incoming US administration","China September 2024 stimulus follow-through disappointment","TWD and KRW depreciation amplifying USD losses","India valuation correction after an extended bull run"],"prev_key":"2024-10","prev_key_chain":["2024-10"],"status":"exact","title":"China stimulus fade and tariff fear","title_zh":"中国刺激褪色与关税恐慌","turn_id":"aaxj:peak:2024-10"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From the April 2025 trough, AAXJ has risen 95.5% into mid-2026 — the dominant move in the current window. The advance has been led by the AI semiconductor complex: Taiwan, anchored by TSMC's central role in AI infrastructure, and Korean memory makers benefiting from surging HBM demand. A weaker USD through 2025 amplified local-currency gains into stronger USD returns, while China contributed more modestly as domestic stimulus partly offset persistent foreign-investor caution. As this leg runs into months beyond reliable knowledge, treat its specific drivers as provisional: the verified signal is the magnitude (a roughly 95.5% rally) leaving the index at a stretched Peak (position 81.5/100), where it is highly exposed to any AI-capex demand rollover or renewed dollar strength.","body_zh":"自2025年4月低点起，AAXJ至2026年年中累计上涨95.5%，是当前窗口内的主导行情。涨势由AI半导体板块引领：以台积电在AI基础设施中的核心地位为支撑的台湾，以及受益于HBM高带宽内存需求激增的韩国存储企业。2025年美元走弱将本币涨幅放大为更强的美元回报，而中国贡献相对有限，国内刺激部分抵消了外资持续的谨慎态度。由于这段行情延伸至可靠认知之外的月份，其具体驱动因素应视为暂定：可验证的信号是涨幅本身（约95.5%），使指数处于偏高的顶峰（位置81.5/100），对任何AI资本开支需求回落或美元重新走强高度敏感。","drivers":["Taiwan AI semiconductor leadership (TSMC complex)","Korea HBM memory demand for AI","USD weakness amplifying local-currency gains","China domestic stimulus partially offsetting foreign-investor caution"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"AI semiconductor-led surge","title_zh":"AI半导体主导的上行","turn_id":"aaxj:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"AAXJ sits at a cycle Peak with a position of 81.5/100, well into stretched territory after a 95.5% rally from the April 2025 trough. The fund ranks first in relative strength among all tracked markets over the past 63 days (+7.3% vs SPY), led by Taiwan's TSMC-anchored AI semiconductor surge and South Korea's memory-chip recovery, with a broadly weaker USD lifting USD-denominated Asian returns. At this elevation the index is effectively pricing in sustained AI capex and benign US-Asia trade conditions; any demand-destruction signal or renewed dollar strength would pose material downside from current levels.","now_zh":"AAXJ目前处于周期顶峰，位置读数81.5/100，估值明显偏高——自2025年4月低点以来累计上涨95.5%。过去63个交易日相对标普500强出7.3个百分点，为所有跟踪市场中相对强度排名第一。台湾台积电主导的AI半导体行情与韩国存储芯片复苏共同领涨，美元走弱进一步放大了以美元计价的亚洲回报。在当前高位，市场已隐含AI资本开支持续扩张及美亚贸易环境平稳的预期，一旦需求侧出现降温信号或美元重新走强，回调风险不容忽视。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"eem":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eem:trough:2011-10"},"2012-03-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eem:peak:2012-03"},"2012-06-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eem:trough:2012-06"},"2013-01-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eem:peak:2013-01"},"2013-06-24":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eem:trough:2013-06"},"2014-09-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eem:peak:2014-09"},"2016-01-20":{"body":"From January 2016 to January 2018, EEM surged 91.7% as a topping US dollar, China's credit-driven reflation, and a synchronized global recovery lifted the asset class. The Fed adopted a more cautious, gradual stance after early-2016 volatility, stabilizing EM currencies and easing borrowing conditions. Chinese stimulus — particularly infrastructure and housing credit — revived commodity demand, benefiting commodity-exporting EM economies alongside the China-heavy index. EM currencies recovered against the dollar, providing an additional tailwind for USD-based investors.","body_zh":"2016年1月至2018年1月，EEM大涨91.7%，受益于美元见顶、中国信贷驱动的再通胀以及全球经济同步复苏。受2016年初市场波动影响，美联储转向更谨慎、渐进的立场，稳定了新兴市场货币并降低了借贷成本。中国在基础设施和房地产信贷方面的刺激重振了大宗商品需求，使商品出口型新兴市场经济体以及指数中的中国权重受益。新兴市场货币对美元走强，为美元计价投资者提供了额外顺风。","drivers":["Fed cautious/gradual stance, USD peak","China credit-driven reflation (infrastructure, housing)","Commodity price recovery","Synchronized global growth, EM FX appreciation"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"EM Bull: Dollar Turn & China Reflation","title_zh":"新兴市场牛市：美元见顶与中国再通胀","turn_id":"eem:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eem:peak:2018-01"},"2018-10-29":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"eem:trough:2018-10"},"2020-01-13":{"body":"From January to March 2020, EEM fell 33.9% as the COVID-19 pandemic triggered a global risk-off liquidation. Dollar funding stress sent the DXY sharply higher, inflicting additional losses on EM assets in USD terms. Commodity prices collapsed (WTI futures went negative in late April 2020), hitting LatAm and EMEA constituents hard. The selloff was fast and indiscriminate, compressing all EM regions simultaneously.","body_zh":"2020年1月至3月，EEM下跌33.9%，新冠疫情引发全球风险资产抛售。美元融资紧张推动美元指数急升，以美元计价的新兴市场资产损失进一步扩大。大宗商品价格崩塌（WTI原油期货在4月底一度跌为负值），重创拉美和EMEA成分。此次抛售迅猛且无差别，各新兴市场区域同步承压。","drivers":["Global risk-off, USD funding squeeze","Commodity collapse (oil, metals)","EM capital flight, currency depreciation","Pandemic lockdown demand shock"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Shock: Synchronized EM Drawdown","title_zh":"新冠冲击：新兴市场同步大幅回撤","turn_id":"eem:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From March 2020 to February 2021, EEM rallied 92.4% on Fed zero rates and QE, a sharp weakening of the dollar (DXY fell roughly 10-12% from its March 2020 peak into year-end), and China's early exit from COVID lockdowns enabling a V-shaped industrial recovery. Chinese internet mega-caps (Tencent, Alibaba, Meituan) and Taiwan Semiconductor surged on accelerating digitalization demand, contributing outsized index gains. Dollar depreciation boosted USD-translated returns on top of strong local-currency performance.","body_zh":"2020年3月至2021年2月，EEM大涨92.4%，受益于美联储零利率与量化宽松、美元急剧走弱（美元指数自2020年3月高点至年底下跌约10-12%），以及中国率先退出封控、工业呈现V形复苏。中国互联网巨头（腾讯、阿里巴巴、美团）和台积电受数字化需求加速推动大幅上涨，对指数贡献超高。美元贬值在强劲本币表现之上进一步提升了美元计价回报。","drivers":["Fed ZIRP + QE, DXY decline","China early COVID exit, industrial V-recovery","China internet & Taiwan tech mega-cap surge","EM currency appreciation vs USD"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-COVID EM Bull: China Tech & Weak Dollar","title_zh":"疫后新兴市场牛市：中国科技与美元走弱","turn_id":"eem:trough:2020-03"},"2021-02-17":{"body":"From February 2021 to October 2022, EEM fell 39.8% as the Fed pivoted to its most aggressive tightening cycle in decades, pushing the DXY to two-decade highs and pressuring EM currencies and debt. Simultaneously, China launched sweeping regulatory crackdowns on its internet and education sectors through 2021, erasing large amounts of market cap from index heavyweights. The Russia-Ukraine war from early 2022 added commodity volatility and risk aversion, while China's zero-COVID policy curtailed economic activity.","body_zh":"2021年2月至2022年10月，EEM下跌39.8%。美联储转向数十年来最激进的紧缩周期，推动美元指数升至20年高位，压制新兴市场货币和债务。与此同时，中国2021年对互联网和教育行业展开大规模监管整治，指数重仓股市值大幅蒸发。2022年初起的俄乌战争加剧了大宗商品波动和避险情绪，而中国的清零政策则压制了经济活动。","drivers":["Fed tightening, DXY two-decade high, USD surge","China internet & education regulatory crackdown","China zero-COVID economic suppression","Russia-Ukraine war, commodity volatility, risk aversion"],"prev_key":"2021-02","prev_key_chain":["2021-02"],"status":"exact","title":"EM Bear: Fed Tightening & China Crackdown","title_zh":"新兴市场熊市：美联储紧缩与中国监管整治","turn_id":"eem:peak:2021-02"},"2022-10-24":{"body":"From October 2022 to October 2024, EEM gained 46.5% as the dollar peaked and retreated from two-decade highs, China abruptly ended its zero-COVID policy in late 2022 sparking a reopening rally, and Taiwan and South Korea benefited from rising AI-related semiconductor demand. The China reopening drove sharp gains into early 2023, but the recovery proved uneven as the property sector remained distressed; Taiwan and India increasingly carried the index. The leg was moderate relative to prior cycles given persistent China property headwinds and periodic USD rebounds.","body_zh":"2022年10月至2024年10月，EEM上涨46.5%。美元自20年高位见顶回落，中国于2022年底突然结束清零政策引发重开放行情，台湾和韩国受益于AI相关半导体需求上升。中国重开放推动2023年初大幅上涨，但受地产行业持续低迷拖累，复苏节奏不均；台湾和印度日益成为指数的主要支撑。相较于以往周期，本轮反弹因中国地产顽疾和美元阶段性反弹而显得温和。","drivers":["USD peak & reversal from two-decade highs","China zero-COVID exit, reopening demand","Taiwan & South Korea AI semiconductor tailwind","India structural growth offsetting China drag"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"EM Recovery: Reopening Hope & Peak Dollar","title_zh":"新兴市场复苏：重开放预期与美元见顶","turn_id":"eem:trough:2022-10"},"2024-10-07":{"body":"From October 2024 to April 2025, EEM declined 17.3% as the dollar strengthened on resilient US growth and sticky inflation expectations, compressing EM asset valuations in USD terms. China's late-2024 stimulus announcements initially sparked a rally that faded when markets questioned the scale and follow-through of fiscal measures. EM currencies broadly weakened against a re-strengthening dollar, amplifying the drawdown across the index's currency-sensitive holdings.","body_zh":"2024年10月至2025年4月，EEM下跌17.3%。美国经济韧性和通胀预期黏性支撑美元走强，以美元计价的新兴市场资产估值承压。中国2024年末的刺激公告初期触发上涨，但市场随即质疑财政措施的力度与落实，行情回落。新兴市场货币普遍对再度走强的美元贬值，放大了指数中汇率敏感持仓的回撤幅度。","drivers":["USD re-strengthening, DXY rebound","China stimulus disappointment, property overhang","EM currency headwinds","Global risk appetite compression"],"prev_key":"2024-10","prev_key_chain":["2024-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Pullback: Strong Dollar & China Stimulus Doubts","title_zh":"回调：强势美元与中国刺激存疑","turn_id":"eem:peak:2024-10"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From April 2025 to June 2026, EEM rose roughly 90% in USD terms, the largest leg in this cycle. The advance was led by EM-Asia technology — Taiwan and South Korea, EEM's semiconductor-heavy components — alongside broad dollar weakness that amplified USD-translated returns on top of local-currency gains. By June 2026 the index reads pos 81/100 (peak phase) with RS rank 2 and +5.1 RS versus SPY over 63 days; the cycle model flags an elevated risk of a turn toward trough, centered around November 2026. Drivers beyond mid-2026 are forward-looking and not yet confirmed.","body_zh":"2025年4月至2026年6月，EEM以美元计累计上涨约90%，为本轮周期中最大的一段。涨势由新兴亚洲科技引领——台湾和韩国这两大半导体权重成分——并叠加美元全面走弱，在本币涨幅之上放大了美元计价回报。截至2026年6月，指数位置为81/100（顶部阶段），相对强度排名第2，63日相对SPY为+5.1；周期模型警示下行拐点风险上升，中枢约在2026年11月。2026年中以后的驱动因素属前瞻判断，尚未得到证实。","drivers":["EM-Asia semiconductor leadership (Taiwan, South Korea)","USD weakness amplifying USD-denominated returns","Position extended (pos 81), peak phase","Cycle model projects turn toward trough ~Nov 2026"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"AI-Led EM Bull & Weak Dollar","title_zh":"AI驱动的新兴市场牛市与美元走弱","turn_id":"eem:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"EEM (MSCI Emerging Markets) sits at a cycle peak with a position score of 81/100, having rallied roughly 90% in USD terms from its April 2025 trough. At pos 81 the index is extended — historically a zone where forward returns compress and risk-reward tilts toward caution. Relative strength versus SPY is mildly positive over the trailing 63 days (+5.1 RS), ranking second among all markets tracked, while the cycle model projects a turn toward trough centered around November 2026. As a USD-denominated EM proxy, the move blends local-equity gains across EM Asia with the EM currency basket versus the dollar, so dollar softness has amplified the USD-translated return.","now_zh":"EEM（MSCI新兴市场）当前处于周期顶部区域，位置分值81/100，自2025年4月低点以美元计累计反弹约90%。在81分位置，指数已明显偏高，历史规律显示前向回报趋于压缩，风险收益比向下偏斜。相对于SPY的63日相对强度微幅正值（+5.1），在全部市场中排名第二；周期模型预计下行拐点中枢约在2026年11月。作为美元计价的新兴市场代理，本轮涨幅叠加了新兴亚洲本地股票走势与新兴市场货币篮子对美元的变化，因此美元走弱放大了以美元衡量的回报。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"efa":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"efa:trough:2011-10"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"efa:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-25":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"efa:trough:2011-11"},"2012-03-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"efa:peak:2012-03"},"2012-06-01":{"body":"ECB President Draghi's July 2012 'whatever it takes' pledge and the subsequent OMT programme collapsed peripheral sovereign spreads and broke the eurozone breakup fear that had crushed EFA into mid-2012. A synchronised European re-rating, with EUR/USD firm, carried EFA up 62% in USD terms through July 2014. The leg ended as the ECB diverged from a tightening-bias Fed, pushing EUR/USD lower and removing the currency tailwind.","body_zh":"欧央行行长德拉吉2012年7月发表'不惜一切'承诺，随后推出直接货币交易计划（OMT），欧元区边缘国主权利差大幅收窄，化解了此前压制EFA的欧元区解体恐慌。欧洲股市同步重新定价、欧元/美元走强，EFA至2014年7月以美元计价上涨62%。随后欧央行与趋紧倾向的美联储出现分歧，欧元回落，货币顺风消散，本腿结束。","drivers":["ECB OMT backstop","EUR/USD recovery","Peripheral spread compression","Europe bank re-rating"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行OMT计划背书","欧元/美元回升","边缘国利差收窄","欧洲银行股重新定价"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Draghi backstop lifts European equities","title_zh":"德拉吉背书提振欧洲股市","turn_id":"efa:trough:2012-06"},"2014-06-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"efa:peak:2014-06"},"2015-01-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"efa:trough:2015-01"},"2015-05-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"efa:peak:2015-05"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"After a sharp global selloff in early 2016 driven by China growth fears and an oil collapse, central-bank pivots -- the ECB expanding QE in March 2016 and the Fed going slow on hikes -- unleashed a synchronised reflation trade. EFA gained 55% in USD terms through January 2018, aided by a weaker dollar (DXY fell roughly 10% in 2017), a cyclical rebound in European PMIs, and strong financials and industrials earnings. EUR/USD climbed from about 1.04 to above 1.20 over 2017, materially boosting USD-translated returns.","body_zh":"2016年初，受中国增长忧虑和油价崩溃冲击，全球大幅下跌；随后各央行转向——欧央行2016年3月扩大量化宽松、美联储放缓加息——引发同步再通胀行情。EFA至2018年1月以美元计价上涨55%，受益于美元走弱（2017年美元指数跌约10%）、欧洲PMI周期性反弹及金融与工业板块盈利回升。2017年欧元/美元从约1.04升至1.20以上，显著抬升美元计价回报。","drivers":["ECB QE expansion March 2016","USD bear trend 2017","European PMI reflation","Fed slow-hike path"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行2016年3月扩大量化宽松","2017年美元熊市","欧洲PMI再通胀","美联储放缓加息"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Synchronised global reflation rally","title_zh":"同步全球再通胀行情","turn_id":"efa:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"efa:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"The global Q4 2018 selloff -- driven by Fed rate-hike fears, trade-war escalation, and USD strength -- bottomed sharply in December 2018 as the Fed pivoted to a pause in early 2019. EFA gained 28% in USD terms through January 2020, supported by trade-truce optimism (the US-China phase-one deal in late 2019) and a stabilising EUR/USD. The leg stayed modest relative to prior cycles, as lingering trade uncertainty and tepid European growth capped the upside.","body_zh":"2018年第四季度全球市场因美联储加息预期、贸易战升级和美元走强而大幅下跌，美联储于2019年初转向暂停加息后市场触底反弹。EFA至2020年1月以美元计价上涨28%，受益于贸易休战乐观情绪（2019年底美中第一阶段协议）及欧元/美元企稳。但因贸易不确定性持续和欧洲增长疲弱，本腿涨幅较前几轮偏低。","drivers":["Fed early-2019 pivot","US-China phase-one trade truce","EUR/USD stabilisation","Global PMI bottoming"],"drivers_zh":["美联储2019年初转向","美中第一阶段贸易协议","欧元/美元企稳","全球PMI触底"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot sparks a modest recovery","title_zh":"美联储转向引发温和修复","turn_id":"efa:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-17":{"body":"COVID-19 spread from China into Europe in February 2020, hitting EFA's largest weight with full force as Italy became the first major Western outbreak. A safe-haven dollar surge compounded local-equity losses, driving EFA down 34% in USD terms in roughly six weeks to the March 2020 low. European banks and energy stocks -- core EAFE holdings -- amplified the drawdown relative to less cyclically exposed US indices.","body_zh":"2020年2月，新冠疫情从中国蔓延至欧洲，重创EFA最大权重区域；意大利成为首个主要西方暴发地。避险美元飙升进一步放大本币股票跌幅，EFA在约六周内以美元计价下跌34%，至2020年3月触底。欧洲银行股和能源股（EAFE核心持仓）较周期性暴露度较低的美国指数跌幅更深。","drivers":["COVID-19 European outbreak","Safe-haven USD surge","European bank and energy selloff","Global liquidity shock"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情欧洲暴发","避险美元飙升","欧洲银行与能源股抛售","全球流动性冲击"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID shock collapses developed markets","title_zh":"新冠冲击令发达市场骤然崩跌","turn_id":"efa:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"Unprecedented coordinated monetary and fiscal stimulus -- ECB PEPP, the EU Next Generation fund (EUR 750bn), and BoJ yield-curve control -- reflated risk assets globally. EFA gained 83% in USD terms from March 2020 through September 2021, with EUR/USD rising from about 1.07 to 1.23 contributing materially to USD-translated returns. EAFE's cyclical tilt (banks, industrials, energy) leveraged the reopening trade, and European vaccination progress through mid-2021 supported the final stretch of the move.","body_zh":"史无前例的协同货币与财政刺激——欧央行疫情紧急购债计划（PEPP）、欧盟下一代基金（7500亿欧元）、日央行收益率曲线控制——推动全球风险资产再通胀。EFA从2020年3月至2021年9月以美元计价上涨83%，欧元/美元从约1.07升至约1.23对美元计价回报贡献显著。EAFE周期性偏重（银行、工业、能源）充分受益于重开仓交易，2021年中期欧洲疫苗接种进展支撑了行情最后一段。","drivers":["ECB PEPP and EU Next Generation fund","EUR/USD appreciation to ~1.23","Global reopening cyclical trade","BoJ yield-curve control"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行PEPP与欧盟下一代基金","欧元/美元升至约1.23","全球重开仓周期性交易","日央行收益率曲线控制"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic stimulus -- coordinated global reflation","title_zh":"疫情刺激：协同全球再通胀","turn_id":"efa:trough:2020-03"},"2021-09-07":{"body":"Surging European natural-gas prices from mid-2021, then Russia's invasion of Ukraine in February 2022, delivered a severe supply shock that hit Europe's energy-dependent economy disproportionately. As the Nord Stream 1 shutdown drove EUR/USD below parity (to roughly 0.96) by late September 2022, currency gains for USD investors were erased even as the ECB hiked; EFA fell 29.5% in USD terms. European banks, industrials, and consumer discretionary all declined on earnings downgrades.","body_zh":"2021年中起欧洲天然气价格飙升，2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰后供应冲击骤然加剧，严重打击欧洲能源依赖型经济体。随着北溪一号停供，欧元/美元于2022年9月底跌破平价（至约0.96），尽管欧央行加息，美元投资者的货币收益仍被抹去；EFA以美元计价下跌29.5%。欧洲银行股、工业股及可选消费股均因盈利预期下调而下挫。","drivers":["Russia-Ukraine energy supply shock","EUR/USD drop below parity","ECB hikes amid recession fears","European earnings downgrades"],"drivers_zh":["俄乌能源供应冲击","欧元/美元跌破平价","欧央行加息伴随衰退恐慌","欧洲盈利预期下调"],"prev_key":"2021-09","prev_key_chain":["2021-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Energy crisis and Ukraine war crush EAFE","title_zh":"能源危机与乌克兰战争重创EAFE","turn_id":"efa:peak:2021-09"},"2022-09-27":{"body":"With EUR/USD having bottomed near parity and European energy prices retreating from their 2022 peaks, EAFE staged a 63% USD-term recovery from September 2022 through March 2025. The ECB's hiking cycle peaked and turned toward cuts in mid-2024, and a weaker dollar trend through 2025 -- amplified by US tariff uncertainty -- provided a major currency tailwind. EFA's 2025 calendar-year return of roughly 31% was driven significantly by EUR/USD and JPY/USD appreciation.","body_zh":"随着欧元/美元在平价附近触底、欧洲能源价格从2022年峰值回落，EAFE从2022年9月至2025年3月以美元计价累计反弹63%。欧央行加息周期见顶后于2024年中转向降息，2025年美元走弱趋势——因美国关税不确定性而放大——提供了重要货币顺风。EFA 2025年全年回报约31%，主要由欧元和日元对美元升值驱动。","drivers":["EUR/USD recovery from parity","ECB hiking peak then easing in 2024","US tariff-driven USD weakness 2025","European energy-price normalisation"],"drivers_zh":["欧元/美元从平价回升","欧央行加息见顶后2024年转向降息","美国关税驱动的2025年美元走弱","欧洲能源价格正常化"],"prev_key":"2022-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Multi-year recovery off the energy and EUR trough","title_zh":"能源危机与欧元触底后的多年修复","turn_id":"efa:trough:2022-09"},"2025-03-19":{"body":"A sharp global risk-off episode in March-April 2025, linked to renewed US tariff escalation, caused EFA to fall 14% in USD terms over roughly one month. The move reflected both local-equity weakness and a brief flight to dollar safety, though the broader dollar downtrend resumed quickly as markets priced tariff damage to the US economy itself. EFA bottomed in April 2025, setting up the next and most powerful up-leg.","body_zh":"2025年3月至4月，因美国关税再度升级引发剧烈全球避险情绪，EFA在约一个月内以美元计价下跌14%。此次回调同时反映本地股票走弱和美元短暂避险需求，但市场随即开始定价关税对美国经济自身的伤害，美元更广泛的下行趋势迅速恢复。EFA于2025年4月触底，为下一段最强劲的上升行情奠定基础。","drivers":["US tariff escalation shock","Brief safe-haven dollar bid","Global risk-off selloff","Rapid reversal as dollar weakness resumes"],"drivers_zh":["美国关税升级冲击","短暂避险美元需求","全球风险规避抛售","美元走弱恢复后快速反转"],"prev_key":"2025-03","prev_key_chain":["2025-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Tariff shock brief pullback","title_zh":"关税冲击引发短暂回调","turn_id":"efa:peak:2025-03"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From the April 2025 trough, EFA gained 50.8% in USD terms through June 2026, one of the strongest EAFE runs in years. The primary driver was a sustained USD downtrend as US-exceptionalism narratives faded under tariff uncertainty, fiscal-deficit concerns, and reduced foreign appetite for US assets. European and Japanese local-equity returns were themselves solid -- supported by ECB easing and gradual BoJ normalisation -- but EUR and JPY appreciation against the dollar contributed a substantial share of the USD-denominated gain. With the index now in a Downturn phase off the June 2026 peak, the model projects a trough around November 2026.","body_zh":"从2025年4月低点至2026年6月，EFA以美元计价上涨50.8%，是近年来最强劲的EAFE行情之一。主要驱动力是美元持续走弱——在关税不确定性、财政赤字担忧和外国投资者对美国资产需求下降的背景下，美国例外论叙事褪色。欧洲和日本本币股票回报本身也较为坚实，受益于欧央行降息和日央行渐进正常化，但欧元和日元相对美元的升值贡献了以美元计价涨幅的重要部分。该指数现已自2026年6月峰值进入回落阶段，模型预计低点约在2026年11月前后。","drivers":["Sustained USD downtrend 2025-2026","US-exceptionalism narrative reversal","ECB easing supporting European equities","BoJ normalisation and JPY appreciation"],"drivers_zh":["2025-2026年美元持续走弱","美国例外论叙事逆转","欧央行降息支撑欧洲股市","日央行正常化与日元升值"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Dollar-driven EAFE surge to the 2026 peak","title_zh":"美元主导EAFE飙升至2026年峰值","turn_id":"efa:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"EFA (MSCI EAFE) entered a Downturn phase as of end-June 2026, sitting at position 45/100 -- mid-cycle, neither washed-out nor at a stretched extreme. The ETF peaked in June 2026 after a 50.8% recovery from its April 2025 trough and has begun giving back gains, lagging SPY by about 4 points over the trailing 63 days. The fade follows a historic 2025 for developed ex-US equities: EFA returned roughly 31% in USD terms, with dollar weakness contributing a large share as US tariff and fiscal uncertainty pushed allocators to diversify away from US assets. The cycle model projects the next trough around November 2026, roughly five months out.","now_zh":"EFA（MSCI EAFE）截至2026年6月底进入回落阶段，位置指标约45/100，处于周期中段，既未超买也未触底洗盘。该ETF于2026年6月触峰——自2025年4月低点累计反弹50.8%——随后开始回吐涨幅，过去63个交易日较SPY落后约4个百分点。此次走弱发生在发达国际市场历史性的2025年之后：EFA当年以美元计价回报约31%，其中美元走弱贡献了很大一部分——美国关税与财政不确定性促使资产配置者分散减持美国资产。周期模型预计下一个低点约在2026年11月前后，距今约五个月。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"ilf":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ilf:trough:2011-10"},"2012-03-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ilf:peak:2012-03"},"2014-02-03":{"body":"From February to September 2014, ILF rose about 37% in USD terms in a counter-trend bounce within the broader commodity-cycle decline. The rally was driven by hopes for a market-friendly outcome in Brazil's October 2014 presidential election and a temporary stabilization in commodity prices and the BRL. The move proved to be a bull trap: once Dilma Rousseff was re-elected and commodity prices resumed falling, the rally fully reversed.","body_zh":"从2014年2月至9月，ILF以美元计上涨约37%，这是在大宗商品周期整体下行中的一次反向反弹。涨势受巴西2014年10月总统选举可能出现市场友好结果的预期，以及大宗商品价格与雷亚尔短暂企稳的推动。事后证明这是一个多头陷阱：罗塞夫连任、大宗商品价格重新下跌后，涨幅被完全回吐。","drivers":["Pre-election optimism ahead of Brazil's October 2014 vote","Temporary commodity-price and BRL stabilization","Counter-trend bounce within a structural downtrend"],"prev_key":"2014-02","prev_key_chain":["2014-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Brief 2014 World Cup-year bounce","title_zh":"2014年世界杯年的短暂反弹","turn_id":"ilf:trough:2014-02"},"2014-09-03":{"body":"From September 2014 through January 2016, ILF fell roughly 56% in USD terms as the commodity supercycle unwound. China's slowdown drove iron ore from well above $100/t toward $40/t and oil roughly halved, hitting Vale and Petrobras — ILF's largest weights. Brazil sank into a deep recession (GDP contracted around 3.5-3.8% in both 2015 and 2016) and the Lava Jato corruption scandal paralyzed investment. The BRL depreciated sharply against the USD, amplifying equity losses for dollar-based holders.","body_zh":"从2014年9月至2016年1月，ILF以美元计下跌约56%，大宗商品超级周期瓦解是主因。中国经济放缓将铁矿石价格从远高于每吨100美元压向40美元，油价约腰斩，重创淡水河谷和巴西国家石油公司——ILF最大的权重股。巴西陷入深度衰退（2015和2016年GDP均收缩约3.5-3.8%），洗车行动腐败丑闻令投资冻结。雷亚尔兑美元大幅贬值，放大了美元持有者的股票损失。","drivers":["Iron ore collapse from above $100 toward $40/t","Oil price roughly halved, hitting Petrobras","Brazil deep recession and Lava Jato corruption scandal","Sharp BRL depreciation amplifying USD losses"],"prev_key":"2014-09","prev_key_chain":["2014-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Commodity crash crushes LatAm","title_zh":"大宗商品暴跌重创拉美","turn_id":"ilf:peak:2014-09"},"2016-01-21":{"body":"From January 2016 to January 2018, ILF surged about 124% — one of the strongest LatAm rallies in a decade. Iron ore and oil rebounded off their lows on Chinese stimulus and infrastructure spending. In Brazil, President Temer replaced the impeached Dilma Rousseff and pursued market-friendly reform, including a constitutional spending cap. The BRL recovered as political risk receded and carry flows resumed, adding an FX tailwind on top of the equity re-rating.","body_zh":"从2016年1月至2018年1月，ILF飙涨约124%——十年来拉美最强劲的涨势之一。在中国刺激和基础设施支出推动下，铁矿石和油价从低位回升。巴西方面，特梅尔总统接替遭弹劾的罗塞夫，推行市场友好改革，包括宪法层面的支出上限。随着政治风险消退及套息资金回流，雷亚尔回升，在股票重新定价之上叠加了汇率顺风。","drivers":["Iron ore and oil recovery on China stimulus","Temer market-friendly reforms and spending cap","BRL recovery as political risk receded","Carry-trade inflows resuming"],"prev_key":"2016-01","prev_key_chain":["2016-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Commodity rebound and Temer reforms","title_zh":"大宗商品反弹与特梅尔改革","turn_id":"ilf:trough:2016-01"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ilf:peak:2018-01"},"2018-06-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ilf:trough:2018-06"},"2019-02-05":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ilf:peak:2019-02"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From January to March 2020, ILF fell roughly 55% as COVID-19 triggered a global risk-off collapse. Latin America was heavily exposed: commodity demand cratered, the BRL hit record lows against the USD, and oil briefly traded negative (WTI in April 2020), crushing Petrobras. The dollar surge during the liquidity shock was a second blow for this USD-denominated ETF.","body_zh":"从2020年1月至3月，ILF下跌约55%，新冠疫情引发全球风险厌恶情绪崩溃。拉丁美洲风险敞口巨大：大宗商品需求骤降，雷亚尔兑美元跌至历史新低，油价一度为负（2020年4月WTI），重创巴西国家石油公司。流动性冲击期间美元飙升，对这一以美元计价的ETF造成第二重打击。","drivers":["Global risk-off liquidity shock","Oil collapse, WTI briefly negative","BRL at record lows vs USD","USD surge compressing returns"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"rekey_shift_days":68,"status":"shifted","title":"COVID crash hits LatAm hard","title_zh":"新冠冲击重创拉美","turn_id":"ilf:trough:2020-03"},"2021-06-07":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ilf:peak:2021-06"},"2021-12-20":{"body":"From December 2021 to April 2022, ILF added about 41% even as global equities began turning risk-off. The driver was commodities: Russia's February 2022 invasion of Ukraine sent energy, metals, and agricultural prices surging, benefiting Brazilian oil, iron ore, and soy exporters. Brazil's central bank had been aggressively hiking the Selic rate to fight inflation, which helped keep the BRL relatively firm in this window.","body_zh":"从2021年12月至2022年4月，尽管全球股市开始转向风险规避，ILF仍上涨约41%。驱动力来自大宗商品：2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰导致能源、金属和农产品价格飙升，令巴西石油、铁矿石和大豆出口商受益。巴西央行此前大幅加息（Selic利率）以抗击通胀，有助于在此窗口期保持雷亚尔相对坚挺。","drivers":["Ukraine-war energy, metals and grain price spike","Brazil oil, iron ore and soy export windfall","Aggressive Selic hikes supporting the BRL"],"prev_key":"2021-12","prev_key_chain":["2021-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Ukraine-war commodity tailwind","title_zh":"乌克兰战争的大宗商品顺风","turn_id":"ilf:trough:2021-12"},"2022-04-04":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"ilf:peak:2022-04"},"2022-07-14":{"body":"From July 2022 to December 2023, ILF gained about 58% against a volatile backdrop. Commodity prices normalized from their war-driven spikes, but the move higher was supported by resilient Brazilian corporate earnings, still-elevated commodity prices, and China's exit from zero-COVID in late 2022/early 2023, which lifted iron ore and copper demand. Lula narrowly won the October 2022 election; initial fiscal-spending concerns kept the BRL under intermittent pressure, capping dollar-denominated gains.","body_zh":"从2022年7月至2023年12月，ILF在波动背景下上涨约58%。大宗商品价格从战争推升的高位回归正常，但上涨得到巴西企业盈利韧性、仍处高位的大宗商品价格，以及2022年底至2023年初中国结束动态清零（提振铁矿石和铜需求）的支撑。卢拉在2022年10月选举中以微弱优势胜出；初期财政支出忧虑使雷亚尔间歇性承压，限制了美元计涨幅。","drivers":["China zero-COVID exit lifting iron ore and copper","Still-elevated commodity prices post-Ukraine","Resilient Brazilian corporate earnings","BRL pressured by fiscal-spending concerns"],"prev_key":"2022-07","prev_key_chain":["2022-07"],"status":"exact","title":"Lula election and resilient earnings","title_zh":"卢拉当选与坚韧的企业盈利","turn_id":"ilf:trough:2022-07"},"2023-12-19":{"body":"From December 2023 to January 2025, ILF fell about 24% in USD terms as concern over Brazil's fiscal trajectory mounted. Brazil's headline fiscal deficit ran wide (high single digits as a share of GDP), the Lula administration repeatedly tested its fiscal-rule limits, and the BRL weakened steadily — amplifying the dollar-terms drawdown even as local equities held up better. Elevated US rates also reduced the relative carry appeal of Brazilian assets, encouraging outflows.","body_zh":"从2023年12月至2025年1月，ILF以美元计下跌约24%，市场对巴西财政轨迹的担忧加剧。巴西名义财政赤字处于高位（占GDP的高个位数百分比），卢拉政府屡次试探财政规则边界，雷亚尔持续走弱——即便本地股市相对坚挺，仍放大了美元口径的回撤。美国利率高企也削弱了巴西资产的相对套息吸引力，助推资本外流。","drivers":["Brazil headline fiscal deficit running wide","Steady BRL depreciation amplifying USD drawdown","Elevated US rates reducing LatAm carry appeal","Fiscal-rule credibility questioned"],"prev_key":"2023-12","prev_key_chain":["2023-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Fiscal worries and a weaker real","title_zh":"财政忧虑与雷亚尔走弱","turn_id":"ilf:peak:2023-12"},"2025-01-03":{"body":"From January 2025 to the April 2026 peak, ILF rose about 91% in USD terms in a powerful recovery off a deeply oversold base. The rebound was consistent with stabilization in the BRL after a long depreciation, firmer commodity prices benefiting the region's miners and energy names, and EM-vs-DM rotation flows favoring cheap Latin American equities. This leg runs beyond reliably verifiable knowledge, so the magnitude and direction reflect the reported price series rather than specific confirmed catalysts; the subsequent rollover into the current Trough (peak April 2026) is the key fact for positioning.","body_zh":"从2025年1月至2026年4月峰值，ILF以美元计上涨约91%，是自深度超卖基础上的有力复苏。此次反弹与雷亚尔在长期贬值后趋于企稳、大宗商品价格回稳（利好本地区矿业与能源股），以及新兴市场对发达市场的轮动资金青睐廉价拉美股票相一致。此段超出可可靠核实的知识范围，因此其幅度与方向反映已报告的价格序列，而非具体已证实的催化剂；随后回落进入当前底部阶段（峰值为2026年4月）才是对仓位最关键的事实。","drivers":["BRL stabilizing after a prolonged depreciation","Firmer commodity prices aiding miners and energy","EM-vs-DM rotation into cheap LatAm equities","Rebound off a deeply oversold base (magnitude per reported data)"],"prev_key":"2025-01","prev_key_chain":["2025-01"],"status":"exact","title":"Strong rebound off the January 2025 low","title_zh":"自2025年1月低点的强劲反弹","turn_id":"ilf:trough:2025-01"}},"now":"ILF sits in a Trough phase (position 13.7/100) after rolling over from an April 2026 peak. Over the past 63 days it has lagged SPY by 13.4 percentage points, a meaningful underperformance consistent with a risk-off rotation away from commodity-linked emerging markets. Because ILF is USD-priced, the drawdown reflects both softer local-currency Latin American equities and dollar strength compressing returns when translated back to USD. The ETF nonetheless remains above its 200-day moving average, so the broader uptrend off the January 2025 low is intact but under pressure.","now_zh":"ILF目前处于底部阶段（位置13.7/100），自2026年4月峰值后回落。过去63个交易日相对标普500落后13.4个百分点，属明显跑输，与资金撤离大宗商品挂钩新兴市场的风险偏好收缩走势一致。由于ILF以美元计价，本轮回撤同时反映拉美本币股市走弱以及美元走强对换算回美元后回报的压制。不过ETF仍高于200日均线，因此自2025年1月低点以来的上升趋势尚未被打破，但承压明显。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"vgk":{"legs":{"2011-09-22":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2011-09"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-25":{"body":"After the acute eurozone sovereign stress of mid-2011, Draghi's appointment as ECB president in November 2011 and early signals of ECB flexibility provided a sentiment floor. European equities bounced roughly 24.5% in this short leg through March 2012, aided by a modest EUR stabilisation that limited USD-denominated drag. The move was a relief rally rather than a new bull trend, as peripheral spreads remained elevated.","body_zh":"2011年中欧元区主权债务危机急剧恶化后，德拉吉于2011年11月就任欧央行行长并释放灵活立场的早期信号，为市场情绪提供了支撑。欧洲股市在这段短暂行情中至2012年3月反弹约24.5%，同期欧元小幅企稳也限制了美元计价资产的拖累。这波行情属于情绪修复式反弹，而非新一轮牛市，因为外围国国债息差仍处高位。","drivers":["Draghi ECB appointment reducing tail-risk premium","EUR stabilisation limiting FX drag","Oversold European bank and sovereign positioning"],"drivers_zh":["德拉吉出任欧央行行长，系统性尾部风险溢价收窄","欧元企稳，限制了汇率拖累","欧洲银行股与主权债仓位严重超卖"],"prev_key":"2011-11","prev_key_chain":["2011-11"],"status":"exact","title":"Euro Crisis Relief Rally","title_zh":"欧债危机企稳反弹","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2011-11"},"2012-03-19":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:peak:2012-03"},"2012-06-01":{"body":"Draghi's July 2012 \"whatever it takes\" speech and the subsequent Outright Monetary Transactions program broke the doom loop between sovereigns and banks, triggering a sustained 72.9% rally through July 2014. The ECB backstop compressed peripheral spreads dramatically, reigniting risk appetite across European financials and cyclicals. EUR/USD held broadly firm over this period, adding a modest positive FX overlay for USD-based investors.","body_zh":"德拉吉2012年7月的\"不惜一切\"演讲及随后推出的直接货币交易（OMT）计划，打破了主权债务与银行体系之间的恶性循环，触发了长达两年、累计涨幅72.9%的持续反弹。欧央行的背书大幅压缩了外围国主权利差，重燃了市场对欧洲金融股与周期股的风险偏好。欧元/美元在此期间整体保持坚挺，为美元计价投资者带来温和的正向汇率叠加效应。","drivers":["ECB OMT backstop eliminating euro breakup risk","Peripheral sovereign spread compression","European bank recapitalization progress"],"drivers_zh":["欧央行OMT计划消除欧元区解体尾部风险","外围国主权利差大幅收窄","欧洲银行业资本重组推进"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Whatever It Takes Two-Year Bull Run","title_zh":"不惜一切承诺开启两年牛市","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2012-06"},"2014-06-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:peak:2014-06"},"2015-01-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2015-01"},"2015-05-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:peak:2015-05"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"After the February 2016 global growth scare and the subsequent June 2016 Brexit shock, European equities staged a 54.4% recovery through January 2018, riding the 2016-2017 global synchronized growth upswing. Euro-area GDP growth accelerated and the ECB maintained its asset purchase program, keeping financial conditions easy. EUR/USD trended higher from mid-2017 as the ECB began signalling QE tapering, boosting USD-denominated returns in the final phase of this leg.","body_zh":"经历2016年2月全球增长恐慌及随后6月的脱欧冲击后，欧洲股市展开54.4%的复苏行情，延续至2018年1月，受益于2016至2017年全球同步增长周期。欧元区GDP增速加快，欧央行维持资产购买计划，金融条件保持宽松。2017年中起欧元/美元趋势性走强，因欧央行开始释放缩减购债信号，在这段行情末期为美元计价回报带来提振。","drivers":["Global synchronized growth 2016-2017","ECB QE keeping euro financial conditions easy","EUR/USD appreciation from mid-2017 ECB taper signals","French 2017 election political risk resolved"],"drivers_zh":["2016至2017年全球同步经济增长","欧央行持续购债维持宽松金融条件","欧央行2017年中缩债信号推动欧元/美元升值","2017年法国大选政治风险平稳落地"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Synchronized Growth and ECB QE","title_zh":"全球同步增长与欧央行量化宽松","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"Following the Q4 2018 global equity selloff driven by US-China trade-war escalation and Fed overtightening fears, VGK rose 30.3% from December 2018 through January 2020 as the Fed pivoted dovish and US-China trade tensions eased. European industrials and exporters, sensitive to global trade volumes, led the recovery. EUR/USD remained broadly range-bound against the dollar during this leg, a roughly neutral FX contribution.","body_zh":"2018年四季度全球股市因中美贸易战升级与美联储过度加息担忧大幅下挫，此后VGK从2018年12月反弹至2020年1月，累计涨幅30.3%，受益于美联储转向鸽派及中美贸易紧张缓和。高度依赖全球贸易量的欧洲工业股与出口商引领复苏。本段行情中欧元/美元整体区间震荡，汇率因素影响大致中性。","drivers":["Fed dovish pivot removing overtightening fear","US-China trade de-escalation reducing uncertainty","European industrial exporter recovery on stabilising global trade","ECB TLTRO III liquidity support"],"drivers_zh":["美联储转向鸽派，消除过度紧缩担忧","中美贸易紧张缓和，减少不确定性","全球贸易趋稳推动欧洲工业出口商复苏","欧央行通过TLTRO III补充流动性"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Trade Truce and Fed Pivot Rebound","title_zh":"贸易休战与美联储转向推动反弹","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-02":{"body":"The COVID-19 pandemic triggered a sharp 37.1% drawdown from January to March 2020 as Europe emerged as an early epicenter outside Asia. Italy's lockdown in early March and the rapid spread across the continent paralysed economic activity, crushed cyclical and travel-exposed sectors, and sparked a flight to the USD that compounded losses in dollar terms. The velocity of the decline was among the sharpest in the ETF's history.","body_zh":"新冠疫情触发了从2020年1月至3月共37.1%的急剧回撤，欧洲成为亚洲以外的早期震中。意大利于3月初宣布封锁，疫情迅速蔓延全欧洲，经济活动陷入瘫痪，周期性行业与旅游相关板块大幅下挫，同时资金涌向美元，进一步放大了以美元计价的损失。此次下跌速度是该ETF历史上最急剧的之一。","drivers":["COVID-19 pandemic economic shutdown","Europe as early pandemic epicenter outside Asia","USD safe-haven surge amplifying USD-denominated losses","Cyclical and travel sector collapse"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情导致经济停摆","欧洲成为亚洲外首要疫情重灾区","美元避险需求飙升，放大美元计价损失","周期性行业与旅行相关板块崩跌"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID Pandemic Crash","title_zh":"新冠疫情冲击暴跌","turn_id":"vgk:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"From the March 2020 trough, VGK surged roughly 99.2% through September 2021 as unprecedented global fiscal and monetary stimulus, the rollout of effective vaccines from late 2020, and the EU's EUR 750 billion Next Generation EU recovery fund unleashed a powerful reflation trade. European cyclicals, banks, and industrials outperformed as the global economy reopened. EUR/USD climbed from roughly 1.08 to about 1.23 by early 2021, providing a substantial additional FX tailwind for USD-denominated returns.","body_zh":"从2020年3月底部起，VGK至2021年9月累计大涨约99.2%，受益于全球史无前例的财政与货币刺激、2020年底有效疫苗的推出，以及欧盟7500亿欧元下一代欧盟复苏基金所触发的强劲再通胀行情。全球经济重开放推动欧洲周期股、银行股与工业股跑赢大盘。欧元/美元从约1.08升至2021年初的约1.23，为美元计价回报提供了可观的额外汇率顺风。","drivers":["Coordinated global fiscal and monetary stimulus","COVID vaccine rollout enabling economic reopening","EU Next Generation EUR750bn recovery fund","EUR/USD rally from ~1.08 to ~1.23 adding large FX tailwind"],"drivers_zh":["全球财政与货币政策协同刺激","新冠疫苗推出推动经济重开放","欧盟7500亿欧元下一代欧盟复苏基金","欧元/美元从约1.08升至约1.23带来显著汇率顺风"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Pandemic Stimulus and Reopening Rally","title_zh":"疫情刺激政策与重开放推动大幅反弹","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2020-03"},"2021-09-02":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:peak:2021-09"},"2022-03-07":{"body":"Russia's invasion of Ukraine in February 2022 produced a brief bounce followed by a sustained 26.9% drawdown into September 2022, hitting Europe disproportionately hard given its heavy dependence on Russian natural gas. Energy prices spiked to historic levels, stoking double-digit inflation and forcing the ECB into its fastest tightening cycle on record. EUR/USD fell from around 1.13 to below parity (under 0.97) by September 2022, a historic EUR weakness that compounded equity losses in USD terms.","body_zh":"2022年2月俄罗斯入侵乌克兰，短暂反弹后转入延续至2022年9月、累计26.9%的持续下跌，欧洲因高度依赖俄罗斯天然气而受到不成比例的重创。能源价格飙升至历史高位，引发两位数通胀，迫使欧央行以史上最快速度启动加息周期。欧元/美元从约1.13跌至2022年9月的平价以下（低于0.97），历史性的欧元贬值在美元计价层面额外放大了损失。","drivers":["Russia-Ukraine war and natural gas supply disruption","European energy import shock driving double-digit inflation","ECB forced into fastest tightening cycle on record","EUR/USD collapse below parity amplifying USD losses"],"drivers_zh":["俄乌战争与天然气供应中断","欧洲能源进口冲击推动两位数通胀","欧央行被迫启动史上最快加息周期","欧元/美元跌破平价，放大美元计价损失"],"prev_key":"2022-03","prev_key_chain":["2022-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Russia-Ukraine Energy Crisis Selloff","title_zh":"俄乌战争能源危机冲击下跌","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2022-03"},"2022-03-29":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:peak:2022-03"},"2022-09-27":{"body":"From the September 2022 trough, VGK delivered a 120.9% total return through February 2026 - the longest and largest single up-leg in the 15-year dataset. European natural gas prices cratered from their August 2022 peak as a mild winter, rapid LNG import build-out, and demand destruction averted a catastrophic shortage. China's 2023 reopening lifted demand for European luxury and industrial goods, and broad USD softening through 2023-2024 added a persistent FX tailwind. The ECB began cutting rates in mid-2024, supporting the advance. The 2025-into-early-2026 extension carried the leg to its February 2026 peak; the precise late-stage drivers are less certain, but the move topped out before the current pullback.","body_zh":"从2022年9月低点至2026年2月，VGK累计涨幅120.9%，是15年数据集中持续时间最长、幅度最大的单段上涨。欧洲天然气价格从2022年8月峰值急剧回落，原因是暖冬、快速建设的LNG进口能力以及需求破坏共同化解了短缺危机。2023年中国重开放提振了欧洲奢侈品与工业品需求，2023至2024年美元整体走弱提供了持续的汇率顺风。欧央行于2024年中开始降息，对涨势形成支撑。2025年至2026年初的延伸将这段行情推升至2026年2月峰值；其后段的具体驱动较难确认，但该走势已在当前回调前见顶。","drivers":["European natural gas price collapse from August 2022 peak","China 2023 reopening boosting luxury and industrial demand","USD weakening through 2023-2024 adding FX tailwind","ECB rate-cut cycle beginning mid-2024","Energy headwind reversal supporting European earnings"],"drivers_zh":["欧洲天然气价格从2022年8月峰值大幅回落","中国2023年重开放提振奢侈品与工业品需求","2023至2024年美元走弱带来持续汇率顺风","欧央行2024年中开启降息周期","能源逆风逆转支撑欧洲企业盈利"],"prev_key":"2022-09","prev_key_chain":["2022-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Energy Crisis Floor to Multi-Year Bull Leg","title_zh":"能源危机筑底开启多年牛市","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2022-09"},"2025-03-18":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:peak:2025-03"},"2025-04-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vgk:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"VGK (FTSE Developed Europe) sits in mid-Expansion at a cycle position score of 47.7/100, well off its February 2026 peak but still trading above its 200-day moving average. The ETF has lagged SPY by roughly 3.9 percentage points over the past 63 days, ranking fifth of the tracked universe. With the EUR/GBP currency tailwind that lifted the bloc through 2025 now less supportive and global growth expectations softening, cycle models project a trough as early as July 2026, suggesting the current pullback may have further to run.","now_zh":"VGK（富时发达欧洲ETF）目前处于扩张期中段，周期位置得分47.7/100，距2026年2月峰值已有明显回落，但仍站稳于200日均线之上。过去63个交易日相对SPY落后约3.9个百分点，在跟踪市场中排名第五。此前支撑欧洲资产的欧元与英镑汇率顺风已不再强劲，叠加全球增长预期走软，周期模型预计最早于2026年7月触及阶段性低点，当前回调可能尚未结束。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"vpl":{"legs":{"2011-12-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vpl:trough:2011-12"},"2012-02-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vpl:peak:2012-02"},"2012-06-01":{"body":"From mid-2012 Japan launched aggressive fiscal stimulus under Abe, and the BOJ began unprecedented quantitative and qualitative easing (QQE) from April 2013, targeting a doubling of the monetary base. The yen fell sharply versus the dollar through 2015, amplifying USD returns for overseas holders of Japanese equities even as the Nikkei re-rated. Korea and Australia contributed via the late China commodity/demand cycle. VPL gained 55.9% in USD terms over this roughly three-year leg, with the local equity rally partly offset by the yen's depreciation drag on USD translation.","body_zh":"2012年中期，日本在安倍晋三领导下推出大规模财政刺激，日本央行自2013年4月起实施前所未有的量化质化宽松（QQE），目标是将货币基础翻番。日元至2015年兑美元大幅贬值，在日经指数重估的同时放大了海外持有者的美元回报。韩国和澳大利亚则通过中国大宗商品/需求周期的尾声形成贡献。在此约三年的上行段中，VPL以美元计涨幅达55.9%，本地股市上涨部分被日元贬值对美元换算的拖累所抵消。","drivers":["BOJ QQE: monetary base doubling, Nikkei re-rating","JPY depreciation weighed on USD translation","Japan export earnings upgrade on weaker yen","Late China commodity/demand cycle supporting Korea and Australia"],"drivers_zh":["日本央行QQE：货币基础翻番，日经指数重估","日元贬值拖累美元换算","日元走弱推升日本出口企业盈利上调","中国大宗商品/需求周期尾声支撑韩国与澳大利亚"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Abenomics reflation and BOJ QQE surge","title_zh":"安倍经济学通胀与日本央行大规模宽松推升","turn_id":"vpl:trough:2012-06"},"2015-04-28":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vpl:peak:2015-04"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"After the 2015-2016 EM/commodity selloff, global risk appetite recovered sharply from February 2016 on stabilizing oil, a softer Fed path, and China stimulus. A synchronized global manufacturing upturn boosted Japanese auto and machinery exports and Korean semiconductors, while iron ore rebounded off 2016 lows to support Australia. The BOJ adopted yield curve control in September 2016, anchoring JGB yields. VPL gained 67.1% over this nearly two-year run, with local equity gains the primary driver.","body_zh":"经历2015至2016年的新兴市场和大宗商品抛售后，随着油价企稳、美联储政策路径趋于温和以及中国推出刺激，全球风险偏好自2016年2月起急剧修复。全球制造业同步复苏推升了日本汽车与机械出口及韩国半导体，铁矿石从2016年低点反弹支撑澳大利亚。日本央行于2016年9月采用收益率曲线控制，锚定国债收益率。在近两年的上行段中，VPL以美元计涨幅达67.1%，本地股市上涨为主要驱动。","drivers":["Synchronized global manufacturing upturn","Korea semiconductor demand and Japan export recovery","Iron ore price recovery (Australia tailwind)","BOJ yield curve control (September 2016) stabilized JGB market"],"drivers_zh":["全球制造业同步复苏","韩国半导体需求与日本出口复苏","铁矿石价格回升（澳大利亚顺风）","日本央行收益率曲线控制（2016年9月）稳定国债市场"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Global reflation and synchronized manufacturing upturn","title_zh":"全球再通胀与制造业同步复苏","turn_id":"vpl:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vpl:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"After the Q4 2018 global selloff driven by Fed overtightening fears and US-China trade-war escalation, the Fed paused in January 2019 and cut rates from mid-2019, lifting risk assets globally. Pacific equities recovered modestly as trade tensions partially de-escalated, and the yen held roughly 108-110 per dollar, keeping FX translation broadly neutral. This was a relatively shallow +24.3% leg, with neither a strong local rally nor a meaningful FX tailwind.","body_zh":"2018年四季度全球股市在美联储过度紧缩担忧及中美贸易战升级下大幅下挫，美联储随即于2019年1月暂停加息，并于2019年年中开始降息，提振全球风险资产。随着贸易紧张局势局部缓和，太平洋股市温和回升，日元维持在108至110兑美元区间，汇率换算大致中性。本段涨幅相对较浅，VPL以美元计涨24.3%，既无强劲的本地上涨，也无明显的汇率顺风。","drivers":["Fed policy pivot from tightening to cuts (2019)","Partial US-China trade-war de-escalation","JPY roughly stable (limited FX amplification)","Modest, broad-based Pacific equity recovery"],"drivers_zh":["美联储政策从加息转向降息（2019年）","中美贸易战局部缓和","日元大致稳定（汇率放大效应有限）","太平洋股市温和、广泛的修复"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pivot relief rally, pre-COVID","title_zh":"美联储转向预期推动的修复行情","turn_id":"vpl:trough:2018-12"},"2019-12-16":{"body":"As COVID-19 spread and then hit global markets in March 2020, VPL dropped 31.5% in roughly two months. Japan and Korea faced early supply-chain disruptions given deep integration with China, and the yen's classic safe-haven strengthening partially cushioned USD losses, but the global equity collapse overwhelmed any FX support. Australia was hit by a simultaneous commodity-demand shock as Chinese industrial activity stalled.","body_zh":"随着新冠疫情蔓延并于2020年3月冲击全球市场，VPL在约两个月内下跌31.5%。鉴于与中国的深度整合，日本和韩国早期便遭遇供应链中断；日元发挥传统避险功能升值，在一定程度上以美元计减轻了跌幅，但全球股市的整体崩塌压倒了汇率缓冲。澳大利亚则同时受到中国工业活动停滞带来的大宗商品需求冲击。","drivers":["COVID-19 global risk-off: equity collapse across all DM","Japan and Korea supply-chain shock (China-integrated manufacturing)","Commodity demand collapse (Australia iron ore hit)","JPY safe-haven bid provided partial offset in USD terms"],"drivers_zh":["新冠疫情引发全球风险规避：所有发达市场股市崩跌","日本与韩国供应链冲击（与中国高度整合的制造业）","大宗商品需求崩溃（澳大利亚铁矿石受损）","日元避险买盘在美元计价层面提供部分缓冲"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"rekey_shift_days":30,"status":"shifted","title":"COVID crash: global risk-off selloff","title_zh":"新冠冲击：全球风险规避抛售","turn_id":"vpl:peak:2019-12"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"The March 2020 trough unleashed coordinated global central-bank easing and massive fiscal stimulus. Japan and Korea benefited from surging global demand for electronics, semiconductors, and auto components, and Australia rode an extraordinary iron ore price spike toward $200 per tonne by mid-2021 on booming Chinese steel demand. BOJ yield curve control kept the yen relatively stable, leaving FX broadly neutral in USD terms. VPL gained 81.3% over roughly 18 months, broadly tracking the global risk-on recovery.","body_zh":"2020年3月触底后，全球央行协同宽松与大规模财政刺激相继释放。日本与韩国受益于全球对电子产品、半导体和汽车零部件需求的激增，澳大利亚则借助铁矿石价格异常飙升（至2021年中期逼近每吨200美元）与中国钢铁需求繁荣乘势而上。日本央行收益率曲线控制使日元相对稳定，美元层面汇率大致中性。VPL在约18个月内涨幅达81.3%，与全球风险偏好修复基本同步。","drivers":["Global fiscal and monetary stimulus (coordinated G10 easing)","Japan and Korea electronics/semiconductor demand surge","Iron ore price spike toward $200 (Australia windfall)","BOJ yield curve control kept JPY stable (neutral FX)"],"drivers_zh":["全球财政与货币刺激（G10协同宽松）","日本与韩国电子/半导体需求激增","铁矿石价格飙升至接近200美元（澳大利亚受益）","日本央行收益率曲线控制稳定日元（汇率中性）"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Post-COVID recovery and reflation rebound","title_zh":"新冠后修复与再通胀反弹","turn_id":"vpl:trough:2020-03"},"2021-09-15":{"body":"From September 2021 the Fed signaled tapering and then ran its fastest hiking cycle in decades through 2022. The BOJ held firm on yield curve control, and the widening US-Japan rate differential drove the yen from roughly 110 to 150 per dollar by October 2022. While Japanese equities held up reasonably well in local yen terms, the heavy yen depreciation crushed USD returns, and Korea fell on a semiconductor downcycle. VPL fell 31.1%, with Australia only partially insulated by RBA hikes and elevated commodity prices.","body_zh":"自2021年9月起，美联储释放缩减购债信号，随后展开数十年来最快的加息周期。日本央行坚守收益率曲线控制，扩大的美日利差使日元从约110贬至2022年10月的150附近。尽管日本股市以日元计表现尚可，但日元大幅贬值压垮了美元回报，韩国则因半导体下行周期下跌。VPL下跌31.1%，澳大利亚仅因澳联储加息和高位的大宗商品价格而获部分缓冲。","drivers":["BOJ-Fed policy divergence: widening rate differential crushed JPY","JPY depreciation ~110 to ~150 (dominant drag on USD returns)","Korea semiconductor downcycle weighed on the bloc","Australia RBA hikes and commodities offered partial offset"],"drivers_zh":["日本央行与美联储政策分歧：利差扩大压垮日元","日元从约110贬至约150（美元回报的主要拖累）","韩国半导体下行周期拖累整个篮子","澳联储加息与大宗商品提供部分缓冲"],"prev_key":"2021-09","prev_key_chain":["2021-09"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed tightening and yen collapse drag","title_zh":"美联储紧缩与日元崩跌的双重拖累","turn_id":"vpl:peak:2021-09"},"2022-10-14":{"body":"The yen stabilized from October 2022 as the Fed neared its peak rate and Japan's Ministry of Finance intervened in FX markets. The Tokyo Stock Exchange launched its landmark corporate governance reform in early 2023, pressuring companies trading below book value to improve capital efficiency, buybacks, and ROE, catalyzing a sustained Nikkei re-rating and record foreign inflows. Korea and Australia added support via recovering tech demand and commodities. VPL gained 48.4% through September 2024, with the Japanese governance story a key driver alongside a steadier yen.","body_zh":"随着美联储接近利率峰值且日本财务省介入外汇市场，日元自2022年10月起企稳。东京证券交易所于2023年初推出里程碑式的公司治理改革，要求市净率低于1倍的公司提升资本效率、推进回购并改善ROE，催化日经指数持续重估并引发外资创纪录流入。韩国与澳大利亚通过科技需求回升和大宗商品提供支撑。在2024年9月前，VPL以美元计涨幅达48.4%，日本治理改革主题与日元企稳共同成为核心驱动。","drivers":["TSE corporate governance reform (P/B pressure, buybacks, ROE)","Record foreign inflows into Japan equities","JPY stabilization after MoF FX intervention","Recovering Korea tech demand and Australia commodities"],"drivers_zh":["东证所公司治理改革（市净率压力、回购、ROE）","外资创纪录流入日本股市","日本财务省汇率干预后日元企稳","韩国科技需求回升与澳大利亚大宗商品"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Yen stabilization and Japan governance re-rating","title_zh":"日元企稳与日本公司治理重估","turn_id":"vpl:trough:2022-10"},"2024-09-26":{"body":"The BOJ's late-July 2024 rate hike, alongside a weak US jobs print, triggered a violent unwind of the yen carry trade. On 5 August 2024 the Nikkei 225 fell 12.4%, its worst single session since 1987, and the yen surged from roughly 160 toward the low-140s per dollar in weeks, a double hit: local equities cratered while the rapid yen strengthening hurt overseas-earnings translation for exporters. From the September 2024 high to the April 2025 trough VPL fell 16.4%.","body_zh":"日本央行2024年7月底加息，叠加疲弱的美国就业数据，引发日元套利交易的剧烈平仓。2024年8月5日，日经225指数下跌12.4%，为1987年以来最差单日表现，日元在数周内从约160急升至140出头兑美元，形成双重打击：本地股市暴跌，而日元快速升值压缩了出口商的海外利润换算。从2024年9月高点至2025年4月低点，VPL下跌16.4%。","drivers":["BOJ late-July 2024 rate hike triggered carry-trade unwind","Nikkei -12.4% on 5 August 2024 (worst session since 1987)","JPY surge from ~160 toward low-140s (export earnings hit)","Weak US jobs data amplified the global risk-off move"],"drivers_zh":["日本央行2024年7月底加息引发套利交易平仓","日经指数2024年8月5日下跌12.4%（1987年以来最差单日）","日元从约160急升至140出头（出口商盈利受损）","疲弱的美国就业数据放大了全球风险规避行情"],"prev_key":"2024-09","prev_key_chain":["2024-09"],"status":"exact","title":"BOJ hike shock and yen carry unwind","title_zh":"日本央行加息冲击与日元套利交易平仓","turn_id":"vpl:peak:2024-09"},"2025-04-08":{"body":"From the April 2025 trough VPL rose roughly 92% through June 2026, the largest single upcycle in the 15-year dataset. A magnitude this large for a developed-market bloc almost certainly combines genuine local-equity appreciation with a USD-translation tailwind: a broadly weaker dollar through this window mechanically lifts USD returns for Pacific holders before any local gain. Japan's governance-driven re-rating and Korea's semiconductor strength are consistent contributors. Because this leg extends past reliable knowledge, treat the specific catalyst mix as provisional and lean on the quantitative read: cycle position 73.8/100, Peak phase, projected next trough early 2027.","body_zh":"自2025年4月低点至2026年6月，VPL累计上涨约92%，是15年数据集中最大的单次上行周期。对于一个发达市场篮子而言，如此大的涨幅几乎必然同时包含本地股市的真实升值和美元换算的顺风：在此窗口内美元整体走弱，从机制上提升了太平洋持有者的美元回报，尚未计入本地涨幅。日本治理改革驱动的估值重估与韩国半导体的强势是合乎逻辑的贡献项。由于本段延伸至可靠认知之外，具体催化剂组合应视为暂定，并以量化读数为准：周期位置73.8/100，峰值阶段，预测下一个低点约在2027年初。","drivers":["Broad USD weakness likely amplified Pacific USD returns","Japan corporate governance re-rating continued","Korea semiconductor strength supported the bloc","Leg extends past reliable knowledge — catalysts provisional"],"drivers_zh":["美元整体走弱可能放大太平洋市场的美元回报","日本公司治理重估持续","韩国半导体强势支撑整个篮子","本段延伸至可靠认知之外——催化剂为暂定"],"prev_key":"2025-04","prev_key_chain":["2025-04"],"status":"exact","title":"Sharp Pacific rebound off the April 2025 trough","title_zh":"自2025年4月低点的太平洋市场急速反弹","turn_id":"vpl:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"VPL (FTSE Developed Pacific) sits in its Peak phase at a cycle position of 73.8/100, having gained roughly 92% off the April 2025 trough, its sharpest upcycle in the 15-year window. The ETF shows mild positive relative strength versus SPY (+3.4% over 63 days, RS rank 3 of the global-bloc baskets), a relatively rare moment when the Pacific bloc keeps pace with US equities. The move is Japan-led (roughly 56% of fund weight), with South Korea (~18%) and Australia (~16%) the other major contributors, so the run reflects both Japanese governance-driven re-rating and Korean tech strength. At this elevated cycle position the fund is stretched rather than washed-out, with the model projecting the next trough around early 2027.","now_zh":"VPL（富时发达太平洋ETF）目前处于峰值阶段，周期位置为73.8/100，自2025年4月低点以来累计涨幅约92%，是15年窗口内涨幅最大的一次上行周期。该ETF相对标普500呈温和正向相对强度（63日+3.4%，在全球板块篮子中相对强度排名第3），是太平洋发达市场难得与美股同步的时期。上涨由日本主导（约占基金权重56%），韩国（约18%）和澳大利亚（约16%）为其余主要贡献者，因此本轮行情既反映了日本治理改革驱动的估值重估，也反映了韩国科技股的强势。当前周期位置偏高而非超卖，模型预测下一个低点约在2027年初。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}},"vxus":{"legs":{"2011-10-03":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:trough:2011-10"},"2011-10-27":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:peak:2011-10"},"2011-11-25":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:trough:2011-11"},"2012-03-01":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:peak:2012-03"},"2012-06-01":{"body":"The ECB's July 2012 'whatever it takes' pledge broke the acute phase of the eurozone sovereign-debt crisis and unlocked a broad ex-US re-rating. Global growth firmed through 2013-2014, EM currencies stabilized alongside recovering commodity prices, and a mildly soft USD added a modest FX tailwind for unhedged holders. The leg gained roughly 53% over about two years as European peripheral spreads compressed.","body_zh":"欧央行2012年7月的'不惜一切代价'承诺终结了欧元区主权债务危机的急性期，引发非美市场大范围重新定价。2013至2014年全球经济增长趋稳，新兴市场货币随商品价格回升趋于稳定，美元温和走弱为非对冲持有人贡献了一定的汇率顺风。随着欧洲边缘国国债利差收窄，该上行段约两年累计涨幅约53%。","drivers":["ECB 'whatever it takes' pledge","Eurozone peripheral spread compression","Firming global growth 2013-2014","Mild USD weakness"],"prev_key":"2012-06","prev_key_chain":["2012-06"],"status":"exact","title":"Eurozone rescue rally, EM re-rating","title_zh":"欧元区救助反弹，新兴市场重新定价","turn_id":"vxus:trough:2012-06"},"2014-06-19":{"body":"The Fed ended QE in October 2014 while other major central banks eased, launching a broad USD bull market that became a direct FX headwind for VXUS. China's growth deceleration and the August 2015 yuan devaluation rattled EM assets, and oil's collapse from above $100 to below $30 crushed commodity-linked currencies (Canadian dollar, Brazilian real, Australian dollar). The leg fell roughly 25% over about 19 months.","body_zh":"美联储于2014年10月结束量化宽松，而其他主要央行仍在宽松，引发美元全面牛市，直接转化为VXUS的汇率逆风。中国经济减速与2015年8月人民币贬值冲击新兴市场资产，国际油价从100美元以上跌至30美元以下，重创加元、巴西雷亚尔、澳元等大宗商品货币。该下行段历时约19个月，累计跌幅约25%。","drivers":["Fed QE end + USD bull market","China slowdown and yuan devaluation Aug 2015","Oil collapse below $30 crushing commodity FX","European deflation fears"],"prev_key":"2014-07","prev_key_chain":["2014-07"],"rekey_shift_days":26,"status":"shifted","title":"Dollar surge, China slowdown, oil crash","title_zh":"美元飙升，中国放缓，油价暴跌","turn_id":"vxus:peak:2014-06"},"2015-01-06":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:trough:2015-01"},"2015-05-15":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:peak:2015-05"},"2016-02-11":{"body":"With EM currencies bottoming in early 2016 and global PMIs turning up together, ex-US assets began a powerful re-rating. The USD index peaked in late 2016 and rolled over as the eurozone and Japan recoveries gathered pace; the euro gained roughly 15% versus the dollar in 2017. China stabilized growth via credit stimulus, lifting commodity-linked EM FX, while ex-US valuations sat at deep discounts to US peers. The leg returned roughly 63% through January 2018.","body_zh":"新兴市场货币于2016年初见底，全球PMI同步回升，非美资产开启强劲重估。美元指数在2016年底见顶后回落，欧元区和日本复苏提速；2017年欧元兑美元升值约15%。中国通过信贷刺激稳住增长，带动大宗商品类新兴市场货币走强，非美估值相对美股深度折价。该上行段至2018年1月累计回报约63%。","drivers":["USD index peak and rollover 2016-2017","Synchronized global PMI recovery","EUR appreciation vs USD","China credit stabilization lifting commodity EM FX"],"prev_key":"2016-02","prev_key_chain":["2016-02"],"status":"exact","title":"Synchronized global expansion, weak dollar","title_zh":"全球同步扩张，美元走弱","turn_id":"vxus:trough:2016-02"},"2018-01-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:peak:2018-01"},"2018-12-24":{"body":"After the Q4 2018 global equity correction, the Fed pivoted to a pause and then cuts in 2019, easing dollar pressure and allowing ex-US assets to recover. The bounce was shallow and uneven: trade-war uncertainty capped EM upside, the UK faced Brexit paralysis, and eurozone growth was softening. The leg gained roughly 28% before COVID disrupted it in early 2020.","body_zh":"2018年四季度全球股市调整后，美联储于2019年转向暂停加息并随后降息，美元压力缓解，非美资产回升。但此次反弹幅度有限且不均衡：贸易战不确定性压制新兴市场上行空间，英国深陷脱欧僵局，欧元区增长放缓。该上行段累计上涨约28%，随后于2020年初被新冠疫情打断。","drivers":["Fed pause and rate cuts 2019","Trade-war uncertainty capping EM","Brexit paralysis in the UK","Softening eurozone growth"],"prev_key":"2018-12","prev_key_chain":["2018-12"],"status":"exact","title":"Fed pause, shallow global reflation","title_zh":"美联储暂停加息，浅幅全球再通胀","turn_id":"vxus:trough:2018-12"},"2020-01-17":{"body":"COVID-19 triggered a near-simultaneous global equity collapse in February-March 2020, with VXUS falling roughly 35% in under two months. Relative to the US, the ex-US index carried heavier cyclical weights (financials, energy, industrials) and more tourism-dependent economies, and a March 2020 USD safe-haven surge added an extra FX headwind on top of local equity losses.","body_zh":"新冠疫情于2020年2月至3月引发全球股市近乎同步的崩溃，VXUS在不到两个月内下跌约35%。与美国相比，非美指数周期性权重更高（金融、能源、工业），且更依赖旅游业经济体；2020年3月美元避险买盘急升，在本地股票损失之上额外叠加了汇率逆风。","drivers":["Global COVID lockdowns crushing cyclical sectors","USD safe-haven surge March 2020","Heavy cyclical/financial weights vs US tech","Synchronized global demand collapse"],"prev_key":"2020-01","prev_key_chain":["2020-01"],"status":"exact","title":"COVID crash: global synchronized selloff","title_zh":"新冠崩盘：全球同步抛售","turn_id":"vxus:peak:2020-01"},"2020-03-23":{"body":"Coordinated fiscal stimulus (EU Recovery Fund, G20 packages) and near-zero global rates launched a powerful ex-US recovery. The dollar weakened as the Fed expanded its balance sheet, a meaningful FX tailwind for unhedged holders. Commodity-linked markets (Australia, Canada, Brazil) led early, with Europe following as vaccines rolled out through 2021. The leg gained roughly 88% through September 2021.","body_zh":"协调财政刺激（欧盟复苏基金、G20方案）与全球接近零利率共同引发强劲的非美复苏。美联储扩表令美元走弱，为非对冲持有人提供显著汇率顺风。大宗商品出口国（澳大利亚、加拿大、巴西）率先领涨，随着2021年疫苗推进，欧洲跟上。该上行段至2021年9月累计涨幅约88%。","drivers":["EU Recovery Fund and G20 fiscal stimulus","Fed balance-sheet expansion weakening USD","Commodity price surge lifting resource FX","Vaccine-driven European recovery"],"prev_key":"2020-03","prev_key_chain":["2020-03"],"status":"exact","title":"Global reopening and fiscal reflation rally","title_zh":"全球重开与财政再通胀反弹","turn_id":"vxus:trough:2020-03"},"2021-06-14":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:peak:2021-06"},"2022-10-12":{"body":"The DXY peaked in late 2022 as markets began pricing a Fed pivot, and that inflection unlocked a sustained ex-US recovery. Over the following years Europe was supported by fiscal spending (German defense, EU industrial policy), Japan benefited from a weak yen and eventual BOJ normalization, and EM Asia surged on AI supply-chain demand (Taiwan, Korea). A 2025 US tariff shock added to dollar softness and a global rebalancing away from US equities. Through June 2026 the leg has gained roughly 115%; cycle position now reads 57.4/100, signaling the run has matured rather than exhausted.","body_zh":"美元指数于2022年底见顶，市场开始定价美联储转向，非美资产由此开启持续复苏。此后数年，欧洲受财政扩张支撑（德国国防开支、欧盟产业政策），日本受益于日元走弱及日央行最终正常化，亚洲新兴市场因AI供应链需求（台湾、韩国）大幅攀升。2025年美国关税冲击进一步加剧美元疲软及全球资金从美股再平衡。截至2026年6月，该上行段累计涨幅约115%；当前周期位置为57.4/100，表明此轮上涨已趋成熟但尚未耗尽。","drivers":["DXY peak late 2022 and multi-year rollover","Europe fiscal expansion (defense + EU industrial policy)","EM Asia AI supply-chain demand surge","2025 tariff shock adding to USD softness and rebalancing"],"prev_key":"2022-10","prev_key_chain":["2022-10"],"status":"exact","title":"Dollar peak to multi-year ex-US re-rating","title_zh":"美元见顶，非美资产多年重估","turn_id":"vxus:trough:2022-10"},"2024-09-26":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:peak:2024-09"},"2025-04-08":{"prev_key":null,"prev_key_chain":[],"status":"new","turn_id":"vxus:trough:2025-04"}},"now":"VXUS (Vanguard Total International Stock ETF, FTSE Global ex-US) peaked in June 2026 and has entered an early Downturn, sitting at cycle position 57.4 out of 100 -- still in the upper half of its historical range and not yet washed out. Over the prior 63 trading days it lagged SPY by 2.3 percentage points, ranking 4th among the global/regional baskets, a modest rotation back toward US assets after a roughly 115% advance off the October 2022 low. The model projects the next trough around mid-2027 (about 1.8 years out), implying a gradual, drawn-out correction rather than a sharp flush.","now_zh":"VXUS（先锋全球除美国ETF，追踪富时全球除美指数）于2026年6月触顶，已进入初期下行阶段，周期位置为57.4/100，仍处于历史区间上半段，尚未深度超卖。过去63个交易日较SPY落后2.3个百分点，在全球/区域型篮子中排名第4，反映自2022年10月低点累计上涨约115%后，资金温和回流美国资产。模型预示下一个低谷约在2027年中（约1.8年后），意味着这是一次拉锯式、缓慢的回调，而非急速下跌。","as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"archetype_check":null,"prev_revision":null,"_ttl":{"as_of":"2026-07-02","ttl_days":90,"staleness_days":31,"stale_amber":false,"stale_red":false,"archetype_check_id":null,"arch_state":"none","arch_fired_on":null,"revision_note":null}}};
